\s1 The Command to Leave Horeb
\r \ref Exodus 33:1–6|EXO 33:1-6\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb These|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb are the words|הַדְּבָרִ֗ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb spoke|דִּבֶּ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֡ר\rb* \rb east of|בְּעֵ֖בֶר\rb* \rb the Jordan—|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb*  \rb in the Arabah|בָּֽעֲרָבָה֩\rb* \rb opposite|מ֨וֹל\rb* \rb Suph—|ס֜וּף\rb*  \rb between|בֵּֽין־\rb* \rb Paran|פָּארָ֧ן\rb*\rb |וּבֵֽין־\rb* \rb and Tophel,|תֹּ֛פֶל\rb* \rb Laban,|וְלָבָ֥ן\rb* \rb Hazeroth,|וַחֲצֵרֹ֖ת\rb*\rb |וְדִ֥י\rb* \rb and Dizahab.|זָהָֽב׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb It is an eleven-day|אַחַ֨ד\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb*\rb |יוֹם֙\rb* \rb journey from Horeb|מֵֽחֹרֵ֔ב\rb*\f + \fr 1:2 \ft That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai; also in verses 6 and 19\f* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb*\rb |קָדֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb Kadesh-barnea|בַּרְנֵֽעַ׃\rb* \rb by way|דֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb of Mount|הַר־\rb* \rb Seir.|שֵׂעִ֑יר\rb* \v 3 \rb |וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb In the fortieth|בְּאַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb year,|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb on the first day|בְּאֶחָ֣ד\rb*\rb |לַחֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the eleventh|בְּעַשְׁתֵּֽי־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb month,|חֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb proclaimed|דִּבֶּ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb all|כְּ֠כֹל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֧ה\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb concerning them.|אֲלֵהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 4 \rb This was after|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb he had defeated|הַכֹּת֗וֹ\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb Sihon|סִיחֹן֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Amorites,|הָֽאֱמֹרִ֔י\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb lived|יוֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb in Heshbon,|בְּחֶשְׁבּ֑וֹן\rb* \rb and then|וְאֵ֗ת\rb* \rb at Edrei had defeated|בְּאֶדְרֶֽעִי׃\rb* \rb Og|ע֚וֹג\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Bashan,|הַבָּשָׁ֔ן\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb lived|יוֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb in Ashtaroth.|בְּעַשְׁתָּרֹ֖ת\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb On the east side|בְּעֵ֥בֶר\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Moab,|מוֹאָ֑ב\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb began|הוֹאִ֣יל\rb* \rb to explain|בֵּאֵ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb law,|הַתּוֹרָ֥ה\rb* \rb saying:|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*\f + \fr 1:5 \ft Note that \ref Deuteronomy 1:6|DEU 1:6\ref* through Deuteronomy 4:40 may be presented as a continuous section of unbroken speech by Moses. In place of multiple levels of nested quotes, this section has been set apart with a double space.\f*
\p \v 6 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb said|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb to us|אֵלֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb at Horeb:|בְּחֹרֵ֣ב\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “You have stayed|שֶׁ֖בֶת\rb* \rb at this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb mountain|בָּהָ֥ר\rb* \rb long enough.|רַב־\rb* \v 7 \rb Resume|פְּנ֣וּ׀\rb* \rb your journey|וּסְע֣וּ\rb* \rb and go|וּבֹ֨אוּ\rb* \rb to the hill country|הַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the Amorites;|הָֽאֱמֹרִי֮\rb* \rb go to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the neighboring peoples|שְׁכֵנָיו֒\rb* \rb in the Arabah,|בָּעֲרָבָ֥ה\rb* \rb in the hill country,|בָהָ֛ר\rb* \rb in the foothills,|וּבַשְּׁפֵלָ֥ה\rb*\f + \fr 1:7 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shephelah \ft or \fqa lowlands\ft ; that is, the western foothills of Judea\f* \rb in the Negev,|וּבַנֶּ֖גֶב\rb* \rb and along the seacoast|הַיָּ֑ם\rb*\rb |וּבְח֣וֹף\rb* \rb to the land|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִי֙\rb* \rb and to Lebanon,|וְהַלְּבָנ֔וֹן\rb* \rb as far as|עַד־\rb* \rb the great|הַגָּדֹ֖ל\rb* \rb River|הַנָּהָ֥ר\rb*\rb |נְהַר־\rb* \rb Euphrates.|פְּרָֽת׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb See,|רְאֵ֛ה\rb* \rb I have placed|נָתַ֥תִּי\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb before you.|לִפְנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Enter|בֹּ֚אוּ\rb* \rb and possess|וּרְשׁ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְ֠הוָה\rb* \rb swore|נִשְׁבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb He would give|לָתֵ֣ת\rb* \rb to your fathers|לַאֲבֹ֨תֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb Abraham,|לְאַבְרָהָ֨ם\rb* \rb Isaac,|לְיִצְחָ֤ק\rb* \rb and Jacob,|וּֽלְיַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb and to their descendants|וּלְזַרְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb after them.”|אַחֲרֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\s1 Moses Appoints Leaders
\r \ref Exodus 18:13–27|EXO 18:13-27\ref*)
\p \v 9 \rb At that|הַהִ֖וא\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֥ת\rb* \rb I said|וָאֹמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to you,|אֲלֵכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb “I cannot|לֹא־\rb*\rb |אוּכַ֥ל\rb* \rb carry the burden|שְׂאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb for you|אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb alone.|לְבַדִּ֖י\rb* \v 10 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb has multiplied|הִרְבָּ֣ה\rb* \rb you,|אֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb so that today|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb you are|וְהִנְּכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb as numerous|לָרֹֽב׃\rb* \rb as the stars|כְּכוֹכְבֵ֥י\rb* \rb in the sky.|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \v 11 \rb May the LORD,|יְהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of your fathers,|אֲבֽוֹתֵכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb increase you|יֹסֵ֧ף\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb a thousand|אֶ֣לֶף\rb* \rb times over|פְּעָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb and bless|וִיבָרֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb He has promised.|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \v 12 \rb But how|אֵיכָ֥ה\rb* \rb can I bear|אֶשָּׂ֖א\rb* \rb your troubles,|טָרְחֲכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb burdens,|וּמַֽשַּׂאֲכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and disputes|וְרִֽיבְכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb all by myself?|לְבַדִּ֑י\rb* \v 13 \rb Choose|הָב֣וּ\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָ֠כֶם\rb* \rb wise,|חֲכָמִ֧ים\rb* \rb understanding,|וּנְבֹנִ֛ים\rb* \rb and respected|וִידֻעִ֖ים\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֨ים\rb* \rb from each of your tribes,|לְשִׁבְטֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and I will appoint them|וַאֲשִׂימֵ֖ם\rb* \rb as your leaders.”|בְּרָאשֵׁיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb And you answered|וַֽתַּעֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֑י\rb* \rb and said,|וַתֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb “What|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you propose|דִּבַּ֖רְתָּ\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשֽׂוֹת׃\rb* \rb is good.”|טֽוֹב־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb So I took|וָאֶקַּ֞ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the leaders|רָאשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of your tribes,|שִׁבְטֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb wise|חֲכָמִים֙\rb* \rb and respected|וִֽידֻעִ֔ים\rb* \rb men,|אֲנָשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb and appointed|וָאֶתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb as leaders|רָאשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb over you—|עֲלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*  \rb as commanders|שָׂרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of thousands,|אֲלָפִ֜ים\rb*\rb |וְשָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of hundreds,|מֵא֗וֹת\rb*\rb |וְשָׂרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of fifties,|חֲמִשִּׁים֙\rb*\rb |וְשָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb and of tens,|עֲשָׂרֹ֔ת\rb* \rb and as officers|וְשֹׁטְרִ֖ים\rb* \rb for your tribes.|לְשִׁבְטֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb At that|הַהִ֖וא\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֥ת\rb* \rb I charged|וָאֲצַוֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your judges:|שֹׁ֣פְטֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb “Hear|שָׁמֹ֤עַ\rb* \rb the disputes between|בֵּין־\rb* \rb your brothers,|אֲחֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb and judge|וּשְׁפַטְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb fairly|צֶ֔דֶק\rb* \rb between|בֵּֽין־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |וּבֵין־\rb* \rb and his brother|אָחִ֖יו\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb or a foreign resident.|גֵּרֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 17 \rb |לֹֽא־\rb* \rb Show no partiality|תַכִּ֨ירוּ\rb*\rb |פָנִ֜ים\rb* \rb in judging;|בַּמִּשְׁפָּ֗ט\rb* \rb hear|תִּשְׁמָע֔וּן\rb* \rb both small|כַּקָּטֹ֤ן\rb* \rb and great alike.|כַּגָּדֹל֙\rb* \rb Do not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb be intimidated|תָג֙וּרוּ֙\rb* \rb by|מִפְּנֵי־\rb* \rb anyone,|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb judgment|הַמִּשְׁפָּ֖ט\rb* \rb belongs to God.|לֵאלֹהִ֣ים\rb*\rb |ה֑וּא\rb* \rb And bring|תַּקְרִב֥וּן\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb any case|וְהַדָּבָר֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb too difficult|יִקְשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb for you,|מִכֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb and I will hear it.”|וּשְׁמַעְתִּֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb And at that|הַהִ֑וא\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb I commanded|וָאֲצַוֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the things|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you were to do.|תַּעֲשֽׂוּן׃\rb*
\s1 Twelve Spies Sent Out
\r \ref Numbers 13:1–33|NUM 13:1-33\ref*)
\p \v 19 \rb |כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb And just as|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֑נוּ\rb* \rb had commanded us,|צִוָּ֛ה\rb* \rb we set out|וַנִּסַּ֣ע\rb* \rb from Horeb|מֵחֹרֵ֗ב\rb* \rb and went|וַנֵּ֡לֶךְ\rb* \rb toward|דֶּ֚רֶךְ\rb* \rb the hill country|הַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the Amorites,|הָֽאֱמֹרִ֔י\rb* \rb through all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the vast|הַגָּדוֹל֩\rb* \rb and terrifying|וְהַנּוֹרָ֨א\rb*\rb |הַה֜וּא\rb* \rb wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּ֣ר\rb* \rb you have seen.|רְאִיתֶ֗ם\rb* \rb When we reached|וַנָּבֹ֕א\rb*\rb |עַ֖ד\rb*\rb |קָדֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb Kadesh-barnea,|בַּרְנֵֽעַ׃\rb* \v 20 \rb I said:|וָאֹמַ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb “You have reached|בָּאתֶם֙\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb the hill country|הַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the Amorites,|הָאֱמֹרִ֔י\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb us.|לָֽנוּ׃\rb* \v 21 \rb See,|רְ֠אֵה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb has placed|נָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb before you.|לְפָנֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Go up|עֲלֵ֣ה\rb* \rb and take possession of|רֵ֗שׁ\rb* \rb it as|כַּאֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of your fathers,|אֲבֹתֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb has told you.|דִּבֶּ֨ר\rb* \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֖א\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb or discouraged.”|תֵּחָֽת׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb Then all of you|כֻּלְּכֶם֒\rb* \rb approached|וַתִּקְרְב֣וּן\rb* \rb me|אֵלַי֮\rb* \rb and said,|וַתֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb* \rb “Let us send|נִשְׁלְחָ֤ה\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb ahead of us|לְפָנֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb to search out|וְיַחְפְּרוּ־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb and bring us|וְיָשִׁ֤בוּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb word|דָּבָ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of what route|הַדֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb to follow|נַעֲלֶה־\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and which cities|הֶֽעָרִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb to enter.”|נָבֹ֖א\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb The plan|הַדָּבָ֑ר\rb* \rb seemed|בְּעֵינַ֖י\rb* \rb good to me,|וַיִּיטַ֥ב\rb* \rb so I selected|וָאֶקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb twelve|שְׁנֵ֣ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb men|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb from among you,|מִכֶּם֙\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb from each tribe.|לַשָּֽׁבֶט׃\rb* \v 24 \rb They left|וַיִּפְנוּ֙\rb* \rb and went up|וַיַּעֲל֣וּ\rb* \rb into the hill country,|הָהָ֔רָה\rb* \rb and came|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the Valley|נַ֣חַל\rb* \rb of Eshcol|אֶשְׁכֹּ֑ל\rb* \rb and spied out the land.|וַֽיְרַגְּל֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽהּ׃\rb* \v 25 \rb They took|וַיִּקְח֤וּ\rb* \rb some of the fruit|מִפְּרִ֣י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb in their hands,|בְיָדָם֙\rb* \rb carried it down|וַיּוֹרִ֖דוּ\rb* \rb to us,|אֵלֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb and brought us|וַיָּשִׁ֨בוּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֤נוּ\rb* \rb word:|דָבָר֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb “It is a good|טוֹבָ֣ה\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb us.”|לָֽנוּ׃\rb*
\s1 Israel’s Rebellion
\r \ref Numbers 14:1–12|NUM 14:1-12\ref*)
\p \v 26 \rb But you were unwilling|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אֲבִיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to go up;|לַעֲלֹ֑ת\rb* \rb you rebelled|וַתַּמְר֕וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb against the command|פִּ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 27 \rb You grumbled|וַתֵּרָגְנ֤וּ\rb* \rb in your tents|בְאָהֳלֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb and said,|וַתֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb*\rb |בְּשִׂנְאַ֤ת\rb* \rb “Because the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb hates us,|אֹתָ֔נוּ\rb* \rb He has brought us out|הוֹצִיאָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb to deliver|לָתֵ֥ת\rb* \rb us|אֹתָ֛נוּ\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֥ד\rb* \rb of the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֖י\rb* \rb to be annihilated.|לְהַשְׁמִידֵֽנוּ׃\rb* \v 28 \rb Where|אָנָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb can we|אֲנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb go?|עֹלִ֗ים\rb* \rb Our brothers|אַחֵינוּ֩\rb* \rb have made our hearts melt,|הֵמַ֨סּוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |לְבָבֵ֜נוּ\rb* \rb saying:|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb ‘The people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb are larger|גָּד֤וֹל\rb* \rb and taller|וָרָם֙\rb* \rb than we are;|מִמֶּ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb the cities|עָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb are large,|גְּדֹלֹ֥ת\rb* \rb with walls up|וּבְצוּרֹ֖ת\rb* \rb to the heavens.|בַּשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb We even|וְגַם־\rb* \rb saw|רָאִ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb the descendants|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Anakim|עֲנָקִ֖ים\rb* \rb there.’”|שָֽׁם׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb So I said|וָאֹמַ֖ר\rb* \rb to you:|אֲלֵכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb “Do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb be terrified|תַֽעַרְצ֥וּן\rb*\rb |וְֽלֹא־\rb* \rb or afraid|תִֽירְא֖וּן\rb* \rb of them!|מֵהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 30 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb who goes|הַהֹלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb before you,|לִפְנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb will fight|יִלָּחֵ֣ם\rb* \rb for you,|לָכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb just as|כְּ֠כֹל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you saw Him|לְעֵינֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb do|עָשָׂ֧ה\rb* \rb for you|אִתְּכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb in Egypt|בְּמִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \v 31 \rb and|רָאִ֔יתָ\rb* \rb in the wilderness,|וּבַמִּדְבָּר֙\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb carried you,|נְשָׂאֲךָ֙\rb* \rb as|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb a man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb carries|יִשָּׂא־\rb* \rb his son,|בְּנ֑וֹ\rb* \rb all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the way|הַדֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb* \rb by which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you traveled|הֲלַכְתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb you reached|בֹּאֲכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb place.”|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb*
\p \v 32 \rb But in spite|וּבַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb of all this,|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb you did not|אֵֽינְכֶם֙\rb* \rb trust|מַאֲמִינִ֔ם\rb* \rb the LORD|בַּיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 33 \rb who went|הַהֹלֵ֨ךְ\rb* \rb before you|לִפְנֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb on the journey,|בַּדֶּ֗רֶךְ\rb* \rb in the fire|בָּאֵ֣שׁ׀\rb* \rb by night|לַ֗יְלָה\rb* \rb and in the cloud|וּבֶעָנָ֖ן\rb* \rb by day,|יוֹמָֽם׃\rb* \rb to seek out|לָת֥וּר\rb* \rb a place|מָק֖וֹם\rb* \rb for you to camp|לַֽחֲנֹֽתְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and to show you|לַרְאֹֽתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb the road|בַּדֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb to travel.|תֵּֽלְכוּ־\rb*
\s1 Israel’s Penalty
\r \ref Numbers 14:20–35|NUM 14:20-35\ref*)
\p \v 34 \rb When the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb your words,|דִּבְרֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb He grew angry|וַיִּקְצֹ֖ף\rb* \rb and swore an oath,|וַיִּשָּׁבַ֥ע\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 35 \rb “Not|אִם־\rb* \rb one|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb of the|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb men|בָּאֲנָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb evil|הָרָ֖ע\rb* \rb generation|הַדּ֥וֹר\rb* \rb shall see|יִרְאֶ֥ה\rb* \rb the good|הַטּוֹבָ֔ה\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I swore|נִשְׁבַּ֔עְתִּי\rb* \rb to give|לָתֵ֖ת\rb* \rb your fathers,|לַאֲבֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 36 \rb except|זֽוּלָתִ֞י\rb* \rb Caleb|כָּלֵ֤ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jephunneh.|יְפֻנֶּה֙\rb* \rb He|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb will see it,|יִרְאֶ֔נָּה\rb* \rb and I will give|אֶתֵּ֧ן\rb* \rb him|אֶת־\rb* \rb and his descendants|וּלְבָנָ֑יו\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb on which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he has set foot,|דָּֽרַךְ־\rb* \rb because|יַ֕עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he followed|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb wholeheartedly.”|מִלֵּ֖א\rb*
\p \v 37 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb was also angry|הִתְאַנַּ֣ף\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb with me|בִּי֙\rb* \rb on your account,|בִּגְלַלְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and He said,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Not|לֹא־\rb* \rb even|גַּם־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb shall enter|תָבֹ֥א\rb* \rb the land.|שָֽׁם׃\rb* \v 38 \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֤עַ\rb* \rb son|בִּן\rb* \rb of Nun,|נוּן֙\rb* \rb who stands|הָעֹמֵ֣ד\rb* \rb before you,|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb will enter|יָ֣בֹא\rb* \rb it.|שָׁ֑מָּה\rb*\rb |אֹת֣וֹ\rb* \rb Encourage him,|חַזֵּ֔ק\rb* \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb he|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb will enable Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb to inherit|יַנְחִלֶ֥נָּה\rb* \rb the land.|אֶת־\rb* \v 39 \rb And the little ones|וְטַפְּכֶם֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you said|אֲמַרְתֶּ֜ם\rb* \rb would become|יִהְיֶ֗ה\rb* \rb captives—|לָבַ֣ז\rb*  \rb your children|וּ֠בְנֵיכֶם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb on that day|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb know|יָדְע֤וּ\rb* \rb good|ט֣וֹב\rb* \rb from evil—|וָרָ֔ע\rb*  \rb will enter|יָבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb the land that|שָׁ֑מָּה\rb* \rb I will give them,|אֶתְּנֶ֔נָּה\rb* \rb and they|וְהֵ֖ם\rb* \rb will possess it.|יִירָשֽׁוּהָּ׃\rb* \v 40 \rb But you|וְאַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb are to turn back|פְּנ֣וּ\rb* \rb and head|וּסְע֥וּ\rb* \rb for the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּ֖רָה\rb* \rb along the route|דֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb to the Red|סֽוּף׃\rb* \rb Sea.|יַם־\rb*\f + \fr 1:40 \ft Or \fqa the Sea of Reeds\f*”
\s1 The Defeat at Hormah
\r \ref Numbers 14:40–45|NUM 14:40-45\ref*)
\p \v 41 \rb “We have sinned|חָטָאנוּ֮\rb* \rb against the LORD,”|לַֽיהוָה֒\rb* \rb you replied.|וַֽתַּעֲנ֣וּ׀\rb*\rb |וַתֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb “We|אֲנַ֤חְנוּ\rb* \rb will go up|נַעֲלֶה֙\rb* \rb and fight,|וְנִלְחַ֔מְנוּ\rb* \rb as|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb has commanded us.”|צִוָּ֖נוּ\rb* \rb Then each|אִ֚ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of you put on|וַֽתַּחְגְּר֗וּ\rb* \rb his weapons|כְּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of war,|מִלְחַמְתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb thinking it easy|וַתָּהִ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb to go up|לַעֲלֹ֥ת\rb* \rb into the hill country.|הָהָֽרָה׃\rb*
\p \v 42 \rb But the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb “Tell|אֱמֹ֤ר\rb* \rb them|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb to go up|תַֽעֲלוּ֙\rb* \rb and fight,|תִלָּ֣חֲמ֔וּ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I am not|אֵינֶ֖נִּי\rb* \rb with you|בְּקִרְבְּכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb to keep you from|וְלֹא֙\rb* \rb defeat|תִּנָּֽגְפ֔וּ\rb* \rb by|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb your enemies.”|אֹיְבֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 43 \rb So I spoke|וָאֲדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to you,|אֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb but you would not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb listen.|שְׁמַעְתֶּ֑ם\rb* \rb You rebelled against|וַתַּמְרוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the command|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and presumptuously|וַתָּזִ֖דוּ\rb* \rb went up|וַתַּעֲל֥וּ\rb* \rb into the hill country.|הָהָֽרָה׃\rb*
\p \v 44 \rb Then the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֜י\rb* \rb who lived|הַיֹּשֵׁ֨ב\rb* \rb in|הַהוּא֙\rb* \rb the hills|בָּהָ֤ר\rb* \rb came out|וַיֵּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb against you|לִקְרַאתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and chased|וַיִּרְדְּפ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb you like|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |תַּעֲשֶׂ֖ינָה\rb* \rb a swarm of bees.|הַדְּבֹרִ֑ים\rb* \rb They routed|וַֽיַּכְּת֥וּ\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb from Seir|בְּשֵׂעִ֖יר\rb* \rb all the way|עַד־\rb* \rb to Hormah.|חָרְמָֽה׃\rb* \v 45 \rb And you returned|וַתָּשֻׁ֥בוּ\rb* \rb and wept|וַתִּבְכּ֖וּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb but He|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb would not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb to your voice|בְּקֹ֣לְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb give ear|הֶאֱזִ֖ין\rb* \rb to you.|אֲלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 46 \rb For this reason you stayed|וַתֵּשְׁב֥וּ\rb* \rb in Kadesh|בְקָדֵ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |יָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb for a long time—|רַבִּ֑ים\rb*  \rb a very long time.|כַּיָּמִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |יְשַׁבְתֶּֽם׃\rb*
\c 2
\s1 Wanderings in the Wilderness
\p \v 1 \rb Then we turned back|וַנֵּ֜פֶן\rb* \rb and headed|וַנִּסַּ֤ע\rb* \rb for the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּ֙רָה֙\rb* \rb by way|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Red|ס֔וּף\rb* \rb Sea,|יַם־\rb*\f + \fr 2:1 \ft Or \fqa the Sea of Reeds\f* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֑י\rb* \rb had instructed me,|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb and for many|רַבִּֽים׃ס\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֥ים\rb* \rb we wandered around|וַנָּ֥סָב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Mount|הַר־\rb* \rb Seir.|שֵׂעִ֖יר\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb At this time the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֥י\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 3 \rb “You have been wandering around|סֹ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb hill country|הָהָ֣ר\rb* \rb long enough;|רַב־\rb* \rb turn|פְּנ֥וּ\rb* \rb to the north|צָפֹֽנָה׃\rb* \v 4 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and command|צַ֣ו\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹר֒\rb* \rb the people:|הָעָם֮\rb* \rb ‘You|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb will pass|עֹֽבְרִ֗ים\rb* \rb through the territory|בִּגְבוּל֙\rb* \rb of your brothers,|אֲחֵיכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb the descendants|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of Esau,|עֵשָׂ֔ו\rb* \rb who live|הַיֹּשְׁבִ֖ים\rb* \rb in Seir.|בְּשֵׂעִ֑יר\rb* \rb They will be afraid|וְיִֽירְא֣וּ\rb* \rb of you,|מִכֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb so you must be very|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb careful.|וְנִשְׁמַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \v 5 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb provoke|תִּתְגָּר֣וּ\rb* \rb them,|בָ֔ם\rb* \rb for|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb I will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb give|אֶתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb any of their land,|מֵֽאַרְצָ֔ם\rb* \rb not even|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb a footprint,|מִדְרַ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |כַּף־\rb*\rb |רָ֑גֶל\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I have given|נָתַ֖תִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Mount|הַ֥ר\rb* \rb Seir|שֵׂעִֽיר׃\rb* \rb to Esau|לְעֵשָׂ֔ו\rb* \rb as his possession.|יְרֻשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \v 6 \rb You are to pay|תִּשְׁבְּר֧וּ\rb* \rb them|מֵֽאִתָּ֛ם\rb* \rb in silver|בַּכֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb for the food|אֹ֣כֶל\rb* \rb you eat|וַאֲכַלְתֶּ֑ם\rb* \rb and|וְגַם־\rb*\rb |תִּכְר֧וּ\rb*\rb |מֵאִתָּ֛ם\rb*\rb |בַּכֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb the water|מַ֜יִם\rb* \rb you drink.’”|וּשְׁתִיתֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Indeed,|כִּי֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb has blessed|בֵּֽרַכְךָ֗\rb* \rb you in all|בְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb the work|מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb of your hands.|יָדֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb He has watched over|יָדַ֣ע\rb* \rb your journey|לֶכְתְּךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb through this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb vast|הַגָּדֹ֖ל\rb* \rb wilderness.|הַמִּדְבָּ֥ר\rb* \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb has been with you|עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb these|זֶ֣ה׀\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb years,|שָׁנָ֗ה\rb* \rb and you have lacked|חָסַ֖רְתָּ\rb* \rb nothing.|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |דָּבָֽר׃\rb*
