\p \v 20 \rb (That too|אַף־\rb* \rb was regarded|תֵּחָשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb as the land|אֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of the Rephaim,|רְפָאִ֥ים\rb* \rb who|רְפָאִ֤ים\rb* \rb used to live|יָֽשְׁבוּ־\rb* \rb there,|בָהּ֙\rb*\rb |לְפָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb though the Ammonites|וְהָֽעַמֹּנִ֔ים\rb* \rb called|יִקְרְא֥וּ\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb Zamzummites.|זַמְזֻמִּֽים׃\rb* \v 21 \rb They were a people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb great|גָּד֥וֹל\rb* \rb and many,|וְרַ֛ב\rb* \rb as tall|וָרָ֖ם\rb* \rb as the Anakites.|כָּעֲנָקִ֑ים\rb* \rb But the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb destroyed them|וַיַּשְׁמִידֵ֤ם\rb* \rb from before the Ammonites,|מִפְּנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb who drove them out|וַיִּירָשֻׁ֖ם\rb* \rb and settled|וַיֵּשְׁב֥וּ\rb* \rb in their place,|תַחְתָּֽם׃\rb* \v 22 \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb He had done|עָשָׂה֙\rb* \rb for the descendants|לִבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Esau|עֵשָׂ֔ו\rb* \rb who lived|הַיֹּשְׁבִ֖ים\rb* \rb in Seir,|בְּשֵׂעִ֑יר\rb* \rb when|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb He destroyed|הִשְׁמִ֤יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Horites|הַחֹרִי֙\rb* \rb from before them.|מִפְּנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb They drove them out|וַיִּֽירָשֻׁם֙\rb* \rb and have lived|וַיֵּשְׁב֣וּ\rb* \rb in their place|תַחְתָּ֔ם\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day.|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \v 23 \rb And the Avvim,|וְהָֽעַוִּ֛ים\rb* \rb who lived|הַיֹּשְׁבִ֥ים\rb* \rb in villages|בַּחֲצֵרִ֖ים\rb* \rb as|עַד־\rb* \rb far as Gaza,|עַזָּ֑ה\rb* \rb were destroyed by|הִשְׁמִידֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Caphtorites,|כַּפְתֹּרִים֙\rb* \rb who came|הַיֹּצְאִ֣ים\rb* \rb out of Caphtor|מִכַּפְתּ֔וֹר\rb*\f + \fr 2:23 \ft That is, Crete\f* \rb and settled|וַיֵּשְׁב֥וּ\rb* \rb in their place.)|תַחְתָּֽם׃\rb*
\s1 The Defeat of Sihon
