\s1 An Exhortation to Obedience
\r \ref Deuteronomy 11:1–7|DEU 11:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Hear|שְׁמַ֤ע\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb now,|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb O Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb the statutes|הַֽחֻקִּים֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and ordinances|הַמִּשְׁפָּטִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb I|אָֽנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb am teaching|מְלַמֵּ֥ד\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to follow,|לַעֲשׂ֑וֹת\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb you may live|תִּֽחְי֗וּ\rb* \rb and may enter|וּבָאתֶם֙\rb* \rb and take possession|וִֽירִשְׁתֶּ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of your fathers,|אֲבֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you.|לָכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 2 \rb You must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb add|תֹסִ֗פוּ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָר֙\rb* \rb or subtract|תִגְרְע֖וּ\rb* \rb from|מִמֶּ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb command|מְצַוֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb you,|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb so that you may keep|לִשְׁמֹ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the commandments|מִצְוֺת֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb am giving you.|מְצַוֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Your eyes|עֵֽינֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb have seen|הָֽרֹאֹ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb did|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |בְּבַ֣עַל\rb* \rb at Baal-peor,|פְּע֑וֹר\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb destroyed|הִשְׁמִיד֛וֹ\rb* \rb from among you|מִקִּרְבֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb*\rb |הָאִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb followed|הָלַךְ֙\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בַֽעַל־\rb* \rb Baal of Peor.|פְּע֔וֹר\rb* \v 4 \rb But you|וְאַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb who held fast|הַדְּבֵקִ֔ים\rb* \rb to the LORD|בַּיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb are alive|חַיִּ֥ים\rb* \rb to this day,|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb* \rb every one of you.|כֻּלְּכֶ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb See,|רְאֵ֣ה׀\rb* \rb I have taught|לִמַּ֣דְתִּי\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb statutes|חֻקִּים֙\rb* \rb and ordinances|וּמִשְׁפָּטִ֔ים\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהָ֑י\rb* \rb has commanded me,|צִוַּ֖נִי\rb* \rb so that you may follow them|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |כֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb in|בְּקֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֛ם\rb* \rb are about to enter|בָּאִ֥ים\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb and possess.|לְרִשְׁתָּֽהּ׃\rb* \v 6 \rb Observe them|וַעֲשִׂיתֶם֒\rb* \rb carefully,|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּם֮\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this|הִ֤וא\rb* \rb will show your wisdom|חָכְמַתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb and understanding|וּבִ֣ינַתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the peoples,|הָעַמִּ֑ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb will hear|יִשְׁמְע֗וּן\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb statutes|הַחֻקִּ֣ים\rb* \rb and say,|וְאָמְר֗וּ\rb* \rb “Surely|רַ֚ק\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb great|הַגָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb nation|הַגּ֥וֹי\rb* \rb is a wise|חָכָ֣ם\rb* \rb and understanding|וְנָב֔וֹן\rb* \rb people.”|עַם־\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb what|מִי־\rb* \rb nation is|ג֣וֹי\rb* \rb great enough|גָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb to|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb have|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb a god|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb as near|קְרֹבִ֣ים\rb* \rb to them|אֵלָ֑יו\rb* \rb as the LORD|כַּיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God is to us|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb whenever|בְּכָּל־\rb* \rb we call|קָרְאֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb on Him?|אֵלָֽיו׃\rb* \v 8 \rb And what|וּמִי֙\rb* \rb nation is|גּ֣וֹי\rb* \rb great enough|גָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb to|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb have|ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb righteous|צַדִּיקִ֑ם\rb* \rb statutes|חֻקִּ֥ים\rb* \rb and ordinances|וּמִשְׁפָּטִ֖ים\rb* \rb like this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb entire|כְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb law|הַתּוֹרָ֣ה\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb set|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb before you|לִפְנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb today?|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Only|רַ֡ק\rb* \rb be on your guard|הִשָּׁ֣מֶר\rb* \rb and diligently|מְאֹ֗ד\rb* \rb watch|וּשְׁמֹ֨ר\rb* \rb yourselves,|נַפְשְׁךָ֜\rb* \rb so that you do not|פֶּן־\rb* \rb forget|תִּשְׁכַּ֨ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the things|הַדְּבָרִ֜ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb your eyes|עֵינֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb have seen,|רָא֣וּ\rb* \rb and so that they do not|וּפֶן־\rb* \rb slip|יָס֙וּרוּ֙\rb* \rb from your heart|מִלְּבָ֣בְךָ֔\rb* \rb as|כֹּ֖ל\rb*\rb |יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb long as you live.|חַיֶּ֑יךָ\rb* \rb Teach them|וְהוֹדַעְתָּ֥ם\rb* \rb to your children|לְבָנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and grandchildren.|וְלִבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |בָנֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 10 \rb The day|י֗וֹם\rb* \rb you stood|עָמַ֜דְתָּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶיךָ֮\rb* \rb at Horeb,|בְּחֹרֵב֒\rb*\f + \fr 4:10 \ft That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai; also in verse 15\f* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|בֶּאֱמֹ֨ר\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb “Gather|הַקְהֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb before Me|אֶת־\rb* \rb to hear|וְאַשְׁמִעֵ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My words,|דְּבָרָ֑י\rb* \rb so that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb they may learn|יִלְמְד֜וּן\rb* \rb to fear|לְיִרְאָ֣ה\rb* \rb Me|אֹתִ֗י\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the days|הַיָּמִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb they|הֵ֤ם\rb* \rb live|חַיִּים֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth,|הָ֣אֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb and that|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb they may teach them|יְלַמֵּדֽוּן׃\rb* \rb to their children.”|בְּנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb You came near|וַתִּקְרְב֥וּן\rb* \rb and stood|וַתַּֽעַמְד֖וּן\rb* \rb at the base|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb of the mountain,|הָהָ֑ר\rb* \rb a mountain|וְהָהָ֞ר\rb* \rb blazing|בֹּעֵ֤ר\rb* \rb with fire|בָּאֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb*\rb |לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb the heavens,|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb with black clouds|עָנָ֥ן\rb* \rb and deep|וַעֲרָפֶֽל׃\rb* \rb darkness.|חֹ֖שֶׁךְ\rb* \v 12 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֧ר\rb* \rb to you|אֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb out of|מִתּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the fire.|הָאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb You|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb heard|שֹׁמְעִ֔ים\rb* \rb the sound|ק֤וֹל\rb* \rb of the words|דְּבָרִים֙\rb* \rb but saw|רֹאִ֖ים\rb* \rb no|אֵינְכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb form;|וּתְמוּנָ֛ה\rb* \rb there was only|זוּלָתִ֥י\rb* \rb a voice.|קֽוֹל׃\rb* \v 13 \rb He declared|וַיַּגֵּ֨ד\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb His covenant,|בְּרִית֗וֹ\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb He commanded|צִוָּ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb you to follow—|לַעֲשׂ֔וֹת\rb*  \rb the Ten|עֲשֶׂ֖רֶת\rb* \rb Commandments|הַדְּבָרִ֑ים\rb*\f + \fr 4:13 \ft Hebrew \fqa the Ten Words\f* \rb that He wrote|וַֽיִּכְתְּבֵ֔ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֖י\rb* \rb tablets|לֻח֥וֹת\rb* \rb of stone.|אֲבָנִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb |וְאֹתִ֞י\rb* \rb At that|הַהִ֔וא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb commanded me|צִוָּ֤ה\rb* \rb to teach|לְלַמֵּ֣ד\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb the statutes|חֻקִּ֖ים\rb* \rb and ordinances|וּמִשְׁפָּטִ֑ים\rb* \rb you are to follow|לַעֲשֹׂתְכֶ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֕רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֛ם\rb* \rb are crossing|עֹבְרִ֥ים\rb* \rb the Jordan|שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb to possess.|לְרִשְׁתָּֽהּ׃\rb*
\s1 A Warning against Idolatry
\r \ref Deuteronomy 12:29–32|DEU 12:29-32\ref*; \ref Ezekiel 6:1–7|EZK 6:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 15 \rb So since|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you saw|רְאִיתֶם֙\rb* \rb no|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb form|תְּמוּנָ֔ה\rb* \rb of any kind|כָּל־\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֗וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb spoke|דִּבֶּ֨ר\rb* \rb to you|אֲלֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb out of|מִתּ֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the fire|הָאֵֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb at Horeb,|בְּחֹרֵ֖ב\rb* \rb be careful|וְנִשְׁמַרְתֶּ֥ם\rb*\rb |לְנַפְשֹׁתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֖ד\rb* \v 16 \rb that you do not|פֶּ֨ן־\rb* \rb act corruptly|תַּשְׁחִת֔וּן\rb* \rb and make|וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb an idol|פֶּ֖סֶל\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb of any form|תְּמוּנַ֣ת\rb* \rb or|כָּל־\rb* \rb shape,|סָ֑מֶל\rb* \rb whether in the likeness|תַּבְנִ֥ית\rb* \rb of a male|זָכָ֖ר\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb female,|נְקֵבָֽה׃\rb* \v 17 \rb |תַּבְנִ֕ית\rb* \rb of any|כָּל־\rb* \rb beast|בְּהֵמָ֖ה\rb* \rb that is|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb on the earth|בָּאָ֑רֶץ\rb*\rb |תַּבְנִית֙\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb or bird|צִפּ֣וֹר\rb*\rb |כָּנָ֔ף\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb flies|תָּע֖וּף\rb* \rb in the air,|בַּשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 18 \rb or|תַּבְנִ֕ית\rb* \rb of any|כָּל־\rb* \rb creature that crawls|רֹמֵ֖שׂ\rb* \rb on the ground|בָּאֲדָמָ֑ה\rb*\rb |תַּבְנִ֛ית\rb* \rb or|כָּל־\rb* \rb fish|דָּגָ֥ה\rb* \rb that is|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in the waters|בַּמַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb below.|מִתַּ֥חַת\rb*\rb |לָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb When you look|תִּשָּׂ֨א\rb*\rb |עֵינֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb to the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֗יְמָה\rb* \rb and see|וְֽ֠רָאִיתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sun|הַשֶּׁ֨מֶשׁ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb moon|הַיָּרֵ֜חַ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and stars—|הַכּֽוֹכָבִ֗ים\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb the host|צְבָ֣א\rb* \rb of heaven—|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb do not be|וּפֶן־\rb* \rb enticed|וְנִדַּחְתָּ֛\rb* \rb to bow down|וְהִשְׁתַּחֲוִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb and worship|וַעֲבַדְתָּ֑ם\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb has apportioned|חָלַ֜ק\rb* \rb to all|לְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the nations|הָֽעַמִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb under|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb heaven.|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 20 \rb Yet the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb has taken|לָקַ֣ח\rb* \rb you|וְאֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb and brought|וַיּוֹצִ֥א\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb out of the iron|הַבַּרְזֶ֖ל\rb* \rb furnace,|מִכּ֥וּר\rb* \rb out of Egypt,|מִמִּצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb to be|לִהְי֥וֹת\rb*\rb |ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb the people|לְעַ֥ם\rb* \rb of His inheritance,|נַחֲלָ֖ה\rb* \rb as you are today.|כַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb The LORD, however,|וַֽיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb was angry|הִתְאַנֶּף־\rb* \rb with me|בִּ֖י\rb* \rb on account|עַל־\rb* \rb of you,|דִּבְרֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and He swore|וַיִּשָּׁבַ֗ע\rb* \rb that I would not|לְבִלְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb cross|עָבְרִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb*\rb |וּלְבִלְתִּי־\rb* \rb to enter|בֹא֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the good|הַטּוֹבָ֔ה\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb as an inheritance.|נַחֲלָֽה׃\rb* \v 22 \rb For I will not|אֵינֶ֥נִּי\rb* \rb be crossing|עֹבֵ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan,|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb must die|מֵת֙\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb land.|בָּאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb But you|וְאַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb shall cross over|עֹֽבְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb and take possession of|וִֽירִשְׁתֶּ֕ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb that|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb good|הַטּוֹבָ֖ה\rb* \rb land.|הָאָ֥רֶץ\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb Be careful|הִשָּׁמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb that you|לָכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb do not|פֶּֽן־\rb* \rb forget|תִּשְׁכְּחוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the covenant|בְּרִ֤ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹ֣הֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He made|כָּרַ֖ת\rb* \rb with you;|עִמָּכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb do not make|וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֨ם\rb* \rb an idol|פֶּ֙סֶל֙\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb in the form|תְּמ֣וּנַת\rb* \rb of anything|כֹּ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He|יְהוָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb has forbidden you.|צִוְּךָ֖\rb* \v 24 \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb is a consuming|אֹכְלָ֖ה\rb*\rb |ה֑וּא\rb* \rb fire,|אֵ֥שׁ\rb*\f + \fr 4:24 \ft Cited in \ref Hebrews 12:29|HEB 12:29\ref*\f* \rb a jealous|קַנָּֽא׃פ\rb* \rb God.|אֵ֖ל\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb After|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have|תוֹלִ֤יד\rb* \rb children|בָּנִים֙\rb* \rb and grandchildren|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and you have been in the land|בָּאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb a long time,|וְנוֹשַׁנְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb if you then act corruptly|וְהִשְׁחַתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb and make|וַעֲשִׂ֤יתֶם\rb* \rb an idol|פֶּ֙סֶל֙\rb* \rb of any|כֹּ֔ל\rb* \rb form—|תְּמ֣וּנַת\rb* \rb doing|וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֛ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה־\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and provoking Him to anger—|לְהַכְעִיסֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 26 \rb I call heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֣יִם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and earth|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb as witnesses|הַעִידֹתִי֩\rb* \rb against you|בָכֶ֨ם\rb* \rb this day|הַיּ֜וֹם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you will quickly|מַהֵר֒\rb* \rb perish|אָבֹ֣ד\rb*\rb |תֹּאבֵדוּן֮\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֜ם\rb* \rb are crossing|עֹבְרִ֧ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֛ן\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb to possess.|לְרִשְׁתָּ֑הּ\rb* \rb You will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb live long|תַאֲרִיכֻ֤ן\rb*\rb |יָמִים֙\rb* \rb upon it,|עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb but|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb will be utterly destroyed.|הִשָּׁמֵ֖ד\rb*\rb |תִּשָּׁמֵדֽוּן׃\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb will scatter|וְהֵפִ֧יץ\rb* \rb you among the peoples,|בָּעַמִּ֑ים\rb* \rb and only a few of you|מְתֵ֣י\rb*\rb |מִסְפָּ֔ר\rb* \rb will survive|וְנִשְׁאַרְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֕ם\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb* \rb will drive you.|יְנַהֵ֧ג\rb* \v 28 \rb And there|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb you will serve|וַעֲבַדְתֶּם־\rb* \rb man-made|מַעֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |יְדֵ֣י\rb*\rb |אָדָ֑ם\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb of wood|עֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb and stone,|וָאֶ֔בֶן\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb cannot|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb see|יִרְאוּן֙\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb hear|יִשְׁמְע֔וּן\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb eat|יֹֽאכְל֖וּן\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb smell.|יְרִיחֻֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb But if from there|מִשָּׁ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb you will seek|וּבִקַּשְׁתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb you will find|וּמָצָ֑אתָ\rb* \rb Him|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb if you seek Him|תִדְרְשֶׁ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָבְךָ֖\rb* \rb and with all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb your soul.|נַפְשֶֽׁךָ׃\rb* \v 30 \rb When you are in distress|בַּצַּ֣ר\rb* \rb and all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb things|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb have happened to you,|וּמְצָא֕וּךָ\rb* \rb then in later|בְּאַחֲרִית֙\rb* \rb days|הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb* \rb you will return|וְשַׁבְתָּ֙\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and listen|וְשָׁמַעְתָּ֖\rb* \rb to His voice.|בְּקֹלֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 31 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb is a merciful|רַחוּם֙\rb* \rb God;|אֵ֤ל\rb* \rb He will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb abandon you|יַרְפְּךָ֖\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb destroy you|יַשְׁחִיתֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb forget|יִשְׁכַּח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb with your fathers,|אֲבֹתֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He swore to them by oath.|נִשְׁבַּ֖ע\rb*
\s1 The LORD Alone Is God
\p \v 32 \rb Indeed,|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb ask|שְׁאַל־\rb* \rb now|נָא֩\rb* \rb from one end|וּלְמִקְצֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the other|קְצֵ֣ה\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb about the days|לְיָמִ֨ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb long|רִֽאשֹׁנִ֜ים\rb* \rb preceded|הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb you,|לְפָנֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb from|לְמִן־\rb* \rb the day|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֤ים׀\rb* \rb created|בָּרָ֨א\rb* \rb man|אָדָם֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb earth:|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb Has anything as|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb great|הַגָּדוֹל֙\rb* \rb as this|כַּדָּבָ֤ר\rb* \rb ever happened|הֲנִֽהְיָ֗ה\rb* \rb or|א֖וֹ\rb*\rb |כָּמֹֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb been reported?|הֲנִשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \v 33 \rb Has a people|עָם֩\rb* \rb ever heard|הֲשָׁ֣מַֽע\rb* \rb the voice|ק֨וֹל\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb*\f + \fr 4:33 \ft Or \fqa of a god\f* \rb speaking|מְדַבֵּ֧ר\rb* \rb out of|מִתּוֹךְ־\rb* \rb the fire,|הָאֵ֛שׁ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb have,|שָׁמַ֥עְתָּ\rb* \rb and lived?|וַיֶּֽחִי׃\rb* \v 34 \rb Or|א֣וֹ׀\rb* \rb has any god|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb tried|הֲנִסָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |לָ֠בוֹא\rb* \rb to take|לָקַ֨חַת\rb* \rb as his own|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb a nation|גוֹי֮\rb* \rb out of|מִקֶּ֣רֶב\rb* \rb another nation—|גּוֹי֒\rb*  \rb by trials,|בְּמַסֹּת֩\rb* \rb signs,|בְּאֹתֹ֨ת\rb* \rb wonders,|וּבְמוֹפְתִ֜ים\rb* \rb and war,|וּבְמִלְחָמָ֗ה\rb* \rb by a strong|חֲזָקָה֙\rb* \rb hand|וּבְיָ֤ד\rb* \rb and an outstretched|נְטוּיָ֔ה\rb* \rb arm,|וּבִזְר֣וֹעַ\rb* \rb and by great|גְּדֹלִ֑ים\rb* \rb terrors—|וּבְמוֹרָאִ֖ים\rb*  \rb as|כְּ֠כֹל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb did|עָשָׂ֨ה\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb in Egypt,|בְּמִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb before your eyes?|לְעֵינֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 35 \rb You|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb were shown these things|הָרְאֵ֣תָ\rb* \rb so that you would know|לָדַ֔עַת\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb is God;|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb there is no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb other|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb besides Him.|מִלְבַדּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 36 \rb He let you hear|הִשְׁמִֽיעֲךָ֥\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His voice|קֹל֖וֹ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֛יִם\rb* \rb to discipline you,|לְיַסְּרֶ֑ךָּ\rb* \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb earth|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb He showed|הֶרְאֲךָ֙\rb* \rb you|אֶת־\rb* \rb His great|הַגְּדוֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb fire,|אִשּׁ֣וֹ\rb* \rb and you heard|שָׁמַ֖עְתָּ\rb* \rb His words|וּדְבָרָ֥יו\rb* \rb out of|מִתּ֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the fire.|הָאֵֽשׁ׃\rb* \v 37 \rb Because|וְתַ֗חַת\rb*\rb |כִּ֤י\rb* \rb He loved|אָהַב֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your fathers,|אֲבֹתֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb He chose|וַיִּבְחַ֥ר\rb* \rb their descendants|בְּזַרְע֖וֹ\rb* \rb after them|אַחֲרָ֑יו\rb* \rb and brought you|וַיּוֹצִֽאֲךָ֧\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb by His presence|בְּפָנָ֛יו\rb* \rb and great|הַגָּדֹ֖ל\rb* \rb power,|בְּכֹח֥וֹ\rb* \v 38 \rb to drive out|לְהוֹרִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb before you|מִמְּךָ֖\rb*\rb |מִפָּנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb nations|גּוֹיִ֛ם\rb* \rb greater|גְּדֹלִ֧ים\rb* \rb and mightier than you,|וַעֲצֻמִ֛ים\rb* \rb and to bring you|לַהֲבִֽיאֲךָ֗\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb into their land|אַרְצָ֛ם\rb* \rb and give it to you|לָֽתֶת־\rb* \rb for your|לְךָ֧\rb* \rb inheritance,|נַחֲלָ֖ה\rb* \rb as it is this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day.|כַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*
\p \v 39 \rb Know therefore|וְיָדַעְתָּ֣\rb* \rb this day|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb* \rb and take|וַהֲשֵׁבֹתָ֮\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb heart|לְבָבֶךָ֒\rb* \rb that|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb is God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb in heaven|בַּשָּׁמַ֣יִם\rb* \rb above|מִמַּ֔עַל\rb* \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb below;|מִתָּ֑חַת\rb* \rb there is no|אֵ֖ין\rb* \rb other.|עֽוֹד׃\rb* \v 40 \rb Keep|וְשָׁמַרְתָּ֞\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His statutes|חֻקָּ֣יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and commandments,|מִצְוֺתָ֗יו\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֤י\rb* \rb am giving you today,|מְצַוְּךָ֙\rb*\rb |הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb so that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb you and your children|וּלְבָנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb after you|אַחֲרֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb may prosper,|יִיטַ֣ב\rb* \rb and that|וּלְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb you may live long|תַּאֲרִ֤יךְ\rb*\rb |יָמִים֙\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|הַ֣אֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb for all|כָּל־\rb* \rb time.|הַיָּמִֽים׃פ\rb*
\s1 Cities of Refuge
\r \ref Numbers 35:9–34|NUM 35:9-34\ref*; \ref Deuteronomy 19:1–14|DEU 19:1-14\ref*; \ref Joshua 20:1–9|JOS 20:1-9\ref*)
\p \v 41 \rb Then|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb set aside|יַבְדִּ֤יל\rb* \rb three|שָׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb across|בְּעֵ֖בֶר\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb* \rb to the east|מִזְרְחָ֖ה\rb*\rb |שָֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb* \v 42 \rb to which|שָׁ֜מָּה\rb* \rb a manslayer|רוֹצֵ֗חַ\rb* \rb could flee|לָנֻ֨ס\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb after killing|יִרְצַ֤ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his neighbor|רֵעֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb unintentionally|בִּבְלִי־\rb*\rb |דַ֔עַת\rb*\rb |וְה֛וּא\rb* \rb without|לֹא־\rb* \rb prior|מִתְּמ֣וֹל\rb*\rb |שִׁלְשׁ֑וֹם\rb* \rb malice.|שֹׂנֵ֥א\rb*\rb |ל֖וֹ\rb*
\p \rb To save one’s own life,|וָחָֽי׃\rb* \rb he could flee|וְנָ֗ס\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֛ת\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb cities:|הֶעָרִ֥ים\rb* \v 43 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Bezer|בֶּ֧צֶר\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֛ר\rb* \rb on the plateau|הַמִּישֹׁ֖ר\rb*\rb |בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb belonging to the Reubenites,|לָרֻֽאוּבֵנִ֑י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Ramoth|רָאמֹ֤ת\rb* \rb in Gilead|בַּגִּלְעָד֙\rb* \rb belonging to the Gadites,|לַגָּדִ֔י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb or Golan|גּוֹלָ֥ן\rb* \rb in Bashan|בַּבָּשָׁ֖ן\rb* \rb belonging to the Manassites.|לַֽמְנַשִּֽׁי׃\rb*
\s1 Introduction to the Law
\p \v 44 \rb This|וְזֹ֖את\rb* \rb is the law|הַתּוֹרָ֑ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb set|שָׂ֣ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Israelites.|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 45 \rb These are|אֵ֚לֶּה\rb* \rb the testimonies,|הָֽעֵדֹ֔ת\rb* \rb statutes,|וְהַֽחֻקִּ֖ים\rb* \rb and ordinances|וְהַמִּשְׁפָּטִ֑ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb proclaimed|דִּבֶּ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb them|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb after they had come out|בְּצֵאתָ֖ם\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 46 \rb while they were in the valley|בַּגַּ֗יְא\rb* \rb across|בְּעֵ֨בֶר\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֜ן\rb* \rb facing|מ֚וּל\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb Beth-peor|פְּע֔וֹר\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb of Sihon|סִיחֹן֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Amorites,|הָֽאֱמֹרִ֔י\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb lived|יוֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb in Heshbon|בְּחֶשְׁבּ֑וֹן\rb* \rb and was defeated|הִכָּ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb by Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb and the Israelites|וּבְנֵֽי\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb after they had come out|בְּצֵאתָ֖ם\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 47 \rb They took possession|וַיִּֽירְשׁ֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of the land belonging to Sihon|אַרְצ֜וֹ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |אֶ֣רֶץ׀\rb* \rb to Og|ע֣וֹג\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Bashan—|הַבָּשָׁ֗ן\rb*  \rb the two|שְׁנֵי֙\rb* \rb Amorite|הָֽאֱמֹרִ֔י\rb* \rb kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb across|בְּעֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb* \rb to the east—|מִזְרַ֖ח\rb*\rb |שָֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb*  \v 48 \rb extending from Aroer|מֵעֲרֹעֵ֞ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the rim|שְׂפַת־\rb* \rb of the Arnon|אַרְנֹ֛ן\rb* \rb Valley|נַ֧חַל\rb* \rb as far as|וְעַד־\rb* \rb Mount|הַ֥ר\rb* \rb Siyon|שִׂיאֹ֖ן\rb*\f + \fr 4:48 \ft Or \fqa Sion\ft ; Syriac \fqa Sirion\f* \rb (that is,|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb Hermon),|חֶרְמֽוֹן׃\rb* \v 49 \rb including all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Arabah|הָ֨עֲרָבָ֜ה\rb* \rb on the east|מִזְרָ֔חָה\rb* \rb side|עֵ֤בֶר\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּן֙\rb* \rb and as far as|וְעַ֖ד\rb* \rb the Sea|יָ֣ם\rb* \rb of the Arabah,|הָעֲרָבָ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 4:49 \ft That is, the Dead Sea\f* \rb below|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb the slopes|אַשְׁדֹּ֥ת\rb* \rb of Pisgah.|הַפִּסְגָּֽה׃פ\rb*
\c 5
\s1 The Covenant at Horeb
\p \v 1 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁה֮\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb to them:|אֶל־\rb*\f + \fr 5:1 \ft Note that \ref Deuteronomy 5:1|DEU 5:1\ref* through Deuteronomy 26:19 may be presented as a continuous section of unbroken speech by Moses. In place of multiple levels of nested quotes, this section has been set apart with a double space.\f*
\p \rb Hear,|שְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb O Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the statutes|הַחֻקִּ֣ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and ordinances|הַמִּשְׁפָּטִ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb declare|דֹּבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb in your hearing|בְּאָזְנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb this day.|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb Learn|וּלְמַדְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb and observe them|לַעֲשֹׂתָֽם׃\rb* \rb carefully.|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \v 2 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb made|כָּרַ֥ת\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֖ית\rb* \rb with us|עִמָּ֛נוּ\rb* \rb at Horeb.|בְּחֹרֵֽב׃\rb*\f + \fr 5:2 \ft That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai\f*
\p \v 3 \rb He|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb make|כָּרַ֥ת\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb covenant|הַבְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb our fathers,|אֲבֹתֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb but|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb with|אִתָּ֗נוּ\rb*\rb |אֲנַ֨חְנוּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb all|כֻּלָּ֥נוּ\rb* \rb of us who are alive|חַיִּֽים׃\rb* \rb here today.|פֹ֛ה\rb*\rb |הַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \v 4 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb spoke|דִּבֶּ֨ר\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb face|פָּנִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb to face|בְּפָנִ֗ים\rb* \rb out of|מִתּ֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the fire|הָאֵֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb on the mountain.|בָּהָ֖ר\rb*
\s1 The Ten Commandments
\r \ref Exodus 20:1–17|EXO 20:1-17\ref*)
\p \v 5 \rb At that|הַהִ֔וא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb I|אָ֠נֹכִי\rb* \rb was standing|עֹמֵ֨ד\rb* \rb between|בֵּין־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb and you|וּבֵֽינֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb to declare|לְהַגִּ֥יד\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you were afraid|יְרֵאתֶם֙\rb* \rb of|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the fire|הָאֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb and would not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb go up|עֲלִיתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb the mountain.|בָּהָ֖ר\rb* \rb And He said:|לֵאמֹֽר׃ס\rb* \v 6 \rb “I|אָֽנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb brought you out|הוֹצֵאתִ֛יךָ\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb out of the house|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of slavery.|עֲבָדִֽ֑ים׃\rb*
\li1 \v 7 \rb You shall have|יִהְיֶ֥ה־\rb* \rb no|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |לְךָ֛֩\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֖֜ים\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֥֨ים\rb* \rb before|עַל־\rb* \rb Me.|פָּנָֽ֗יַ׃\rb*\f + \fr 5:7 \ft Or \fqa besides Me\f*
\li1 \v 8 \rb You shall not|לֹֽ֣א־\rb* \rb make|תַעֲשֶׂ֥ה־\rb* \rb for yourself|לְךָ֥֣\rb* \rb an idol|פֶ֣֙סֶל֙׀\rb* \rb in the form|תְּמוּנָ֔֡ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤֣ר\rb* \rb of anything|כָּל־\rb* \rb in the heavens|בַּשָּׁמַ֣֙יִם֙׀\rb* \rb above,|מִמַּ֔֡עַל\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר֩\rb* \rb on the earth|בָּאָ֖֨רֶץ\rb* \rb below,|מִתָּ֑֜חַת\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb or in the waters|בַּמַּ֖֣יִם׀\rb* \rb beneath.|מִתַּ֥֣חַת\rb*\rb |לָאָֽ֗רֶץ׃\rb* \v 9 \rb You shall not|לֹא־\rb* \rb bow down|תִשְׁתַּחֲוֶ֥֣ה\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֖ם֮\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb or worship them;|תָעָבְדֵ֑ם֒\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I,|אָנֹכִ֞י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb am a jealous|קַנָּ֔א\rb* \rb God,|אֵ֣ל\rb* \rb visiting|פֹּ֠קֵד\rb* \rb the iniquity|עֲוֺ֨ן\rb* \rb of the fathers|אָב֧וֹת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb their children|בָּנִ֛ים\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb to the third|שִׁלֵּשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and fourth generations|רִבֵּעִ֖ים\rb* \rb of those who hate Me,|לְשֹׂנְאָֽ֑י׃\rb* \v 10 \rb but showing|וְעֹ֤֥שֶׂה\rb* \rb loving devotion|חֶ֖֙סֶד֙\rb* \rb to a thousand generations|לַֽאֲלָפִ֑֔ים\rb*\f + \fr 5:10 \ft Hebrew \fqa loving devotion to thousands\ft ; forms of the Hebrew \fqa chesed \ft are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as \fqa loving devotion\ft ; the range of meaning includes \fqa love\ft , \fqa goodness\ft , \fqa kindness\ft , \fqa faithfulness\ft , and \fqa mercy\ft , as well as \fqa loyalty to a covenant\ft .\f* \rb of those who love Me|לְאֹהֲבַ֖י\rb* \rb and keep|וּלְשֹׁמְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb My commandments.|מִצְוֹתוֹ׃ס\rb*
\li1 \v 11 \rb You shall not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb take|תִשָּׂ֛א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the name|שֵֽׁם־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb in vain,|לַשָּׁ֑וְא\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb leave anyone unpunished|יְנַקֶּה֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb takes|יִשָּׂ֥א\rb* \rb His name|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in vain.|לַשָּֽׁוְא׃ס\rb*
\li1 \v 12 \rb Observe|שָׁמ֣֛וֹר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֖֨ת\rb* \rb day|י֥וֹם֩\rb* \rb by keeping it holy,|לְקַדְּשׁ֑֜וֹ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶֽ֗יךָ׃\rb* \rb has commanded you.|צִוְּךָ֖֣׀\rb* \v 13 \rb Six|שֵׁ֤֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֣ים֙\rb* \rb you shall labor|תַּֽעֲבֹ֔ד֮\rb* \rb and do|וְעָשִׂ֖֣יתָ\rb* \rb all|כָּֿל־\rb* \rb your work,|מְלַאכְתֶּֽךָ֒׃\rb* \v 14 \rb but the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֜֔י\rb* \rb day|וְי֙וֹם֙\rb* \rb is a Sabbath|שַׁבָּ֖֣ת׀\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣֥ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֑֗יךָ\rb* \rb on which you must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb do|תַעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb any|כָל־\rb* \rb work—|מְלָאכָ֡ה\rb* \rb neither you,|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb nor your son|וּבִנְךָֽ־\rb* \rb or daughter,|וּבִתֶּ֣ךָ\rb* \rb nor your manservant|וְעַבְדְּךָֽ־\rb* \rb or maidservant,|וַ֠אֲמָתֶךָ\rb* \rb nor your ox|וְשׁוֹרְךָ֨\rb* \rb or donkey|וַחֲמֹֽרְךָ֜\rb* \rb or any|וְכָל־\rb* \rb of your livestock,|בְּהֶמְתֶּ֗ךָ\rb* \rb nor the foreigner|וְגֵֽרְךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb within your gates,|בִּשְׁעָרֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֗עַן\rb* \rb your manservant|עַבְדְּךָ֥\rb* \rb and maidservant|וַאֲמָתְךָ֖\rb* \rb may rest|יָנ֛וּחַ\rb* \rb as you do.|כָּמֽ֑וֹךָ׃\rb* \v 15 \rb Remember|וְזָכַרְתָּ֞֗\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י־\rb* \rb you were|הָיִ֣֙יתָ֙׀\rb* \rb a slave|עֶ֤֥בֶד\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֔֗יִם\rb* \rb and that the LORD|יְהוָ֤֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֤֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb brought you out|וַיֹּצִ֨אֲךָ֜֩\rb* \rb of there|מִשָּׁ֔ם֙\rb* \rb with a mighty|חֲזָקָ֖ה֙\rb* \rb hand|בְּיָ֤֥ד\rb* \rb and an outstretched|נְטוּיָ֑֔ה\rb* \rb arm.|וּבִזְרֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb That is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb has commanded|צִוְּךָ֙\rb* \rb you to keep|לַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Sabbath|הַשַׁבָּֽת׃ס\rb* \rb day.|י֥וֹם\rb*
\li1 \v 16 \rb Honor|כַּבֵּ֤ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and your mother,|אִמֶּ֔ךָ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb has commanded you,|צִוְּךָ֖\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֣עַן׀\rb* \rb your days|יָמֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb may be long|יַאֲרִיכֻ֣ן\rb* \rb and that|וּלְמַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb it may go well|יִ֣יטַב\rb* \rb with you|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb in|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the land|הָֽאֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you.|לָֽךְ׃ס\rb*\f + \fr 5:16 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 15:4|MAT 15:4\ref*, Matthew 19:19, Mark 7:10, Luke 18:20, and Ephesians 6:2–3\f*
\li1 \v 17 \rb You shall not|לֹ֥֖א\rb* \rb murder.|תִּֿרְצָֽח׃ס\rb*\f + \fr 5:17 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 5:21|MAT 5:21\ref*, Matthew 19:18, Mark 10:19, Luke 18:20, Romans 13:9, and James 2:11\f*
\li1 \v 18 \rb You shall not|וְלֹ֖֣א\rb* \rb commit adultery.|תִּֿנְאָֽ֑ף׃ס\rb*\f + \fr 5:18 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 5:27|MAT 5:27\ref*, Matthew 19:18, Mark 10:19, Luke 18:20, Romans 13:9, and James 2:11\f*
\li1 \v 19 \rb You shall not|וְלֹ֖֣א\rb* \rb steal.|תִּֿגְנֹֽ֔ב׃ס\rb*\f + \fr 5:19 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 19:18|MAT 19:18\ref*, Mark 10:19, Luke 18:20, and Romans 13:9\f*
\li1 \v 20 \rb You shall not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb bear|תַעֲנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb false|שָֽׁוְא׃ס\rb* \rb witness|עֵ֥ד\rb* \rb against your neighbor.|בְרֵֽעֲךָ֖\rb*\f + \fr 5:20 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 19:18|MAT 19:18\ref*, Mark 10:19, and Luke 18:20\f*
\li1 \v 21 \rb You shall not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb covet|תַחְמֹ֖ד\rb*\f + \fr 5:21 \ft Cited in \ref Romans 7:7|ROM 7:7\ref* and Romans 13:9\f* \rb your neighbor’s|רֵעֶ֑ךָס\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֨א\rb* \rb wife.|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb You shall not covet|תִתְאַוֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb your neighbor’s|רֵעֶ֗ךָ\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb or field,|שָׂדֵ֜הוּ\rb* \rb or his manservant|וְעַבְדּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb or maidservant,|וַאֲמָתוֹ֙\rb* \rb or his ox|שׁוֹר֣וֹ\rb* \rb or donkey,|וַחֲמֹר֔וֹ\rb* \rb or anything|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb belongs to your neighbor.”|לְרֵעֶֽךָ׃ס\rb*
\s1 Moses Intercedes for the People
\r \ref Exodus 20:18–21|EXO 20:18-21\ref*; \ref Hebrews 12:18–29|HEB 12:18-29\ref*)
\p \v 22 \rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb spoke|דִּבֶּר֩\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֡לֶּה\rb* \rb commandments|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb in a loud|גָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb voice|ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb assembly|קְהַלְכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb out of|מִתּ֤וֹךְ\rb* \rb the fire,|הָאֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb the cloud,|הֶֽעָנָ֣ן\rb* \rb and the deep darkness|וְהָֽעֲרָפֶ֔ל\rb* \rb on the mountain;|בָּהָ֗ר\rb* \rb He added|יָסָ֑ף\rb* \rb nothing more.|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb And He wrote them|וַֽיִּכְתְּבֵ֗ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵי֙\rb* \rb tablets|לֻחֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of stone|אֲבָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and gave them|וַֽיִּתְּנֵ֖ם\rb* \rb to me.|אֵלָֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb And when you heard|כְּשָׁמְעֲכֶ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the voice|הַקּוֹל֙\rb* \rb out of|מִתּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the darkness|הַחֹ֔שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb while the mountain|וְהָהָ֖ר\rb* \rb was blazing|בֹּעֵ֣ר\rb* \rb with fire,|בָּאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the heads|רָאשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of your tribes|שִׁבְטֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and your elders|וְזִקְנֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb approached|וַתִּקְרְב֣וּן\rb* \rb me,|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \v 24 \rb and you said,|וַתֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb* \rb “Behold,|הֵ֣ן\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has shown us|הֶרְאָ֜נוּ\rb* \rb His glory|כְּבֹד֣וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and greatness,|גָּדְל֔וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and we have heard|שָׁמַ֖עְנוּ\rb* \rb His voice|קֹל֥וֹ\rb* \rb out of|מִתּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the fire.|הָאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb Today|הַיּ֤וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb we have seen|רָאִ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a man|הָֽאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb can live|וָחָֽי׃\rb* \rb even if God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb speaks|יְדַבֵּ֧ר\rb* \rb with him.|אֶת־\rb* \v 25 \rb But now,|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb why|לָ֣מָּה\rb* \rb should we die?|נָמ֔וּת\rb* \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb great|הַגְּדֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb fire|הָאֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb will consume us,|תֹֽאכְלֵ֔נוּ\rb* \rb and we will die,|וָמָֽתְנוּ׃\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb*\rb |יֹסְפִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb we|אֲנַ֗חְנוּ\rb* \rb hear|לִ֠שְׁמֹעַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the voice|ק֨וֹל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb any longer.|ע֖וֹד\rb* \v 26 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb of all|כָל־\rb* \rb flesh|בָּשָׂ֡ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb has heard|שָׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb the voice|קוֹל֩\rb* \rb of the living|חַיִּ֜ים\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֨ים\rb* \rb speaking|מְדַבֵּ֧ר\rb* \rb out of|מִתּוֹךְ־\rb* \rb the fire,|הָאֵ֛שׁ\rb* \rb as we have,|כָּמֹ֖נוּ\rb* \rb and survived?|וַיֶּֽחִי׃\rb* \v 27 \rb Go near|קְרַ֤ב\rb* \rb and listen|וּֽשֲׁמָ֔ע\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb to all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb says.|יֹאמַ֖ר\rb* \rb Then you|וְאַ֣תְּ׀\rb* \rb can tell|תְּדַבֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֵלֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb us|אֵת֩\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֛ינוּ\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb tells you;|יְדַבֵּ֜ר\rb* \rb we will listen|וְשָׁמַ֥עְנוּ\rb* \rb and obey.”|וְעָשִֽׂינוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb you spoke|בְּדַבֶּרְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלָ֑י\rb* \rb and He|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb “I have heard|שָׁמַ֖עְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |ק֨וֹל\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֜י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֤ם\rb* \rb have spoken|דִּבְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb to you.|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb They have done well|הֵיטִ֖יבוּ\rb* \rb in all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they have spoken.|דִּבֵּֽרוּ׃\rb* \v 29 \rb If only|מִֽי־\rb*\rb |יִתֵּ֡ן\rb* \rb they had|וְהָיָה֩\rb* \rb such|זֶ֜ה\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb a heart|לְבָבָ֨ם\rb* \rb to fear|לְיִרְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb Me|אֹתִ֛י\rb* \rb and keep|וְלִשְׁמֹ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb My commandments|מִצְוֺתַ֖י\rb* \rb always,|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֑ים\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb it might be well|יִיטַ֥ב\rb* \rb with them|לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb and with their children|וְלִבְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb forever.|לְעֹלָֽם׃\rb* \v 30 \rb Go|לֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb and tell|אֱמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb them:|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb ‘Return|שׁ֥וּבוּ\rb* \rb to your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb tents.’|לְאָהֳלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 31 \rb But you|וְאַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb stand|עֲמֹ֣ד\rb* \rb here|פֹּה֮\rb* \rb with Me,|עִמָּדִי֒\rb* \rb that I may speak|וַאֲדַבְּרָ֣ה\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֗יךָ\rb*\rb |אֵ֧ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the commandments|הַמִּצְוָ֛ה\rb* \rb and statutes|וְהַחֻקִּ֥ים\rb* \rb and ordinances|וְהַמִּשְׁפָּטִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you are to teach them|תְּלַמְּדֵ֑ם\rb* \rb to follow|וְעָשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb in the land|בָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb am giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to possess.”|לְרִשְׁתָּֽהּ׃\rb*
\p \v 32 \rb So be careful|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשׂ֔וֹת\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb has commanded you;|צִוָּ֛ה\rb* \rb you are not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to turn aside|תָסֻ֖רוּ\rb* \rb to the right|יָמִ֥ין\rb* \rb or to the left.|וּשְׂמֹֽאל׃\rb* \v 33 \rb You must walk|תֵּלֵ֑כוּ\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the ways|הַדֶּ֗רֶךְ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb has commanded you,|צִוָּ֜ה\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֤עַן\rb* \rb you may live|תִּֽחְיוּן֙\rb* \rb and prosper|וְט֣וֹב\rb* \rb and prolong|וְהַאֲרַכְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb your days|יָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you will possess.|תִּֽירָשֽׁוּן׃\rb*
\c 6
\s1 The Greatest Commandment
\r \ref Matthew 22:34–40|MAT 22:34-40\ref*; \ref Mark 12:28–34|MRK 12:28-34\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb These are|וְזֹ֣את\rb* \rb the commandments|הַמִּצְוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and statutes|הַֽחֻקִּים֙\rb* \rb and ordinances|וְהַמִּשְׁפָּטִ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb has instructed me|צִוָּ֛ה\rb* \rb to teach you|לְלַמֵּ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb to follow|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֛ם\rb* \rb are about to enter|עֹבְרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb and possess,|לְרִשְׁתָּֽהּ׃\rb* \v 2 \rb so that you|לְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb and your children|וּבִנְךָ֣\rb* \rb and grandchildren|וּבֶן־\rb*\rb |בִּנְךָ֔\rb* \rb may fear|תִּירָ֜א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of your lives|חַיֶּ֑יךָ\rb* \rb by keeping|לִ֠שְׁמֹר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb His statutes|חֻקֹּתָ֣יו\rb* \rb and commandments|וּמִצְוֺתָיו֮\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb give|מְצַוֶּךָ֒\rb* \rb you,|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb and so that|וּלְמַ֖עַן\rb* \rb your days|יָמֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb may be prolonged.|יַאֲרִכֻ֥ן\rb* \v 3 \rb Hear,|וְשָׁמַעְתָּ֤\rb* \rb O Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb and be careful|וְשָׁמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb to observe them,|לַעֲשׂ֔וֹת\rb* \rb so that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb you may prosper|יִיטַ֣ב\rb*\rb |לְךָ֔\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb and multiply|תִּרְבּ֖וּן\rb* \rb greatly|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb in a land|אֶ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb flowing|זָבַ֥ת\rb* \rb with milk|חָלָ֖ב\rb* \rb and honey,|וּדְבָֽשׁ׃פ\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of your fathers,|אֲבֹתֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb has promised|דִּבֶּ֨ר\rb* \rb you.|לָ֔ךְ\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Hear,|שְׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb O Israel:|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God,|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה׀\rb* \rb is One.|אֶחָֽד׃\rb*\f + \fr 6:4 \ft Or \fqa The LORD our God is One LORD \ft or \fqa The LORD is our God, the LORD is One \ft or \fqa The LORD is our God, the LORD alone\ft ; cited in \ref Mark 12:29|MRK 12:29\ref*\f* \v 5 \rb And you shall love|וְאָ֣הַבְתָּ֔\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָבְךָ֥\rb* \rb and with all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb your soul|נַפְשְׁךָ֖\rb* \rb and with all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb your strength.|מְאֹדֶֽךָ׃\rb*\f + \fr 6:5 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 22:37|MAT 22:37\ref*, Mark 12:30, and Luke 10:27\f*
\p \v 6 \rb These|הָאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֧י\rb* \rb am commanding you|מְצַוְּךָ֛\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb are to be|וְהָי֞וּ\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb your hearts.|לְבָבֶֽךָ׃\rb* \v 7 \rb And you shall teach them diligently|וְשִׁנַּנְתָּ֣ם\rb* \rb to your children|לְבָנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and speak|וְדִבַּרְתָּ֖\rb* \rb of them|בָּ֑ם\rb* \rb when you sit|בְּשִׁבְתְּךָ֤\rb* \rb at home|בְּבֵיתֶ֙ךָ֙\rb* \rb and when you walk|וּבְלֶכְתְּךָ֣\rb* \rb along the road,|בַדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb when you lie down|וּֽבְשָׁכְבְּךָ֖\rb* \rb and when you get up.|וּבְקוּמֶֽךָ׃\rb* \v 8 \rb Tie them|וּקְשַׁרְתָּ֥ם\rb* \rb as reminders|לְא֖וֹת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb your hands|יָדֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb and bind them|וְהָי֥וּ\rb*\rb |לְטֹטָפֹ֖ת\rb* \rb on your foreheads.|בֵּ֥ין\rb*\rb |עֵינֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 9 \rb Write them|וּכְתַבְתָּ֛ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the doorposts|מְזוּזֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of your houses|בֵּיתֶ֖ךָ\rb* \rb and on your gates.|וּבִשְׁעָרֶֽיךָ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb |וְהָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb And when|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb brings|יְבִיאֲךָ֣׀\rb* \rb you into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb* \rb He swore|נִשְׁבַּ֧ע\rb* \rb to your fathers,|לַאֲבֹתֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb to Abraham,|לְאַבְרָהָ֛ם\rb* \rb Isaac,|לְיִצְחָ֥ק\rb* \rb and Jacob,|וּֽלְיַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb that He would give|לָ֣תֶת\rb* \rb you—|לָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb a land with great|גְּדֹלֹ֥ת\rb* \rb and splendid|וְטֹבֹ֖ת\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb build,|בָנִֽיתָ׃\rb* \v 11 \rb with houses|וּבָ֨תִּ֜ים\rb* \rb full of|מְלֵאִ֣ים\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb good|טוּב֮\rb* \rb thing with which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb fill them,|מִלֵּאתָ֒\rb* \rb with wells|וּבֹרֹ֤ת\rb*\rb |חֲצוּבִים֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb dig,|חָצַ֔בְתָּ\rb* \rb and with vineyards|כְּרָמִ֥ים\rb* \rb and olive groves|וְזֵיתִ֖ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb plant—|נָטָ֑עְתָּ\rb* \rb and when you eat|וְאָכַלְתָּ֖\rb* \rb and are satisfied,|וְשָׂבָֽעְתָּ׃\rb* \v 12 \rb be careful|הִשָּׁ֣מֶר\rb* \rb not|פֶּן־\rb* \rb to forget|תִּשְׁכַּ֖ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb brought you out|הוֹצִֽיאֲךָ֛\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb out of the house|מִבֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of slavery.|עֲבָדִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Fear|תִּירָ֖א\rb*\rb |וְאֹת֣וֹ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb serve Him only,|תַעֲבֹ֑ד\rb* \rb and take your oaths|תִּשָּׁבֵֽעַ׃\rb* \rb in His name.|וּבִשְׁמ֖וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 6:13 \ft Or \fqa serve Him, and take your oaths only in His name\ft ; cited in \ref Matthew 4:10|MAT 4:10\ref* and Luke 4:8\f* \v 14 \rb Do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb follow|תֵֽלְכ֔וּן\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֑ים\rb* \rb gods,|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb the gods|מֵאֱלֹהֵי֙\rb* \rb of the peoples|הָֽעַמִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb around you.|סְבִיבוֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 15 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb who is among you,|בְּקִרְבֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb is a jealous|קַנָּ֛א\rb* \rb God.|אֵ֥ל\rb* \rb Otherwise|פֶּן־\rb* \rb the anger|אַף־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb will be kindled|יֶ֠חֱרֶה\rb* \rb against you,|בָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and He will wipe you|וְהִשְׁמִ֣ידְךָ֔\rb* \rb off|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the earth.|הָאֲדָמָֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb Do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb test|תְנַסּ֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you tested Him|נִסִּיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb at Massah.|בַּמַּסָּֽה׃\rb*\f + \fr 6:16 \fqa Massah \ft means \fqa testing\ft ; see \ref Exodus 17:7|EXO 17:7\ref*; cited in Matthew 4:7 and Luke 4:12.\f* \v 17 \rb You are to diligently keep|שָׁמ֣וֹר\rb*\rb |תִּשְׁמְר֔וּן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the commandments|מִצְוֺ֖ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and the testimonies|וְעֵדֹתָ֥יו\rb* \rb and statutes|וְחֻקָּ֖יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He has given you.|צִוָּֽךְ׃\rb* \v 18 \rb Do|וְעָשִׂ֛יתָ\rb* \rb what is right|הַיָּשָׁ֥ר\rb* \rb and good|וְהַטּ֖וֹב\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb it may be well|יִ֣יטַב\rb* \rb with you|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and that you may enter|וּבָ֗אתָ\rb* \rb and possess|וְיָֽרַשְׁתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the good|הַטֹּבָ֔ה\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God swore|נִשְׁבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb to give your fathers,|לַאֲבֹתֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 19 \rb driving out|לַהֲדֹ֥ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your enemies|אֹיְבֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb before you,|מִפָּנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb has said.|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb*
\s1 Teach Your Children
\p \v 20 \rb In the future,|מָחָ֖ר\rb* \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb your son|בִנְךָ֛\rb* \rb asks,|יִשְׁאָלְךָ֥\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “What|מָ֣ה\rb* \rb is the meaning of the decrees|הָעֵדֹ֗ת\rb* \rb and statutes|וְהַֽחֻקִּים֙\rb* \rb and ordinances|וְהַמִּשְׁפָּטִ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb has commanded you?”|צִוָּ֛ה\rb* \v 21 \rb then you are to tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb him,|לְבִנְךָ֔\rb* \rb “We were|הָיִ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb slaves|עֲבָדִ֛ים\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|לְפַרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb in Egypt,|בְּמִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb but the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb brought us out|וַיּוֹצִיאֵ֧נוּ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb with a mighty|חֲזָקָֽה׃\rb* \rb hand.|בְּיָ֥ד\rb* \v 22 \rb Before our eyes|לְעֵינֵֽינוּ׃\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֡ה\rb* \rb inflicted|וַיִּתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb great|גְּדֹלִ֨ים\rb* \rb and devastating|וְרָעִ֧ים׀\rb* \rb signs|אוֹתֹ֣ת\rb* \rb and wonders|וּ֠מֹפְתִים\rb* \rb on Egypt,|בְּמִצְרַ֛יִם\rb* \rb on Pharaoh,|בְּפַרְעֹ֥ה\rb* \rb and on all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb his household.|בֵּית֖וֹ\rb* \v 23 \rb But He brought|הוֹצִ֣יא\rb* \rb us out|וְאוֹתָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb from there|מִשָּׁ֑ם\rb* \rb to|לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb lead us in|הָבִ֣יא\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔נוּ\rb* \rb and give|לָ֤תֶת\rb* \rb us|לָ֙נוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He had sworn|נִשְׁבַּ֖ע\rb* \rb to our fathers.|לַאֲבֹתֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb commanded us|וַיְצַוֵּ֣נוּ\rb* \rb to observe|לַעֲשׂוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb statutes|הַחֻקִּ֣ים\rb* \rb and to fear|לְיִרְאָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God,|אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb that we may always be prosperous|לְט֥וֹב\rb*\rb |לָ֙נוּ֙\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb* \rb and preserved,|לְחַיֹּתֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb as we are to this day.|כְּהַיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \v 25 \rb And if we are careful|נִשְׁמֹ֨ר\rb* \rb to observe|לַעֲשׂ֜וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb one of these|הַזֹּ֗את\rb* \rb commandments|הַמִּצְוָ֣ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֛י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God,|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He has commanded us,|צִוָּֽנוּ׃ס\rb* \rb then that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb will be|תִּֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb our|לָּ֑נוּ\rb* \rb righteousness.”|וּצְדָקָ֖ה\rb*
\c 7
\s1 Drive Out the Nations
\p \v 1 \rb When|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb brings|יְבִֽיאֲךָ֙\rb* \rb you into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֕רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb are entering|בָא־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb to possess,|לְרִשְׁתָּ֑הּ\rb* \rb and He drives out|וְנָשַׁ֣ל\rb* \rb before you|מִפָּנֶ֡יךָ\rb* \rb many|רַבִּ֣ים׀\rb* \rb nations—|גּֽוֹיִם־\rb* \rb the Hittites,|הַֽחִתִּי֩\rb* \rb Girgashites,|וְהַגִּרְגָּשִׁ֨י\rb* \rb Amorites,|וְהָאֱמֹרִ֜י\rb* \rb Canaanites,|וְהַכְּנַעֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb Perizzites,|וְהַפְּרִזִּ֗י\rb* \rb Hivites,|וְהַֽחִוִּי֙\rb* \rb and Jebusites,|וְהַיְבוּסִ֔י\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָ֣ה\rb* \rb nations|גוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb larger|רַבִּ֥ים\rb* \rb and stronger|וַעֲצוּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb than you—|מִמֶּֽךָּ׃\rb* \v 2 \rb and when the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb has delivered them over|וּנְתָנָ֞ם\rb* \rb to you|לְפָנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb to defeat them,|וְהִכִּיתָ֑ם\rb* \rb then you must devote them to complete destruction.|הַחֲרֵ֤ם\rb*\f + \fr 7:2 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering; also twice in verse 26.\f* \rb |תַּחֲרִים֙\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔ם\rb*\rb Make|תִכְרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb treaty|בְּרִ֖ית\rb*\f + \fr 7:2 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa berit \ft are translated in most passages as \fqa covenant\ft .\f* \rb with them|לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb and show them no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb mercy.|תְחָנֵּֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Do not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb intermarry|תִתְחַתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb with them.|בָּ֑ם\rb* \rb Do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb give|תִתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb your daughters|בִּתְּךָ֙\rb* \rb to their sons|לִבְנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb or|לֹא־\rb* \rb take|תִקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb their daughters|וּבִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb for your sons,|לִבְנֶֽךָ׃\rb* \v 4 \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they will turn your sons|בִּנְךָ֙\rb* \rb away|יָסִ֤יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from following Me|מֵֽאַחֲרַ֔י\rb* \rb to serve|וְעָבְד֖וּ\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֑ים\rb* \rb gods.|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb Then the anger|אַף־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb will burn|וְחָרָ֤ה\rb* \rb against you,|בָּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and He will swiftly|מַהֵֽר׃\rb* \rb destroy you.|וְהִשְׁמִידְךָ֖\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Instead,|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb you are to do to them:|תַעֲשׂוּ֙\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb tear down|תִּתֹּ֔צוּ\rb* \rb their altars,|מִזְבְּחֹתֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb smash|תְּשַׁבֵּ֑רוּ\rb* \rb their sacred pillars,|וּמַצֵּבֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb cut down|תְּגַדֵּע֔וּן\rb* \rb their Asherah poles,|וַאֲשֵֽׁירֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb and burn|תִּשְׂרְפ֥וּן\rb* \rb their idols|וּפְסִילֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in the fire.|בָּאֵֽשׁ׃\rb* \v 6 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֔ה\rb* \rb are a people|עַ֤ם\rb* \rb holy|קָדוֹשׁ֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb has chosen you|בָּחַ֣ר׀\rb* \rb to be|לִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb a people|לְעַ֣ם\rb* \rb for His|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb prized possession|סְגֻלָּ֔ה\rb* \rb out of all|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb peoples|הָֽעַמִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the earth.|הָאֲדָמָֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb set His affection|חָשַׁ֧ק\rb* \rb on you|בָּכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and choose|וַיִּבְחַ֣ר\rb* \rb you|בָּכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb because you were more numerous|מֵֽרֻבְּכֶ֞ם\rb* \rb than the other|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb peoples,|הָֽעַמִּ֗ים\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb were the fewest|הַמְעַ֖ט\rb* \rb of all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb peoples.|הָעַמִּֽים׃\rb* \v 8 \rb But|כִּי֩\rb* \rb because the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb loved|מֵֽאַהֲבַ֨ת\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and kept|וּמִשָּׁמְר֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the oath|הַשְּׁבֻעָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb He swore|נִשְׁבַּע֙\rb* \rb to your fathers,|לַאֲבֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb He|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb brought you out|הוֹצִ֧יא\rb* \rb with a mighty|חֲזָקָ֑ה\rb* \rb hand|בְּיָ֣ד\rb* \rb and redeemed you|וַֽיִּפְדְּךָ֙\rb* \rb from the house|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of slavery,|עֲבָדִ֔ים\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֖ד\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֥ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Know therefore|וְיָ֣דַעְתָּ֔\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb is God,|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb the faithful|הַֽנֶּאֱמָ֔ן\rb* \rb God|הָאֵל֙\rb* \rb who keeps|שֹׁמֵ֧ר\rb* \rb His covenant|הַבְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of loving devotion|וְהַחֶ֗סֶד\rb* \rb for a thousand|לְאֶ֥לֶף\rb* \rb generations|דּֽוֹר׃\rb* \rb of those who love Him|לְאֹהֲבָ֛יו\rb* \rb and keep|וּלְשֹׁמְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb His commandments.|מִצְוֹתוֹ\rb* \v 10 \rb But those who hate Him|לְשֹׂנְאָ֛יו\rb* \rb He repays|וּמְשַׁלֵּ֧ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb their faces|פָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb with destruction;|לְהַאֲבִיד֑וֹ\rb* \rb He will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb hesitate|יְאַחֵר֙\rb* \rb to repay|יְשַׁלֶּם־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his face|פָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb the one who hates Him.|לְשֹׂ֣נְא֔וֹ\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb So keep|וְשָׁמַרְתָּ֨\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the commandments|הַמִּצְוָ֜ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb statutes|הַֽחֻקִּ֣ים\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb ordinances|הַמִּשְׁפָּטִ֗ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֧י\rb* \rb am giving you|מְצַוְּךָ֛\rb* \rb to follow|לַעֲשׂוֹתָֽם׃פ\rb* \rb this day.|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb*
\s1 The Promises of God
\r \ref Exodus 23:20–33|EXO 23:20-33\ref*)
\p \v 12 \rb |וְהָיָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb If|עֵ֣קֶב\rb* \rb you listen to|תִּשְׁמְע֗וּן\rb*\rb |אֵ֤ת\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb ordinances|הַמִּשְׁפָּטִים֙\rb* \rb and keep them carefully,|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb then the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb will keep|וְשָׁמַר֩\rb* \rb His covenant|הַבְּרִית֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the loving devotion|הַחֶ֔סֶד\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He swore|נִשְׁבַּ֖ע\rb* \rb to your fathers.|לַאֲבֹתֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 13 \rb He will love you|וַאֲהֵ֣בְךָ֔\rb* \rb and bless you|וּבֵרַכְךָ֖\rb* \rb and multiply you.|וְהִרְבֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb He will bless|וּבֵרַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb the fruit|פְּרִֽי־\rb* \rb of your womb|בִטְנְךָ֣\rb* \rb and the produce|וּפְרִֽי־\rb* \rb of your land—|אַ֠דְמָתֶךָ\rb* \rb your grain,|דְּגָ֨נְךָ֜\rb* \rb new wine,|וְתִֽירֹשְׁךָ֣\rb* \rb and oil,|וְיִצְהָרֶ֗ךָ\rb* \rb the young|שְׁגַר־\rb* \rb of your herds|אֲלָפֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb and the lambs|וְעַשְׁתְּרֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of your flocks—|צֹאנֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb in|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the land|הָֽאֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He swore|נִשְׁבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb to your fathers|לַאֲבֹתֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb to give|לָ֥תֶת\rb* \rb you.|לָֽךְ׃\rb* \v 14 \rb You will be|תִּֽהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb blessed|בָּר֥וּךְ\rb* \rb above all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb peoples;|הָעַמִּ֑ים\rb* \rb among you|בְךָ֛\rb* \rb there will be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb barren man|עָקָ֥ר\rb* \rb or woman|וַֽעֲקָרָ֖ה\rb* \rb or livestock.|וּבִבְהֶמְתֶּֽךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb will remove|וְהֵסִ֧יר\rb* \rb from you|מִמְּךָ֖\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb sickness.|חֹ֑לִי\rb* \rb He will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb lay|יְשִׂימָם֙\rb* \rb upon you|בָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb any|וְכָל־\rb* \rb of the terrible|הָרָעִ֜ים\rb* \rb diseases|מַדְוֵי֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you knew|יָדַ֗עְתָּ\rb* \rb in Egypt,|מִצְרַ֨יִם\rb* \rb but He will inflict them|וּנְתָנָ֖ם\rb* \rb on all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb who hate you.|שֹׂנְאֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 16 \rb You must destroy|וְאָכַלְתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the peoples|הָֽעַמִּ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb will deliver|נֹתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb to you.|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb Do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb look|עֵֽינְךָ֖\rb* \rb on them|עֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb with pity.|תָחֹ֥ס\rb* \rb Do not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb worship|תַעֲבֹד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their gods,|אֱלֹ֣הֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb that|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb will be a snare|מוֹקֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb to you.|לָֽךְ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb |כִּ֤י\rb* \rb You may say|תֹאמַר֙\rb* \rb in your heart,|בִּלְבָ֣בְךָ֔\rb* \rb “These|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֥ם\rb* \rb are greater|רַבִּ֛ים\rb* \rb than we are;|מִמֶּ֑נִּי\rb* \rb how|אֵיכָ֥ה\rb* \rb can|אוּכַ֖ל\rb* \rb we drive them out?”|לְהוֹרִישָֽׁם׃\rb* \v 18 \rb But do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be afraid|תִירָ֖א\rb* \rb of them.|מֵהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb Be sure to remember|זָכֹ֣ר\rb*\rb |תִּזְכֹּ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֵ֤ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb did|עָשָׂה֙\rb* \rb to Pharaoh|לְפַרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb and all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb Egypt:|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 19 \rb the great|הַגְּדֹלֹ֜ת\rb* \rb trials|הַמַּסֹּ֨ת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|עֵינֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb saw,|רָא֣וּ\rb* \rb the signs|וְהָאֹתֹ֤ת\rb* \rb and wonders,|וְהַמֹּֽפְתִים֙\rb* \rb and the mighty|הַחֲזָקָה֙\rb* \rb hand|וְהַיָּ֤ד\rb* \rb and outstretched|הַנְּטוּיָ֔ה\rb* \rb arm|וְהַזְּרֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb by which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb brought you out.|הוֹצִֽאֲךָ֖\rb* \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb will do|יַעֲשֶׂ֞ה\rb* \rb the same|כֵּֽן־\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the peoples|הָ֣עַמִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb now fear.|יָרֵ֖א\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb Moreover,|וְגַם֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb will send|יְשַׁלַּ֛ח\rb* \rb the hornet|הַצִּרְעָ֔ה\rb* \rb against them|בָּ֑ם\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb even the survivors|הַנִּשְׁאָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb hiding|וְהַנִּסְתָּרִ֖ים\rb* \rb from you|מִפָּנֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb have perished.|אֲבֹ֗ד\rb* \v 21 \rb Do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be terrified|תַעֲרֹ֖ץ\rb* \rb by them,|מִפְּנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb who is among you,|בְּקִרְבֶּ֔ךָ\rb* \rb is a great|גָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb and awesome|וְנוֹרָֽא׃\rb* \rb God.|אֵ֥ל\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will drive out|וְנָשַׁל֩\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֥ם\rb* \rb before you|מִפָּנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb little|מְעַ֣ט\rb* \rb by little.|מְעָ֑ט\rb* \rb You will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb be enabled|תוּכַל֙\rb* \rb to eliminate them|כַּלֹּתָ֣ם\rb* \rb all at once,|מַהֵ֔ר\rb* \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb the wild|הַשָּׂדֶֽה׃\rb* \rb animals|חַיַּ֥ת\rb* \rb would multiply|תִּרְבֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb around you.|עָלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \v 23 \rb But the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb will give them over|וּנְתָנָ֛ם\rb* \rb to you|לְפָנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb and throw them|וְהָמָם֙\rb* \rb into great|גְדֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb confusion,|מְהוּמָ֣ה\rb* \rb until|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb they are destroyed.|הִשָּׁמְדָֽם׃\rb* \v 24 \rb He will hand their kings|מַלְכֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb over to|וְנָתַ֤ן\rb* \rb you,|בְּיָדֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and you will wipe out|וְהַאֲבַדְתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their names|שְׁמָ֔ם\rb* \rb from under|מִתַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb heaven.|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb No|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb one|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb will be able to stand|יִתְיַצֵּ֥ב\rb* \rb against you;|בְּפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |עַ֥ד\rb* \rb you will annihilate them.|הִשְׁמִֽדְךָ֖\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb You must burn up|תִּשְׂרְפ֣וּן\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb the images|פְּסִילֵ֥י\rb* \rb of their gods;|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb covet|תַחְמֹד֩\rb* \rb the silver|כֶּ֨סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וְזָהָ֤ב\rb* \rb that is on them|עֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb or take it|וְלָקַחְתָּ֣\rb* \rb for yourselves,|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb or|פֶּ֚ן\rb* \rb you will be ensnared|תִּוָּקֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb by it;|בּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb it|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is detestable|תוֹעֲבַ֛ת\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \v 26 \rb And you must not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb bring|תָבִ֤יא\rb* \rb any detestable thing|תֽוֹעֵבָה֙\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb your house,|בֵּיתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb or you,|וְהָיִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb like it,|כָּמֹ֑הוּ\rb* \rb will be set apart for destruction.|חֵ֖רֶם\rb* \rb You are to utterly detest|שַׁקֵּ֧ץ׀\rb*\rb |תְּשַׁקְּצֶ֛נּוּ\rb* \rb and abhor it,|וְתַעֵ֥ב׀\rb*\rb |תְּֽתַעֲבֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb it|הֽוּא׃פ\rb* \rb is set apart for destruction.|חֵ֥רֶם\rb*
\c 8
\s1 Remember the LORD Your God
\p \v 1 \rb You must carefully|תִּשְׁמְר֣וּן\rb* \rb follow|לַעֲשׂ֑וֹת\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb commandment|הַמִּצְוָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֧י\rb* \rb am giving you|מְצַוְּךָ֛\rb* \rb today,|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb you may live|תִּֽחְי֜וּן\rb* \rb and multiply,|וּרְבִיתֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and enter|וּבָאתֶם֙\rb* \rb and possess|וִֽירִשְׁתֶּ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb swore to give|נִשְׁבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb your fathers.|לַאֲבֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 2 \rb Remember that|וְזָכַרְתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|זֶ֛ה\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb led you|הֹלִֽיכֲךָ֜\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the way|הַדֶּ֗רֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb in the wilderness,|בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb He might humble you|עַנֹּֽתְךָ֜\rb* \rb and test you|לְנַסֹּֽתְךָ֗\rb* \rb in order to know|לָדַ֜עַת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb was in your heart,|בִּֽלְבָבְךָ֛\rb* \rb whether or|אִם־\rb* \rb not|לֹֽא׃\rb* \rb you would keep|הֲתִשְׁמֹ֥ר\rb* \rb His commandments.|מִצְוֹתוֹ\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb He humbled you,|וַֽיְעַנְּךָ֮\rb* \rb and in your hunger|וַיַּרְעִבֶךָ֒\rb* \rb He gave you manna|הַמָּן֙\rb* \rb to eat,|וַיַּֽאֲכִֽלְךָ֤\rb*\rb |אֶת\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb neither you|לֹא־\rb* \rb nor|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֹתֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb had known,|יָדַ֔עְתָּ\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֣עַן\rb*\rb |הוֹדִֽעֲךָ֗\rb* \rb you might understand|יָדְע֖וּן\rb* \rb that|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb man|הָֽאָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb does not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb live|יִחְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb bread|הַלֶּ֤חֶם\rb* \rb alone,|לְבַדּוֹ֙\rb* \rb but|כִּ֛י\rb*\rb |יִחְיֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |הָאָדָֽם׃\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb word that comes from|מוֹצָ֥א\rb* \rb the mouth|פִֽי־\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 8:3 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 4:4|MAT 4:4\ref* and Luke 4:4\f* \v 4 \rb Your clothing|שִׂמְלָ֨תְךָ֜\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb wear out|בָֽלְתָה֙\rb*\rb |מֵֽעָלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and your feet|וְרַגְלְךָ֖\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb swell|בָצֵ֑קָה\rb* \rb during these|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb So know|וְיָדַעְתָּ֖\rb* \rb in|עִם־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָבֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb a man|אִישׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb disciplines|יְיַסֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb his son,|בְּנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb so the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb disciplines you.|מְיַסְּרֶֽךָּ׃\rb* \v 6 \rb Therefore you shall keep|וְשָׁ֣מַרְתָּ֔\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the commandments|מִצְוֺ֖ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb walking|לָלֶ֥כֶת\rb* \rb in His ways|בִּדְרָכָ֖יו\rb* \rb and fearing|וּלְיִרְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb Him.|אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb is bringing|מְבִֽיאֲךָ֖\rb* \rb you into|אֶל־\rb* \rb a good|טוֹבָ֑ה\rb* \rb land,|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֚רֶץ\rb* \rb of brooks|נַ֣חֲלֵי\rb*\rb |מָ֔יִם\rb* \rb and fountains|עֲיָנֹת֙\rb* \rb and springs|וּתְהֹמֹ֔ת\rb* \rb that flow|יֹצְאִ֥ים\rb* \rb through the valleys|בַּבִּקְעָ֖ה\rb* \rb and hills;|וּבָהָֽר׃\rb* \v 8 \rb a land|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of wheat,|חִטָּה֙\rb* \rb barley,|וּשְׂעֹרָ֔ה\rb* \rb vines,|וְגֶ֥פֶן\rb* \rb fig trees,|וּתְאֵנָ֖ה\rb* \rb and pomegranates;|וְרִמּ֑וֹן\rb* \rb a land|אֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of olive|זֵ֥ית\rb* \rb oil|שֶׁ֖מֶן\rb* \rb and honey;|וּדְבָֽשׁ׃\rb* \v 9 \rb a land|אֶ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you will eat|תֹּֽאכַל־\rb* \rb food|לֶ֔חֶם\rb* \rb without|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb scarcity,|בְמִסְכֵּנֻת֙\rb* \rb where you will lack|תֶחְסַ֥ר\rb* \rb nothing;|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |כֹּ֖ל\rb*\rb |בָּ֑הּ\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֚רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb whose rocks|אֲבָנֶ֣יהָ\rb* \rb are iron|בַרְזֶ֔ל\rb* \rb and whose hills|וּמֵהֲרָרֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb are ready to be mined|תַּחְצֹ֥ב\rb* \rb for copper.|נְחֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb* \v 10 \rb When you eat|וְאָכַלְתָּ֖\rb* \rb and are satisfied,|וְשָׂבָ֑עְתָּ\rb* \rb you are to bless|וּבֵֽרַכְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the good|הַטֹּבָ֖ה\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He has given|נָֽתַן־\rb* \rb you.|לָֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Be careful|הִשָּׁ֣מֶר\rb* \rb not|פֶּן־\rb* \rb to forget|תִּשְׁכַּ֖ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb by failing|לְבִלְתִּ֨י\rb* \rb to keep|שְׁמֹ֤ר\rb* \rb His commandments|מִצְוֺתָיו֙\rb* \rb and ordinances|וּמִשְׁפָּטָ֣יו\rb* \rb and statutes,|וְחֻקֹּתָ֔יו\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb am giving you|מְצַוְּךָ֖\rb* \rb this day.|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb* \v 12 \rb Otherwise,|פֶּן־\rb* \rb when you eat|תֹּאכַ֖ל\rb* \rb and are satisfied,|וְשָׂבָ֑עְתָּ\rb* \rb when you build|תִּבְנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb fine|טוֹבִ֛ים\rb* \rb houses|וּבָתִּ֥ים\rb* \rb in which to dwell,|וְיָשָֽׁבְתָּ׃\rb* \v 13 \rb and when your herds|וּבְקָֽרְךָ֤\rb* \rb and flocks|וְצֹֽאנְךָ֙\rb* \rb grow large|יִרְבְּיֻ֔ן\rb* \rb and your silver|וְכֶ֥סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וְזָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb increase|יִרְבֶּה־\rb* \rb and all|וְכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you have|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb is multiplied,|יִרְבֶּֽה׃\rb* \v 14 \rb then your heart|לְבָבֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb will become proud,|וְרָ֖ם\rb* \rb and you will forget|וְשָֽׁכַחְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb who brought you out|הַמּוֹצִיאֲךָ֛\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb out of the house|מִבֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of slavery.|עֲבָדִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb He led|הַמּוֹלִ֨יכֲךָ֜\rb* \rb you through the vast|הַגָּדֹ֣ל\rb* \rb and terrifying|וְהַנּוֹרָ֗א\rb* \rb wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֣ר׀\rb* \rb with its venomous|שָׂרָף֙\rb* \rb snakes|נָחָ֤שׁ׀\rb* \rb and scorpions,|וְעַקְרָ֔ב\rb* \rb a thirsty|וְצִמָּא֖וֹן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֵֽין־\rb* \rb and waterless land.|מָ֑יִם\rb* \rb He brought|הַמּוֹצִ֤יא\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb water|מַ֔יִם\rb* \rb from the rock|מִצּ֖וּר\rb* \rb of flint.|הַֽחַלָּמִֽישׁ׃\rb* \v 16 \rb He fed you|הַמַּֽאֲכִ֨לְךָ֥\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֔ר\rb* \rb with manna|מָן֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֹתֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb had not|לֹא־\rb* \rb known,|יָדְע֖וּן\rb* \rb in order to|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb humble you|עַנֹּֽתְךָ֗\rb*\rb |וּלְמַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb and test you,|נַסֹּתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb so that in the end|בְּאַחֲרִיתֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb He might cause you to prosper.|לְהֵיטִֽבְךָ֖\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb You might say|וְאָמַרְתָּ֖\rb* \rb in your heart,|בִּלְבָבֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb “The power|כֹּחִי֙\rb* \rb and strength|וְעֹ֣צֶם\rb* \rb of my hands|יָדִ֔י\rb* \rb have made|עָ֥שָׂה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb wealth|הַחַ֥יִל\rb* \rb for me.”|לִ֖י\rb* \v 18 \rb But remember|וְזָֽכַרְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb that it is the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb who|ה֗וּא\rb* \rb gives|הַנֹּתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֛\rb* \rb the power|כֹּ֖חַ\rb* \rb to gain|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb wealth,|חָ֑יִל\rb* \rb in order to|לְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb confirm|הָקִ֧ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His covenant|בְּרִית֛וֹ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He swore|נִשְׁבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb to your fathers|לַאֲבֹתֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb even to this|הַזֶּֽה׃פ\rb* \rb day.|כַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you ever forget|שָׁכֹ֤חַ\rb*\rb |תִּשְׁכַּח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and go|וְהָֽלַכְתָּ֗\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb to worship|וַעֲבַדְתָּ֖ם\rb* \rb and bow down|וְהִשְׁתַּחֲוִ֣יתָ\rb* \rb to them,|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb I testify|הַעִדֹ֤תִי\rb* \rb against you|בָכֶם֙\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you will surely perish.|אָבֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |תֹּאבֵדֽוּן׃\rb* \v 20 \rb Like the nations|כַּגּוֹיִ֗ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has destroyed|מַאֲבִ֣יד\rb* \rb before you,|מִפְּנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb so|כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb you will perish|תֹאבֵד֑וּן\rb*\rb |עֵ֚קֶב\rb* \rb if you do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb obey|תִשְׁמְע֔וּן\rb*\rb |בְּק֖וֹל\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃פ\rb*
\c 9
\s1 Assurance of Victory
\p \v 1 \rb Hear,|שְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb O Israel:|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb Today|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֨ה\rb* \rb are about to cross|עֹבֵ֤ר\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to go in|לָבֹא֙\rb* \rb and dispossess|לָרֶ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb nations|גּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb greater|גְּדֹלִ֥ים\rb* \rb and stronger|וַעֲצֻמִ֖ים\rb* \rb than you,|מִמֶּ֑ךָּ\rb* \rb with large|גְּדֹלֹ֥ת\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb fortified|וּבְצֻרֹ֖ת\rb* \rb to the heavens.|בַּשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 2 \rb The people|עַֽם־\rb* \rb are strong|גָּד֥וֹל\rb* \rb and tall,|וָרָ֖ם\rb* \rb the descendants|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Anakim.|עֲנָקִ֑ים\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֙עְתָּ֙\rb* \rb about them,|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb and you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb have heard it said,|שָׁמַ֔עְתָּ\rb* \rb “Who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb can stand up|יִתְיַצֵּ֔ב\rb* \rb to|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Anak?”|עֲנָֽק׃\rb* \v 3 \rb But understand|וְיָדַעְתָּ֣\rb* \rb that|כִּי֩\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ\rb*\rb |הֽוּא־\rb* \rb goes across|הָעֹבֵ֤ר\rb* \rb ahead of you|לְפָנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb as a consuming|אֹֽכְלָ֔ה\rb*\rb |ה֧וּא\rb* \rb fire;|אֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb He will destroy them|יַשְׁמִידֵ֛ם\rb*\rb |וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb and subdue them|יַכְנִיעֵ֖ם\rb* \rb before you.|לְפָנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb And you will drive them out|וְהֽוֹרַשְׁתָּ֤ם\rb* \rb and annihilate them|וְהַֽאַבַדְתָּם֙\rb* \rb swiftly,|מַהֵ֔ר\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has promised|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb you.|לָֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb When the LORD|יְהוָה֩\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֨יךָ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֥ם׀\rb* \rb has driven them out|בַּהֲדֹ֣ף\rb* \rb before you,|מִלְּפָנֶיךָ֮\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹר֒\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb say|תֹּאמַ֣ר\rb* \rb in your heart,|בִּלְבָבְךָ֗\rb* \rb “Because of my righteousness|בְּצִדְקָתִי֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb has brought me in|הֱבִיאַ֣נִי\rb* \rb to possess|לָרֶ֖שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb land.”|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb Rather, the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb is driving out|וּבְרִשְׁעַת֙\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֣ם\rb* \rb before you|מִפָּנֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb because of their wickedness.|מוֹרִישָׁ֥ם\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb It is not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb because of your righteousness|בְצִדְקָתְךָ֗\rb* \rb or uprightness|וּבְיֹ֙שֶׁר֙\rb* \rb of heart|לְבָ֣בְךָ֔\rb* \rb that you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb are going in|בָ֖א\rb* \rb to possess|לָרֶ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb their land,|אַרְצָ֑ם\rb* \rb but it is because|כִּ֞י\rb* \rb of their wickedness|בְּרִשְׁעַ֣ת׀\rb* \rb that the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb is driving out|מוֹרִישָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֣ם\rb* \rb before you,|מִפָּנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb to|וּלְמַ֜עַן\rb* \rb keep|הָקִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the promise|הַדָּבָ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb He|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb swore|נִשְׁבַּ֤ע\rb* \rb to your fathers,|לַאֲבֹתֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb to Abraham,|לְאַבְרָהָ֥ם\rb* \rb Isaac,|לְיִצְחָ֖ק\rb* \rb and Jacob.|וּֽלְיַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb* \v 6 \rb Understand, then,|וְיָדַעְתָּ֗\rb* \rb that|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb it is not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb because of your righteousness|בְצִדְקָֽתְךָ֙\rb* \rb that the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱ֠לֹהֶיךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֨ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֜\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb good|הַטּוֹבָ֛ה\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֧רֶץ\rb* \rb to possess,|לְרִשְׁתָּ֑הּ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you|אָֽתָּה׃\rb* \rb are a stiff-necked|קְשֵׁה־\rb*\rb |עֹ֖רֶף\rb* \rb people.|עַם־\rb*
\s1 The Golden Calf
\r \ref Exodus 32:1–35|EXO 32:1-35\ref*; \ref Acts 7:39–43|ACT 7:39-43\ref*)
\p \v 7 \rb Remember this,|זְכֹר֙\rb* \rb and never|אַל־\rb* \rb forget|תִּשְׁכַּ֔ח\rb*\rb |אֵ֧ת\rb* \rb how|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you provoked|הִקְצַ֛פְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb in the wilderness.|בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb* \rb From|לְמִן־\rb* \rb the day|הַיּ֞וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you left|יָצָ֣אתָ׀\rb* \rb the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb you reached|בֹּֽאֲכֶם֙\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb place,|הַמָּק֣וֹם\rb* \rb you have been|הֱיִיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb rebelling|מַמְרִ֥ים\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb At Horeb|וּבְחֹרֵ֥ב\rb*\f + \fr 9:8 \ft That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai\f* \rb you provoked|הִקְצַפְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and He|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb was angry enough|וַיִּתְאַנַּ֧ף\rb* \rb to destroy|לְהַשְׁמִ֥יד\rb* \rb you.|אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 9 \rb When I went up|בַּעֲלֹתִ֣י\rb* \rb on the mountain|הָהָ֗רָה\rb* \rb to receive|לָקַ֜חַת\rb* \rb the tablets|לוּחֹ֤ת\rb* \rb of stone,|הָֽאֲבָנִים֙\rb* \rb the tablets|לוּחֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of the covenant|הַבְּרִ֔ית\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb made|כָּרַ֥ת\rb* \rb with you,|עִמָּכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb I stayed|וָאֵשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb on the mountain|בָּהָ֗ר\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb days|יוֹם֙\rb* \rb and forty|וְאַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb nights.|לַ֔יְלָה\rb* \rb I ate|אָכַ֔לְתִּי\rb* \rb no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֚חֶם\rb* \rb and drank|שָׁתִֽיתִי׃\rb* \rb no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb water.|וּמַ֖יִם\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֗י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gave me|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵי֙\rb* \rb stone|הָֽאֲבָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb tablets,|לוּחֹ֣ת\rb* \rb inscribed|כְּתֻבִ֖ים\rb* \rb by the finger|בְּאֶצְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb with the exact|כְּֽכָל־\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֡ים\rb*\rb |וַעֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb spoke|דִּבֶּר֩\rb* \rb to you|עִמָּכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb out of|מִתּ֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the fire|הָאֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb on the mountain|בָּהָ֛ר\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb of the assembly.|הַקָּהָֽל׃\rb* \v 11 \rb And|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb at the end|מִקֵּץ֙\rb* \rb of forty|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb days|י֔וֹם\rb* \rb and forty|וְאַרְבָּעִ֖ים\rb* \rb nights,|לָ֑יְלָה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֗י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gave me|נָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵ֛י\rb* \rb stone|הָאֲבָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb tablets,|לֻחֹ֥ת\rb* \rb the tablets|לֻח֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the covenant.|הַבְּרִֽית׃\rb* \v 12 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb “Get up|ק֣וּם\rb* \rb and go down|רֵ֤ד\rb* \rb from here|מִזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb at once,|מַהֵר֙\rb* \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb your people,|עַמְּךָ֔\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you brought|הוֹצֵ֖אתָ\rb* \rb out of Egypt,|מִמִּצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb have corrupted themselves.|שִׁחֵ֣ת\rb* \rb How quickly|מַהֵ֗ר\rb* \rb they have turned aside|סָ֣רוּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the way|הַדֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I commanded them!|צִוִּיתִ֔ם\rb* \rb They have made|עָשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb for themselves|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb a molten image.”|מַסֵּכָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb also said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֣י\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “I have seen|רָאִ֙יתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb people,|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb and they|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb are indeed|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb a stiff-necked|קְשֵׁה־\rb*\rb |עֹ֖רֶף\rb* \rb people.|עַם־\rb* \v 14 \rb Leave Me alone,|הֶ֤רֶף\rb* \rb so that I may destroy them|וְאַשְׁמִידֵ֔ם\rb* \rb and blot out|וְאֶמְחֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their name|שְׁמָ֔ם\rb* \rb from|מִמֶּ֙נִּי֙\rb* \rb under|מִתַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb heaven.|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb Then I will make|וְאֶֽעֱשֶׂה֙\rb*\rb |אֽוֹתְךָ֔\rb* \rb you into a nation|לְגוֹי־\rb* \rb mightier|עָצ֥וּם\rb* \rb and greater|וָרָ֖ב\rb* \rb than they are.”|מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb So I went back|וָאֵ֗פֶן\rb* \rb down|וָֽאֵרֵד֙\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the mountain|הָהָ֔ר\rb* \rb while it|וְהָהָ֖ר\rb* \rb was blazing|בֹּעֵ֣ר\rb* \rb with fire,|בָּאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb with the two|וּשְׁנֵי֙\rb* \rb tablets|לֻחֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of the covenant|הַבְּרִ֔ית\rb* \rb in|עַ֖ל\rb*\rb |שְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb my hands.|יָדָֽי׃\rb* \v 16 \rb And I saw|וָאֵ֗רֶא\rb* \rb how|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb you had sinned|חֲטָאתֶם֙\rb* \rb against the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God;|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb you had made|עֲשִׂיתֶ֣ם\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb a molten|מַסֵּכָ֑ה\rb* \rb calf.|עֵ֖גֶל\rb* \rb You had turned aside|סַרְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb quickly|מַהֵ֔ר\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the way|הַדֶּ֕רֶךְ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb had commanded you.|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \v 17 \rb So I took|וָאֶתְפֹּשׂ֙\rb* \rb the two|בִּשְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb tablets|הַלֻּחֹ֔ת\rb* \rb and threw them|וָֽאַשְׁלִכֵ֔ם\rb* \rb out of|מֵעַ֖ל\rb*\rb |שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb my hands,|יָדָ֑י\rb* \rb shattering them|וָאֲשַׁבְּרֵ֖ם\rb* \rb before your eyes.|לְעֵינֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Then I fell down|וָֽאֶתְנַפַּל֩\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb for forty|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb days|יוֹם֙\rb* \rb and forty|וְאַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb nights,|לַ֔יְלָה\rb* \rb as I had done the first time.|כָּרִאשֹׁנָ֗ה\rb* \rb I did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb eat|אָכַ֔לְתִּי\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֚חֶם\rb* \rb or drink|שָׁתִ֑יתִי\rb* \rb water|וּמַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb because of|עַ֤ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the sin|חַטַּאתְכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you had committed|חֲטָאתֶ֔ם\rb* \rb in doing|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb what was evil|הָרַ֛ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and provoking Him to anger.|לְהַכְעִיסֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 19 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I was afraid|יָגֹ֗רְתִּי\rb*\f + \fr 9:19 \ft LXX \fqa And I am greatly terrified\ft ; cited in \ref Hebrews 12:21|HEB 12:21\ref*\f* \rb |מִפְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb of the anger|הָאַף֙\rb* \rb and wrath|וְהַ֣חֵמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb had directed|קָצַ֧ף\rb* \rb against you,|עֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb enough to destroy you.|לְהַשְׁמִ֣יד\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb But the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb listened|וַיִּשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb this|הַהִֽוא׃\rb* \rb time|בַּפַּ֥עַם\rb* \rb as well.|גַּ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb was angry|הִתְאַנַּ֧ף\rb* \rb enough|מְאֹ֖ד\rb* \rb with Aaron|וּֽבְאַהֲרֹ֗ן\rb* \rb to destroy him,|לְהַשְׁמִיד֑וֹ\rb* \rb but at that|הַהִֽוא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֥ת\rb* \rb I also|גַּם־\rb* \rb prayed|וָֽאֶתְפַּלֵּ֛ל\rb* \rb for|בְּעַ֥ד\rb* \rb Aaron.|אַהֲרֹ֖ן\rb* \v 21 \rb And|וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb I took|לָקַחְתִּי֮\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb sinful thing,|חַטַּאתְכֶ֞ם\rb* \rb the calf|הָעֵ֗גֶל\rb* \rb you had made,|עֲשִׂיתֶ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and burned|וָאֶשְׂרֹ֣ף\rb* \rb it|אֹת֣וֹ׀\rb* \rb in the fire.|בָּאֵשׁ֒\rb* \rb Then I crushed it|וָאֶכֹּ֨ת\rb*\rb |אֹת֤וֹ\rb* \rb and ground|טָחוֹן֙\rb* \rb it to|עַ֥ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb powder|דַּ֖ק\rb* \rb as fine as dust,|לְעָפָ֑ר\rb* \rb and I cast|וָֽאַשְׁלִךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it|עֲפָר֔וֹ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the stream|הַנַּ֖חַל\rb* \rb that came down|הַיֹּרֵ֥ד\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the mountain.|הָהָֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb You continued to provoke|מַקְצִפִ֥ים\rb*\rb |הֱיִיתֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb at Taberah,|וּבְתַבְעֵרָה֙\rb*\f + \fr 9:22 \fqa Taberah \ft means \fqa burning\ft ; see \ref Numbers 11:3|NUM 11:3\ref*.\f* \rb at Massah,|וּבְמַסָּ֔ה\rb*\f + \fr 9:22 \fqa Massah \ft means \fqa testing\ft ; see \ref Exodus 17:7|EXO 17:7\ref*.\f*\rb |וּבְקִבְרֹ֖ת\rb* \rb and at Kibroth-hattaavah.|הַֽתַּאֲוָ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 9:22 \fqa Kibroth-hattaavah \ft means \fqa graves of craving\ft ; see \ref Numbers 11:34|NUM 11:34\ref*.\f* \v 23 \rb And when the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb sent you out|וּבִשְׁלֹ֨חַ\rb*\rb |מִקָּדֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb from Kadesh-barnea,|בַּרְנֵ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb He said,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “Go up|עֲלוּ֙\rb* \rb and possess|וּרְשׁ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have given|נָתַ֖תִּי\rb* \rb you.”|לָכֶ֑ם\rb*
\p \rb But you rebelled|וַתַּמְר֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb against the command|פִּ֤י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹ֣הֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb You neither|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb believed|הֶֽאֱמַנְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb Him|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb nor|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb obeyed|שְׁמַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb Him.|בְּקֹלֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 24 \rb You have been|הֱיִיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb rebelling|מַמְרִ֥ים\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb since the day|מִיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb I came to know you.|דַּעְתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 25 \rb So I fell down|וָֽאֶתְנַפַּ֞ל\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb for forty|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb days|הַיּ֛וֹם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb nights,|הַלַּ֖יְלָה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |הִתְנַפָּ֑לְתִּי\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb had said|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb He would destroy|לְהַשְׁמִ֥יד\rb* \rb you.|אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb And I prayed|וָאֶתְפַּלֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb and said,|וָאֹמַר֒\rb* \rb “O Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD,|יְהוִ֗ה\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb destroy|תַּשְׁחֵ֤ת\rb* \rb Your people,|עַמְּךָ֙\rb* \rb Your inheritance,|וְנַחֲלָ֣תְךָ֔\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb You redeemed|פָּדִ֖יתָ\rb* \rb through Your greatness|בְּגָדְלֶ֑ךָ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb and brought out|הוֹצֵ֥אתָ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb with a mighty|חֲזָקָֽה׃\rb* \rb hand.|בְּיָ֥ד\rb* \v 27 \rb Remember|זְכֹר֙\rb* \rb Your servants|לַעֲבָדֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb Abraham,|לְאַבְרָהָ֥ם\rb* \rb Isaac,|לְיִצְחָ֖ק\rb* \rb and Jacob.|וּֽלְיַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb* \rb Overlook|אַל־\rb*\rb |תֵּ֗פֶן\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the stubbornness|קְשִׁי֙\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb and the wickedness|רִשְׁע֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb of their sin.|חַטָּאתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 28 \rb Otherwise,|פֶּן־\rb* \rb those in the land|הָאָרֶץ֮\rb* \rb from which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb You brought us out|הוֹצֵאתָ֣נוּ\rb*\rb |מִשָּׁם֒\rb* \rb will say,|יֹאמְר֗וּ\rb* \rb ‘Because the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb was not|מִבְּלִי֙\rb* \rb able|יְכֹ֣לֶת\rb* \rb to bring them|לַהֲבִיאָ֕ם\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He had promised|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb them,|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and because He hated|וּמִשִּׂנְאָת֣וֹ\rb* \rb them,|אוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb He has brought them out|הוֹצִיאָ֖ם\rb* \rb to kill them|לַהֲמִתָ֥ם\rb* \rb in the wilderness.’|בַּמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb* \v 29 \rb But they|וְהֵ֥ם\rb* \rb are Your people,|עַמְּךָ֖\rb* \rb Your inheritance,|וְנַחֲלָתֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb You brought out|הוֹצֵ֙אתָ֙\rb* \rb by Your great|הַגָּדֹ֔ל\rb* \rb power|בְּכֹחֲךָ֣\rb* \rb and outstretched|הַנְּטוּיָֽה׃פ\rb* \rb arm.”|וּבִֽזְרֹעֲךָ֖\rb*
\c 10
\s1 New Stone Tablets
\r \ref Exodus 34:1–9|EXO 34:1-9\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb At that|הַהִ֜וא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֨ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֧ר\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb “Chisel out|פְּסָל־\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵֽי־\rb* \rb stone|אֲבָנִים֙\rb* \rb tablets|לֻוחֹ֤ת\rb* \rb like the originals,|כָּרִ֣אשֹׁנִ֔ים\rb* \rb come up|וַעֲלֵ֥ה\rb* \rb to Me|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb on the mountain,|הָהָ֑רָה\rb* \rb and make|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb* \rb an ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of wood.|עֵֽץ׃\rb* \v 2 \rb And I will write|וְאֶכְתֹּב֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the tablets|הַלֻּחֹ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the words|הַדְּבָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb were|הָי֛וּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the first|הָרִאשֹׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb tablets,|הַלֻּחֹ֥ת\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you broke;|שִׁבַּ֑רְתָּ\rb* \rb and you are to place them|וְשַׂמְתָּ֖ם\rb* \rb in the ark.”|בָּאָרֽוֹן׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb So I made|וָאַ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb an ark|אֲרוֹן֙\rb* \rb of acacia|שִׁטִּ֔ים\rb* \rb wood,|עֲצֵ֣י\rb* \rb chiseled out|וָאֶפְסֹ֛ל\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵי־\rb* \rb stone|אֲבָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb tablets|לֻחֹ֥ת\rb* \rb like the originals,|כָּרִאשֹׁנִ֑ים\rb* \rb and went up|וָאַ֣עַל\rb* \rb the mountain|הָהָ֔רָה\rb* \rb with the two|וּשְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb tablets|הַלֻּחֹ֖ת\rb* \rb in my hands.|בְּיָדִֽי׃\rb* \v 4 \rb And the LORD wrote|וַיִּכְתֹּ֨ב\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the tablets|הַלֻּחֹ֜ת\rb* \rb what had been written|כַּמִּכְתָּ֣ב\rb* \rb previously,|הָרִאשׁ֗וֹן\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb the Ten|עֲשֶׂ֣רֶת\rb* \rb Commandments|הַדְּבָרִ֔ים\rb*\f + \fr 10:4 \ft Hebrew \fqa the Ten Words\f* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb had spoken|דִּבֶּר֩\rb* \rb to|אֲלֵיכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb you on the mountain|בָּהָ֛ר\rb* \rb out of|מִתּ֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the fire|הָאֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of the assembly.|הַקָּהָ֑ל\rb* \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb gave them|וַיִּתְּנֵ֥ם\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלָֽי׃\rb* \v 5 \rb and I went back|וָאֵ֗פֶן\rb* \rb down|וָֽאֵרֵד֙\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the mountain|הָהָ֔ר\rb* \rb and placed|וָֽאָשִׂם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the tablets|הַלֻּחֹ֔ת\rb* \rb in the ark|בָּאָר֖וֹן\rb* \rb I had made,|עָשִׂ֑יתִי\rb* \rb as|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb had commanded me;|צִוַּ֖נִי\rb* \rb and there|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb they have remained.|וַיִּ֣הְיוּ\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb The Israelites|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb traveled|נָֽסְע֛וּ\rb* \rb from|מִבְּאֵרֹ֥ת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb Beeroth Bene-jaakan|יַעֲקָ֖ן\rb*\f + \fr 10:6 \ft Or \fqa from the wells of the Bene-jaakan\f* \rb to Moserah,|מוֹסֵרָ֑ה\rb* \rb where|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹן֙\rb* \rb died|מֵ֤ת\rb* \rb and was buried,|וַיִּקָּבֵ֣ר\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb and Eleazar|אֶלְעָזָ֥ר\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb succeeded him as priest.|וַיְכַהֵ֛ן\rb*\rb |תַּחְתָּֽיו׃\rb* \v 7 \rb From|וּמִן־\rb* \rb there|מִשָּׁ֥ם\rb* \rb they traveled|נָסְע֖וּ\rb* \rb to Gudgodah,|הַגֻּדְגֹּ֑דָה\rb* \rb and from Gudgodah|הַגֻּדְגֹּ֣דָה\rb* \rb to Jotbathah,|יָטְבָ֔תָה\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb with streams|נַ֥חֲלֵי\rb* \rb of water.|מָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb At that|הַהִ֗וא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb set apart|הִבְדִּ֤יל\rb* \rb the tribe|שֵׁ֣בֶט\rb* \rb of Levi|הַלֵּוִ֔י\rb* \rb to carry|לָשֵׂ֖את\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb to stand|לַעֲמֹד֩\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb to serve Him,|לְשָֽׁרְתוֹ֙\rb* \rb and to pronounce blessings|וּלְבָרֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb in His name,|בִּשְׁמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb as they do to this day.|עַ֖ד\rb*\rb |הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \v 9 \rb That is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֞ן\rb* \rb Levi|לְלֵוִ֛י\rb* \rb has|הָיָ֧ה\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb portion|חֵ֥לֶק\rb* \rb or inheritance|וְנַחֲלָ֖ה\rb* \rb among|עִם־\rb* \rb his brothers;|אֶחָ֑יו\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb is his inheritance,|נַחֲלָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb promised|דִּבֶּ֛ר\rb* \rb him.|לֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb I|וְאָנֹכִ֞י\rb* \rb stayed|עָמַ֣דְתִּי\rb* \rb on the mountain|בָהָ֗ר\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb days|כַּיָּמִים֙\rb* \rb and forty|וְאַרְבָּעִ֖ים\rb* \rb nights,|לָ֑יְלָה\rb* \rb like the first|הָרִ֣אשֹׁנִ֔ים\rb* \rb time,|י֔וֹם\rb* \rb and that|הַהִ֔וא\rb* \rb time|בַּפַּ֣עַם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb again|גַּ֚ם\rb* \rb listened|וַיִּשְׁמַ֨ע\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb and|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb agreed|אָבָ֥ה\rb* \rb not|לֹא־\rb* \rb to destroy you.|הַשְׁחִיתֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb “Get up.|ק֛וּם\rb* \rb Continue|לֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb your journey|לְמַסַּ֖ע\rb* \rb ahead of|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb that they may enter|וְיָבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb and possess|וְיִֽרְשׁ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I swore|נִשְׁבַּ֥עְתִּי\rb* \rb to|לָהֶֽם׃פ\rb* \rb their fathers|לַאֲבֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb to give them.”|לָתֵ֥ת\rb*
\s1 A Call to Obedience
\r \ref Joshua 24:14–28|JOS 24:14-28\ref*)
\p \v 12 \rb And now,|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb O Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb what|מָ֚ה\rb* \rb does the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb ask|שֹׁאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb of you|מֵעִמָּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb but|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb to fear|לְ֠יִרְאָה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb by walking|לָלֶ֤כֶת\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb His ways,|דְּרָכָיו֙\rb* \rb to love Him,|וּלְאַהֲבָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb to serve|וְלַֽעֲבֹד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָבְךָ֖\rb* \rb and with all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb your soul,|נַפְשֶֽׁךָ׃\rb* \v 13 \rb and to keep|לִשְׁמֹ֞ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the commandments|מִצְוֺ֤ת\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb statutes|חֻקֹּתָ֔יו\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb am giving you|מְצַוְּךָ֖\rb* \rb this day|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb for your own good?|לְט֖וֹב\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Behold,|הֵ֚ן\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb belong the heavens,|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb even the highest|וּשְׁמֵ֣י\rb* \rb heavens,|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and the earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb and everything|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in it.|בָּֽהּ׃\rb* \v 15 \rb Yet|רַ֧ק\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has set His affection|חָשַׁ֥ק\rb* \rb on your fathers|בַּאֲבֹתֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb and loved|לְאַהֲבָ֣ה\rb* \rb them.|אוֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb And He has chosen you,|וַיִּבְחַ֞ר\rb* \rb their descendants|בְּזַרְעָ֣ם\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb them,|בָּכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb above all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the peoples,|הָעַמִּ֖ים\rb* \rb even to this day.|כַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּה׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb Circumcise|וּמַלְתֶּ֕ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb*\rb |עָרְלַ֣ת\rb* \rb your hearts, therefore,|לְבַבְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and stiffen|תַקְשׁ֖וּ\rb* \rb your necks|וְעָ֨רְפְּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb more.|עֽוֹד׃\rb* \v 17 \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |ה֚וּא\rb* \rb is God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of gods|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb and Lord|וַאֲדֹנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of lords,|הָאֲדֹנִ֑ים\rb* \rb the great,|הַגָּדֹ֤ל\rb* \rb mighty,|הַגִּבֹּר֙\rb* \rb and awesome|וְהַנּוֹרָ֔א\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb God,|הָאֵ֨ל\rb* \rb showing no|לֹא־\rb* \rb partiality|יִשָּׂ֣א\rb*\rb |פָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and accepting|יִקַּ֖ח\rb* \rb no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb bribe.|שֹֽׁחַד׃\rb* \v 18 \rb He executes|עֹשֶׂ֛ה\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפַּ֥ט\rb* \rb for the fatherless|יָת֖וֹם\rb* \rb and widow,|וְאַלְמָנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and He loves|וְאֹהֵ֣ב\rb* \rb the foreigner,|גֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb giving|לָ֥תֶת\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb food|לֶ֥חֶם\rb* \rb and clothing.|וְשִׂמְלָֽה׃\rb* \v 19 \rb So you also must love|וַאֲהַבְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the foreigner,|הַגֵּ֑ר\rb* \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you yourselves were|הֱיִיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb foreigners|גֵרִ֥ים\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb You are to fear|תִּירָ֖א\rb*\rb |אֹת֣וֹ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb and serve|תַעֲבֹ֑ד\rb* \rb Him.|וּב֣וֹ\rb* \rb Hold fast to Him|תִדְבָּ֔ק\rb* \rb and take your oaths|תִּשָּׁבֵֽעַ׃\rb* \rb in His name.|וּבִשְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \v 21 \rb He|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb is your praise|תְהִלָּתְךָ֖\rb* \rb and He|וְה֣וּא\rb* \rb is your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has done|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb for you|אִתְּךָ֗\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb great|הַגְּדֹלֹ֤ת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and awesome wonders|הַנּֽוֹרָאֹת֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb your eyes|עֵינֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb have seen.|רָא֖וּ\rb* \v 22 \rb Your fathers|אֲבֹתֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb went down|יָרְד֥וּ\rb* \rb to Egypt,|מִצְרָ֑יְמָהּ\rb* \rb seventy|בְּשִׁבְעִ֣ים\rb* \rb in all,|נֶ֔פֶשׁ\rb* \rb and now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb has made|שָֽׂמְךָ֙\rb* \rb you as numerous|לָרֹֽב׃\rb* \rb as the stars|כְּכוֹכְבֵ֥י\rb* \rb in the sky.|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb*
\c 11
\s1 Obedience and Discipline
\r \ref Deuteronomy 4:1–14|DEU 4:1-14\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb You shall therefore love|וְאָ֣הַבְתָּ֔\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb and always|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb* \rb keep|וְשָׁמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb His charge,|מִשְׁמַרְתּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb His statutes,|וְחֻקֹּתָ֧יו\rb* \rb His ordinances,|וּמִשְׁפָּטָ֛יו\rb* \rb and His commandments.|וּמִצְוֺתָ֖יו\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb Know|וִֽידַעְתֶּם֮\rb* \rb this day|הַיּוֹם֒\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb it is not|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your children|בְּנֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb*\rb |לֹֽא־\rb* \rb have known|יָדְעוּ֙\rb* \rb and|וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb seen|רָא֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the discipline|מוּסַ֖ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God:|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His greatness,|גָּדְל֕וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His mighty|הַחֲזָקָ֔ה\rb* \rb hand,|יָדוֹ֙\rb* \rb and His outstretched|הַנְּטוּיָֽה׃\rb* \rb arm;|וּזְרֹע֖וֹ\rb* \v 3 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the signs|אֹֽתֹתָיו֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb and works|מַעֲשָׂ֔יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He did|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb in|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb to Pharaoh|לְפַרְעֹ֥ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb his land;|אַרְצֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 4 \rb what|וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He did|עָשָׂה֩\rb* \rb to the Egyptian|מִצְרַ֜יִם\rb* \rb army|לְחֵ֨יל\rb* \rb and horses|לְסוּסָ֣יו\rb* \rb and chariots|וּלְרִכְבּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb when|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb He made the waters|מֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the Red|סוּף֙\rb* \rb Sea|יַם־\rb*\f + \fr 11:4 \ft Or \fqa the Sea of Reeds\f* \rb engulf|הֵצִ֜יף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb them|פְּנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb as they pursued you,|בְּרָדְפָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and how He|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb destroyed them completely,|וַיְאַבְּדֵ֣ם\rb* \rb even to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this day;|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \v 5 \rb what|וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He did|עָשָׂ֛ה\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb you reached|בֹּאֲכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb place;|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \v 6 \rb and what|וַאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb He did|עָשָׂ֜ה\rb* \rb in the midst|בְּקֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb to Dathan|לְדָתָ֣ן\rb* \rb and Abiram,|וְלַאֲבִירָ֗ם\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Eliab|אֱלִיאָב֮\rb* \rb the Reubenite,|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |רְאוּבֵן֒\rb* \rb when|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb opened|פָּצְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb its mouth|פִּ֔יהָ\rb* \rb and swallowed them,|וַתִּבְלָעֵ֥ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb their households,|בָּתֵּיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb their tents,|אָהֳלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֤ת\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb living thing|הַיְקוּם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb that belonged to them.|בְּרַגְלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb For it is|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb your own eyes|עֵֽינֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb that have seen|הָֽרֹאֹ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb great|הַגָּדֹ֑ל\rb* \rb work|מַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has done.|עָשָֽׂה׃\rb*
\s1 God’s Great Blessings
\r \ref Joshua 1:1–9|JOS 1:1-9\ref*)
\p \v 8 \rb You shall therefore keep|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb commandment|הַמִּצְוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb am giving you today,|מְצַוְּךָ֖\rb*\rb |הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb you may have the strength|תֶּחֶזְק֗וּ\rb* \rb to go in|וּבָאתֶם֙\rb* \rb and possess|וִֽירִשְׁתֶּ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֛ם\rb* \rb are crossing|עֹבְרִ֥ים\rb* \rb the Jordan|שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb to possess,|לְרִשְׁתָּֽהּ׃\rb* \v 9 \rb and so that|וּלְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb you may live long|תַּאֲרִ֤יכוּ\rb*\rb |יָמִים֙\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|הָ֣אֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb swore|נִשְׁבַּ֨ע\rb* \rb to your fathers|לַאֲבֹתֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb to give|לָתֵ֥ת\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and their descendants,|וּלְזַרְעָ֑ם\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb flowing|זָבַ֥ת\rb* \rb with milk|חָלָ֖ב\rb* \rb and honey.|וּדְבָֽשׁ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb are entering|בָא־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb to possess|לְרִשְׁתָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb is not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb like the land|כְאֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb from which|הִ֔וא\rb* \rb you have come,|יְצָאתֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |מִשָּׁ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you sowed|תִּזְרַע֙\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your seed|זַרְעֲךָ֔\rb* \rb and irrigated|וְהִשְׁקִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb on foot,|בְרַגְלְךָ֖\rb* \rb like a vegetable|הַיָּרָֽק׃\rb* \rb garden.|כְּגַ֥ן\rb* \v 11 \rb But the land|וְהָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֜ם\rb* \rb are crossing|עֹבְרִ֥ים\rb* \rb the Jordan|שָׁ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb to possess|לְרִשְׁתָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb is a land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of mountains|הָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb and valleys|וּבְקָעֹ֑ת\rb* \rb that drinks in|תִּשְׁתֶּה־\rb*\rb |מָּֽיִם׃\rb* \rb the rain|לִמְטַ֥ר\rb* \rb from heaven.|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \v 12 \rb It is a land|אֶ֕רֶץ\rb* \rb for which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb cares;|דֹּרֵ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb the eyes|עֵינֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb are always|תָּמִ֗יד\rb* \rb on it,|בָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb from the beginning|מֵֽרֵשִׁית֙\rb* \rb to|וְעַ֖ד\rb* \rb the end|אַחֲרִ֥ית\rb*\rb |שָׁנָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb of the year.|הַשָּׁנָ֔ה\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb So|וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you carefully obey|שָׁמֹ֤עַ\rb*\rb |תִּשְׁמְעוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the commandments|מִצְוֺתַ֔י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb am giving you today,|מְצַוֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb to love|לְאַהֲבָ֞ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb and to serve Him|וּלְעָבְד֔וֹ\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבַבְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and with all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb your soul,|נַפְשְׁכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 14 \rb then I will provide|וְנָתַתִּ֧י\rb*\f + \fr 11:14 \ft Hebrew; SP, LXX, and Vulgate \fqa He will provide\ft ; also in verse 15\f* \rb rain|מְטַֽר־\rb* \rb for your land|אַרְצְכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb in season,|בְּעִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb the autumn and spring rains,|יוֹרֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |וּמַלְק֑וֹשׁ\rb* \rb that you may gather|וְאָסַפְתָּ֣\rb* \rb your grain,|דְגָנֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb new wine,|וְתִֽירֹשְׁךָ֖\rb* \rb and oil.|וְיִצְהָרֶֽךָ׃\rb* \v 15 \rb And I will provide|וְנָתַתִּ֛י\rb* \rb grass|עֵ֥שֶׂב\rb* \rb in the fields|בְּשָׂדְךָ֖\rb* \rb for your livestock,|לִבְהֶמְתֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb and you will eat|וְאָכַלְתָּ֖\rb* \rb and be satisfied.|וְשָׂבָֽעְתָּ׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb But be careful|הִשָּֽׁמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb that you are not|פֶּ֥ן\rb* \rb enticed|יִפְתֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |לְבַבְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb to turn aside|וְסַרְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb to worship|וַעֲבַדְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb and bow down|וְהִשְׁתַּחֲוִיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gods,|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \v 17 \rb or the anger|אַף־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb will be kindled|וְחָרָ֨ה\rb* \rb against you.|בָּכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb He will shut|וְעָצַ֤ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb so that there will be|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb rain,|מָטָ֔ר\rb* \rb nor will|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb the land|וְהָ֣אֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb yield|תִתֵּ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its produce,|יְבוּלָ֑הּ\rb* \rb and you will soon perish|וַאֲבַדְתֶּ֣ם\rb*\rb |מְהֵרָ֗ה\rb* \rb from|מֵעַל֙\rb* \rb the good|הַטֹּבָ֔ה\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you.|לָכֶֽם׃\rb*
\s1 Remember God’s Words
\p \v 18 \rb Fix|וְשַׂמְתֶּם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|אֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb words of mine|דְּבָרַ֣י\rb* \rb in your|עַל־\rb* \rb hearts|לְבַבְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and|וְעַֽל־\rb* \rb minds;|נַפְשְׁכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb tie|וּקְשַׁרְתֶּ֨ם\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֤ם\rb* \rb as reminders|לְאוֹת֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb your hands|יֶדְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and bind them|וְהָי֥וּ\rb*\rb |לְטוֹטָפֹ֖ת\rb* \rb on your foreheads.|בֵּ֥ין\rb*\rb |עֵינֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 19 \rb Teach|וְלִמַּדְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to your children,|בְּנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb speaking|לְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb about them|בָּ֑ם\rb* \rb when you sit|בְּשִׁבְתְּךָ֤\rb* \rb at home|בְּבֵיתֶ֙ךָ֙\rb* \rb and when you walk|וּבְלֶכְתְּךָ֣\rb* \rb along the road,|בַדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb when you lie down|וּֽבְשָׁכְבְּךָ֖\rb* \rb and when you get up.|וּבְקוּמֶֽךָ׃\rb* \v 20 \rb Write them|וּכְתַבְתָּ֛ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the doorposts|מְזוּז֥וֹת\rb* \rb of your houses|בֵּיתֶ֖ךָ\rb* \rb and on your gates,|וּבִשְׁעָרֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 21 \rb so that|לְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb as long as|כִּימֵ֥י\rb* \rb the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb are above|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth,|הָאָֽרֶץ׃ס\rb* \rb your days|יְמֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb and those|וִימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of your children|בְנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb may be multiplied|יִרְבּ֤וּ\rb* \rb in|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the land|הָֽאֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb swore|נִשְׁבַּ֧ע\rb* \rb to give|לָתֵ֣ת\rb* \rb your fathers.|לַאֲבֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you carefully keep|שָׁמֹ֨ר\rb*\rb |תִּשְׁמְר֜וּן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הַזֹּ֗את\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb commandments|הַמִּצְוָ֣ה\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb am giving|מְצַוֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb you to follow—|לַעֲשֹׂתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb to love|לְאַהֲבָ֞ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb to walk|לָלֶ֥כֶת\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb His ways,|דְּרָכָ֖יו\rb* \rb and to hold fast|וּלְדָבְקָה־\rb* \rb to Him—|בֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 23 \rb then the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will drive out|וְהוֹרִ֧ישׁ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֥ם\rb* \rb before you,|מִלִּפְנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and you will dispossess|וִֽירִשְׁתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb nations|גּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb greater|גְּדֹלִ֥ים\rb* \rb and stronger|וַעֲצֻמִ֖ים\rb* \rb than you.|מִכֶּֽם׃\rb* \v 24 \rb Every|כָּל־\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֗וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the sole|כַּֽף־\rb* \rb of your foot|רַגְלְכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb treads|תִּדְרֹ֧ךְ\rb* \rb will be yours.|יִהְיֶ֑ה\rb* \rb Your territory|גְּבֻלְכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb will extend|יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּ֨ר\rb* \rb to Lebanon,|וְהַלְּבָנ֜וֹן\rb* \rb and from|מִן־\rb* \rb the Euphrates|פְּרָ֗ת\rb* \rb River|הַנָּהָ֣ר\rb*\rb |נְהַר־\rb* \rb to|וְעַד֙\rb* \rb the Western|הָֽאַחֲר֔וֹן\rb* \rb Sea.|הַיָּ֣ם\rb*\f + \fr 11:24 \ft That is, the Mediterranean Sea, also called the Great Sea\f* \v 25 \rb No|לֹא־\rb* \rb man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb will be able to stand|יִתְיַצֵּ֥ב\rb* \rb against you;|בִּפְנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb will put|יִתֵּ֣ן׀\rb* \rb the fear|פַּחְדְּכֶ֨ם\rb* \rb and dread|וּמֽוֹרַאֲכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb of you|עַל־\rb* \rb upon|פְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the land,|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb wherever|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you set foot,|תִּדְרְכוּ־\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb He has promised|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb you.|לָכֶֽם׃ס\rb*
\s1 A Blessing and a Curse
\p \v 26 \rb See,|רְאֵ֗ה\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb am setting|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb before you|לִפְנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb a blessing|בְּרָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb and a curse—|וּקְלָלָֽה׃\rb*  \v 27 \rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb a blessing|הַבְּרָכָ֑ה\rb* \rb if|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you obey|תִּשְׁמְע֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the commandments|מִצְוֺת֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb am giving you today,|מְצַוֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb* \v 28 \rb but a curse|וְהַקְּלָלָ֗ה\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֤א\rb* \rb you disobey|תִשְׁמְעוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the commandments|מִצְוֺת֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and turn aside|וְסַרְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the path|הַדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb command|מְצַוֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb by following|לָלֶ֗כֶת\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֛י\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb gods,|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \rb which you have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb known.|יְדַעְתֶּֽם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb When|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb brings|יְבִֽיאֲךָ֙\rb* \rb you into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֕רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb are entering|בָא־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb to possess,|לְרִשְׁתָּ֑הּ\rb* \rb you are to proclaim|וְנָתַתָּ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the blessing|הַבְּרָכָה֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Mount|הַ֣ר\rb* \rb Gerizim|גְּרִזִ֔ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the curse|הַקְּלָלָ֖ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Mount|הַ֥ר\rb* \rb Ebal.|עֵיבָֽל׃\rb* \v 30 \rb Are not|הֲלֹא־\rb* \rb these mountains|הֵ֜מָּה\rb* \rb across|בְּעֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb the Jordan,|הַיַּרְדֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb west|מְב֣וֹא\rb* \rb of the road|דֶּ֚רֶךְ\rb* \rb toward|אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb the sunset,|הַשֶּׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb of the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֔י\rb* \rb who live|הַיֹּשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb in the Arabah|בָּעֲרָבָ֑ה\rb* \rb opposite|מ֚וּל\rb* \rb Gilgal|הַגִּלְגָּ֔ל\rb* \rb near|אֵ֖צֶל\rb* \rb the Oak|אֵלוֹנֵ֥י\rb*\f + \fr 11:30 \ft SP, LXX, and Syriac (see \ref Genesis 12:6|GEN 12:6\ref*); Hebrew \fqa Oaks \ft or \fqa Terebinths \ft or \fqa Great Trees\f* \rb of Moreh?|מֹרֶֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb are about to cross|עֹבְרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb to enter|לָבֹא֙\rb* \rb and possess|לָרֶ֣שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb you.|לָכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb When you take possession|וִֽירִשְׁתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb of it|אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb and settle|וִֽישַׁבְתֶּם־\rb* \rb in it,|בָּֽהּ׃\rb* \v 32 \rb be careful|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb to follow|לַעֲשׂ֔וֹת\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the statutes|הַֽחֻקִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and ordinances|הַמִּשְׁפָּטִ֑ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb am setting|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb before you|לִפְנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb today.|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*
\c 12
\s1 One Place for Worship
\p \v 1 \rb These are|אֵ֠לֶּה\rb* \rb the statutes|הַֽחֻקִּ֣ים\rb* \rb and ordinances|וְהַמִּשְׁפָּטִים֮\rb* \rb you must be careful|תִּשְׁמְר֣וּן\rb* \rb to follow|לַעֲשׂוֹת֒\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the days|הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb live|חַיִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |הָאֲדָמָֽה׃\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֕רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֧י\rb* \rb of your fathers,|אֲבֹתֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb has given|נָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb to possess.|לְרִשְׁתָּ֑הּ\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb Destroy completely|אַבֵּ֣ד\rb*\rb |תְּ֠אַבְּדוּן\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the places|הַמְּקֹמ֞וֹת\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֛ם\rb* \rb are dispossessing|יֹרְשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb have served|עָֽבְדוּ־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb their gods—|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb atop|עַל־\rb* \rb the high|הָֽרָמִים֙\rb* \rb mountains,|הֶהָרִ֤ים\rb* \rb on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the hills,|הַגְּבָע֔וֹת\rb* \rb and under|וְתַ֖חַת\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb green|רַעֲנָן׃\rb* \rb tree.|עֵ֥ץ\rb* \v 3 \rb Tear down|וְנִתַּצְתֶּ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their altars,|מִזְבּחֹתָ֗ם\rb* \rb smash|וְשִׁבַּרְתֶּם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their sacred pillars,|מַצֵּ֣בֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb burn up|תִּשְׂרְפ֣וּן\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb their Asherah poles,|וַאֲשֵֽׁרֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb cut down|תְּגַדֵּע֑וּן\rb* \rb the idols|וּפְסִילֵ֥י\rb* \rb of their gods,|אֱלֹֽהֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and wipe out|וְאִבַּדְתֶּ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their names|שְׁמָ֔ם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb every place.|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb*\rb |הַהֽוּא׃\rb* \v 4 \rb You shall not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb worship|תַעֲשׂ֣וּן\rb* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb in this way.|כֵּ֔ן\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Instead,|כִּ֠י\rb*\rb |אִֽם־\rb* \rb you must seek|תִדְרְשׁ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֞וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb will choose|יִבְחַ֨ר\rb* \rb from among all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb your tribes|שִׁבְטֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to establish|לָשׂ֥וּם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb as a dwelling|לְשִׁכְנ֥וֹ\rb* \rb for His Name,|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |שָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb and there|שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb* \rb you must go.|וּבָ֥אתָ\rb* \v 6 \rb To that place|שָׁ֗מָּה\rb* \rb you are to bring|וַהֲבֵאתֶ֣ם\rb* \rb your burnt offerings|עֹלֹֽתֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb and sacrifices,|וְזִבְחֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb your tithes|מַעְשְׂרֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and heave offerings,|תְּרוּמַ֣ת\rb*\rb |יֶדְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb your vow offerings|וְנִדְרֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb and freewill offerings,|וְנִדְבֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb as well as the firstborn|וּבְכֹרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of your herds|בְּקַרְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and flocks.|וְצֹאנְכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 7 \rb There,|שָׁ֗ם\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb you and your households|וּבָתֵּיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb shall eat|וַאֲכַלְתֶּם־\rb* \rb and rejoice|וּשְׂמַחְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb in all|בְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb you do,|מִשְׁלַ֣ח\rb*\rb |יֶדְכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb because|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb has blessed you.|בֵּֽרַכְךָ֖\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb You are not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb to do|תַעֲשׂ֔וּן\rb* \rb as|כְּ֠כֹל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb we|אֲנַ֧חְנוּ\rb* \rb are doing|עֹשִׂ֛ים\rb* \rb here|פֹּ֖ה\rb* \rb today,|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb where everyone|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb does what|כָּל־\rb* \rb seems right|הַיָּשָׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in his own eyes.|בְּעֵינָֽיו׃\rb* \v 9 \rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you have not|לֹא־\rb* \rb yet|עַד־\rb* \rb come|בָּאתֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |עָ֑תָּה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the resting place|הַמְּנוּחָה֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and the inheritance|הַֽנַּחֲלָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you.|לָֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb When you cross|וַעֲבַרְתֶּם֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּן֒\rb* \rb and live|וִֽישַׁבְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb is giving you as an inheritance,|מַנְחִ֣יל\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and He gives you rest|וְהֵנִ֨יחַ\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the enemies|אֹיְבֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb around you|מִסָּבִ֖יב\rb* \rb and you dwell|וִֽישַׁבְתֶּם־\rb* \rb securely,|בֶּֽטַח׃\rb* \v 11 \rb |וְהָיָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |הַמָּק֗וֹם\rb* \rb then the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb will choose|יִבְחַר֩\rb* \rb a dwelling|לְשַׁכֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb for His Name.|שְׁמוֹ֙\rb* \rb And there|שָׁ֔ם\rb*\rb |שָׁ֣מָּה\rb* \rb you are to bring|תָבִ֔יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb command you:|מְצַוֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb your burnt offerings|עוֹלֹתֵיכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and sacrifices,|וְזִבְחֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb your tithes|מַעְשְׂרֹֽתֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb and special gifts,|וּתְרֻמַ֣ת\rb*\rb |יֶדְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and all|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the choice|מִבְחַ֣ר\rb* \rb offerings|נִדְרֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you vow|תִּדְּר֖וּ\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 12 \rb And you shall rejoice|וּשְׂמַחְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵי֮\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God—|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶם֒\rb* \rb you,|אַתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb your sons|וּבְנֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb and daughters,|וּבְנֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb your menservants|וְעַבְדֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and maidservants,|וְאַמְהֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and the Levite|וְהַלֵּוִי֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb within your gates,|בְּשַֽׁעֲרֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb since|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he has no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb portion|חֵ֥לֶק\rb* \rb or inheritance|וְנַחֲלָ֖ה\rb* \rb among you.|אִתְּכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb Be careful|הִשָּׁ֣מֶר\rb* \rb not|פֶּֽן־\rb* \rb to offer|תַּעֲלֶ֖ה\rb* \rb your burnt offerings|עֹלֹתֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb in just any|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb place|מָק֖וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you see;|תִּרְאֶֽה׃\rb* \v 14 \rb you must offer|תַּעֲלֶ֣ה\rb* \rb them|עֹלֹתֶ֑יךָ\rb*\rb |וְשָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb only|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb in the place|בַּמָּק֞וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb will choose|יִבְחַ֤ר\rb* \rb in one|בְּאַחַ֣ד\rb* \rb of your tribal territories,|שְׁבָטֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb you shall do|תַּעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb command you.|מְצַוֶּֽךָּ׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb But|רַק֩\rb* \rb whenever|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb you|נַפְשְׁךָ֜\rb* \rb want,|אַוַּ֨ת\rb* \rb you may slaughter|תִּזְבַּ֣ח׀\rb* \rb and eat|וְאָכַלְתָּ֣\rb* \rb meat|בָשָׂ֗ר\rb* \rb within any|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb of your gates,|שְׁעָרֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb according to the blessing|כְּבִרְכַּ֨ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb has given|נָֽתַן־\rb* \rb you.|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb Both the ceremonially clean|וְהַטָּהוֹר֙\rb* \rb and unclean|הַטָּמֵ֤א\rb* \rb may eat it|יֹאכְלֶ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb as they would a gazelle|כַּצְּבִ֖י\rb* \rb or deer,|וְכָאַיָּֽל׃\rb* \v 16 \rb but|רַ֥ק\rb* \rb you must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb eat|תֹאכֵ֑לוּ\rb* \rb the blood;|הַדָּ֖ם\rb* \rb pour|תִּשְׁפְּכֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb like water.|כַּמָּֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Within your gates|בִּשְׁעָרֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb you must|תוּכַ֞ל\rb* \rb not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb eat|לֶאֱכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb the tithe|מַעְשַׂ֤ר\rb* \rb of your grain|דְּגָֽנְךָ֙\rb* \rb or new wine|וְתִֽירֹשְׁךָ֣\rb* \rb or oil,|וְיִצְהָרֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb the firstborn|וּבְכֹרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of your herds|בְּקָרְךָ֖\rb* \rb or flocks,|וְצֹאנֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb any|וְכָל־\rb* \rb of the offerings|נְדָרֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you have vowed to give,|תִּדֹּ֔ר\rb* \rb or your freewill offerings|וְנִדְבֹתֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |יָדֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb or special gifts.|וּתְרוּמַ֥ת\rb* \v 18 \rb Instead,|כִּ֡י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb you must eat them|תֹּאכְלֶ֗נּוּ\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵי֩\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb at the place|בַּמָּקוֹם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶיךָ֮\rb* \rb will choose—|יִבְחַ֜ר\rb* \rb you,|אַתָּ֨ה\rb* \rb your sons|וּבִנְךָ֤\rb* \rb and daughters,|וּבִתֶּ֙ךָ֙\rb* \rb your menservants|וְעַבְדְּךָ֣\rb* \rb and maidservants,|וַאֲמָתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and the Levite|וְהַלֵּוִ֖י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb within your gates.|בִּשְׁעָרֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb Rejoice|וְשָׂמַחְתָּ֗\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb in all|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb you do,|מִשְׁלַ֥ח\rb*\rb |יָדֶֽךָ׃\rb* \v 19 \rb and be careful|הִשָּׁ֣מֶר\rb* \rb not|פֶּֽן־\rb* \rb to neglect|תַּעֲזֹ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלֵּוִ֑י\rb* \rb as|כָּל־\rb*\rb |יָמֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb long as you live in|עַל־\rb* \rb your land.|אַדְמָתֶֽךָ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֥יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb expands|יַרְחִיב֩\rb* \rb your territory|גְּבֽוּלְךָ֮\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He has promised,|דִּבֶּר־\rb*\rb |לָךְ֒\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb and you|נַפְשְׁךָ֖\rb* \rb crave|תְאַוֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֶאֱכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb meat|בָּשָׂ֑ר\rb* \rb and say,|וְאָמַרְתָּ֙\rb* \rb “I want to eat|אֹכְלָ֣ה\rb* \rb meat,”|בָשָׂ֔ר\rb* \rb you may eat|תֹּאכַ֥ל\rb* \rb it|בָּשָֽׂר׃\rb* \rb whenever|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb you|נַפְשְׁךָ֖\rb* \rb want.|אַוַּ֥ת\rb* \v 21 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֗וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶיךָ֮\rb* \rb chooses|יִבְחַ֜ר\rb* \rb to put|לָשׂ֣וּם\rb* \rb His Name|שְׁמ֣וֹ\rb*\rb |שָׁם֒\rb* \rb is too far|יִרְחַ֨ק\rb* \rb from you,|מִמְּךָ֜\rb* \rb then you may slaughter|וְזָבַחְתָּ֞\rb* \rb any of the herd|מִבְּקָרְךָ֣\rb* \rb or flock|וּמִצֹּֽאנְךָ֗\rb* \rb He|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has given|נָתַ֤ן\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb you,|לְךָ֔\rb* \rb as|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I have commanded you,|צִוִּיתִ֑ךָ\rb* \rb and you may eat|וְאָֽכַלְתָּ֙\rb* \rb it within your gates|בִּשְׁעָרֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb whenever|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb you|נַפְשֶֽׁךָ׃\rb* \rb want.|אַוַּ֥ת\rb* \v 22 \rb Indeed,|אַ֗ךְ\rb* \rb you may eat|יֵאָכֵ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb it as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you would eat|תֹּאכְלֶ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb a gazelle|הַצְּבִי֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb or deer;|הָ֣אַיָּ֔ל\rb*\rb |כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb both|יַחְדָּ֖ו\rb* \rb the ceremonially unclean|הַטָּמֵא֙\rb* \rb and the clean|וְהַטָּה֔וֹר\rb* \rb may eat it.|יֹאכְלֶֽנּוּ׃\rb* \v 23 \rb Only|רַ֣ק\rb* \rb be sure|חֲזַ֗ק\rb* \rb not|לְבִלְתִּי֙\rb* \rb to eat|אֲכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb the blood,|הַדָּ֔ם\rb* \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּ֖ם\rb* \rb is|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb the life,|הַנָּ֑פֶשׁ\rb* \rb and you must not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb eat|תֹאכַ֥ל\rb* \rb the life|הַנֶּ֖פֶשׁ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the meat.|הַבָּשָֽׂר׃\rb* \v 24 \rb |לֹ֖א\rb* \rb You must not eat the blood;|תֹּאכְלֶ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb pour|תִּשְׁפְּכֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb like water.|כַּמָּֽיִם׃\rb* \v 25 \rb Do not|לֹ֖א\rb* \rb eat it,|תֹּאכְלֶ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb it may go well|יִיטַ֤ב\rb* \rb with you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb and your children|וּלְבָנֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb after you,|אַחֲרֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you will be doing|תַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb what is right|הַיָּשָׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb But|רַ֧ק\rb* \rb you are to take|תִּשָּׂ֣א\rb* \rb your holy things|קָֽדָשֶׁ֛יךָ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |יִהְי֥וּ\rb*\rb |לְךָ֖\rb* \rb and your vow offerings|וּנְדָרֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb and go|וּבָ֔אתָ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb will choose.|יִבְחַ֥ר\rb* \v 27 \rb Present|וְעָשִׂ֤יתָ\rb* \rb the meat|הַבָּשָׂ֣ר\rb* \rb and blood|וְהַדָּ֔ם\rb* \rb of your burnt offerings|עֹלֹתֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֖ח\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb The blood|וְדַם־\rb* \rb of your other sacrifices|זְבָחֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb must be poured out|יִשָּׁפֵךְ֙\rb* \rb beside|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּח֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb but you may eat|תֹּאכֵֽל׃\rb* \rb the meat.|וְהַבָּשָׂ֖ר\rb* \v 28 \rb Be careful|שְׁמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb to obey|וְשָׁמַעְתָּ֗\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb things|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb command you,|מְצַוֶּ֑ךָּ\rb* \rb so that|לְמַעַן֩\rb* \rb it may always go well|יִיטַ֨ב\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb with you|לְךָ֜\rb* \rb and your children|וּלְבָנֶ֤יךָ\rb* \rb after you,|אַחֲרֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you will be doing|תַעֲשֶׂה֙\rb* \rb what is good|הַטּ֣וֹב\rb* \rb and right|וְהַיָּשָׁ֔ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃ס\rb*
\s1 A Warning against Idolatry
\r \ref Deuteronomy 4:15–31|DEU 4:15-31\ref*; \ref Ezekiel 6:1–7|EZK 6:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 29 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb cuts off|יַכְרִית֩\rb* \rb before you|מִפָּנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb are entering|בָא־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֛מָּה\rb* \rb to dispossess,|לָרֶ֥שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb and you drive them out|וְיָרַשְׁתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb and live|וְיָשַׁבְתָּ֖\rb* \rb in their land,|בְּאַרְצָֽם׃\rb* \v 30 \rb be careful|הִשָּׁ֣מֶר\rb* \rb not|פֶּן־\rb* \rb to be ensnared|תִּנָּקֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb by their ways|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb they have been destroyed|הִשָּׁמְדָ֣ם\rb* \rb before you.|מִפָּנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb Do not|וּפֶן־\rb* \rb inquire|תִּדְרֹ֨שׁ\rb* \rb about their gods,|לֵֽאלֹהֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb asking,|לֵאמֹ֨ר\rb* \rb “How|אֵיכָ֨ה\rb* \rb do these|הָאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֤ם\rb* \rb serve|יַעַבְד֜וּ\rb* \rb their gods?|אֱלֹ֣הֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb I will|אָֽנִי׃\rb* \rb do|וְאֶעֱשֶׂה־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb likewise.”|גַּם־\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb You must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb worship|תַעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb in this way,|כֵ֔ן\rb* \rb because|כִּי֩\rb* \rb they practice|עָשׂוּ֙\rb* \rb for their gods|לֵאלֹ֣הֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb abomination|תּוֹעֲבַ֨ת\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb hates.|שָׂנֵ֗א\rb* \rb They even|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |גַ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb burn|יִשְׂרְפ֥וּ\rb* \rb their sons|בְּנֵיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and daughters|בְּנֹ֣תֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb in the fire|בָאֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb as sacrifices to their gods.|לֵֽאלֹהֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 32 \rb |אֹת֥וֹ\rb* \rb See that you do|תִשְׁמְר֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb command you;|מְצַוֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |לַעֲשׂ֑וֹת\rb* \rb do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb add|תֹסֵ֣ף\rb* \rb to it|עָלָ֔יו\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb or subtract|תִגְרַ֖ע\rb* \rb from it.|מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃פ\rb*
\c 13
\s1 Idolaters to Be Put to Death
\p \v 1 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a prophet|נָבִ֔יא\rb* \rb or|א֖וֹ\rb* \rb dreamer|חֹלֵ֣ם\rb* \rb of dreams|חֲל֑וֹם\rb* \rb arises|יָק֤וּם\rb* \rb among you|בְּקִרְבְּךָ֙\rb* \rb and proclaims|וְנָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb a sign|א֖וֹת\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb wonder|מוֹפֵֽת׃\rb* \rb to you,|אֵלֶ֛יךָ\rb* \v 2 \rb and if the sign|הָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb or wonder|וְהַמּוֹפֵ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he has spoken|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb comes about,|וּבָ֤א\rb* \rb but he says,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Let us follow|נֵֽלְכָ֞ה\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֨י\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֛ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֧ים\rb* \rb (which you have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb known)|יְדַעְתָּ֖ם\rb* \rb and let us worship them,”|וְנָֽעָבְדֵֽם׃\rb* \v 3 \rb you must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb listen|תִשְׁמַ֗ע\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵי֙\rb* \rb of that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb prophet|הַנָּבִ֣יא\rb* \rb or|א֛וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb dreamer.|חוֹלֵ֥ם\rb*\rb |הַחֲל֖וֹם\rb* \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb is testing you|מְנַסֶּ֞ה\rb* \rb to find out|לָדַ֗עַת\rb* \rb whether|הֲיִשְׁכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb you love|אֹֽהֲבִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Him|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבַבְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and with all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb your soul.|נַפְשְׁכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 4 \rb |אַחֲרֵ֨י\rb* \rb You are to follow|תֵּלֵ֖כוּ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֹת֣וֹ\rb* \rb fear Him.|תִירָ֑אוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Keep|תִּשְׁמֹ֙רוּ֙\rb* \rb His commandments|מִצְוֺתָ֤יו\rb* \rb and listen|תִשְׁמָ֔עוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֹת֥וֹ\rb* \rb to His voice;|וּבְקֹל֣וֹ\rb* \rb serve Him|תַעֲבֹ֖דוּ\rb* \rb and hold fast|תִדְבָּקֽוּן׃\rb* \rb to Him.|וּב֥וֹ\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Such a|הַה֡וּא\rb* \rb prophet|וְהַנָּבִ֣יא\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb dreamer|חֹלֵם֩\rb*\rb |הַחֲל֨וֹם\rb*\rb |הַה֜וּא\rb* \rb must be put to death,|יוּמָ֗ת\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he has advocated|דִבֶּר־\rb* \rb rebellion|סָ֠רָה\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb who brought you out|הַמּוֹצִ֥יא\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֣ם׀\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb and redeemed you|וְהַפֹּֽדְךָ֙\rb* \rb from the house|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of slavery;|עֲבָדִ֔ים\rb* \rb he has tried to turn you|לְהַדִּֽיחֲךָ֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the way|הַדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb in which|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb has commanded you|צִוְּךָ֛\rb* \rb to walk.|לָלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb So you must purge|וּבִֽעַרְתָּ֥\rb* \rb the evil|הָרָ֖ע\rb* \rb from among you.|מִקִּרְבֶּֽךָ׃\rb*\f + \fr 13:5 \ft Cited in \ref 1 Corinthians 5:13|1CO 5:13\ref*\f*
\p \v 6 \rb If|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb your very own brother,|אָחִ֣יךָ\rb*\rb |בֶן־\rb*\rb |אִ֠מֶּךָ\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb your son|בִנְךָ֨\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb daughter,|בִתְּךָ֜\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ׀\rb* \rb the wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb you embrace,|חֵיקֶ֗ךָ\rb*\f + \fr 13:6 \ft Hebrew \fqa the wife of your bosom\f* \rb or|א֧וֹ\rb* \rb your closest friend|רֵֽעֲךָ֛\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |כְּנַפְשְׁךָ֖\rb* \rb secretly|בַּסֵּ֣תֶר\rb* \rb entices you,|יְסִֽיתְךָ֡\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Let us go|נֵֽלְכָ֗ה\rb* \rb and worship|וְנַֽעַבְדָה֙\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gods”|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb (which|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb neither you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb nor|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb your fathers|וַאֲבֹתֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb have known,|יָדַ֔עְתָּ\rb* \v 7 \rb the gods|מֵאֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the peoples|הָֽעַמִּ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb around you,|סְבִיבֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb whether near|הַקְּרֹבִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb or|א֖וֹ\rb* \rb far,|הָרְחֹקִ֣ים\rb* \rb whether from|מִמֶּ֑ךָּ\rb* \rb one end|מִקְצֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb or the other),|וְעַד־\rb*\rb |קְצֵ֥ה\rb*\rb |הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \v 8 \rb you must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb yield|תֹאבֶ֣ה\rb* \rb to him|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb or listen|תִשְׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb to him.|אֵלָ֑יו\rb* \rb Show him no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb pity,|תָח֤וֹס\rb*\rb |עֵֽינְךָ֙\rb*\rb |עָלָ֔יו\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb and do not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb spare|תַחְמֹ֥ל\rb* \rb him|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb or shield|תְכַסֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb him.|עָלָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Instead,|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you must surely kill him.|הָרֹג֙\rb*\rb |תַּֽהַרְגֶ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb Your hand|יָֽדְךָ֛\rb* \rb must be|תִּֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb the first|בָרִֽאשׁוֹנָ֖ה\rb* \rb against him|בּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb to put him to death,|לַהֲמִית֑וֹ\rb* \rb and then|בָּאַחֲרֹנָֽה׃\rb* \rb the hands|וְיַ֥ד\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people.|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \v 10 \rb Stone him|וּסְקַלְתּ֥וֹ\rb*\rb |בָאֲבָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to death|וָמֵ֑ת\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb trying|בִקֵּ֗שׁ\rb* \rb to turn you|לְהַדִּֽיחֲךָ֙\rb* \rb away from|מֵעַל֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb who brought you out|הַמּוֹצִיאֲךָ֛\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb out of the house|מִבֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of slavery.|עֲבָדִֽים׃\rb* \v 11 \rb Then all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb will hear|יִשְׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb and be afraid,|וְיִֽרָא֑וּן\rb* \rb and will never|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb again|יוֹסִ֣פוּ\rb* \rb do|לַעֲשׂ֗וֹת\rb* \rb such|כַּדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb a wicked|הָרָ֛ע\rb* \rb thing|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb among you.|בְּקִרְבֶּֽךָ׃ס\rb*
\s1 Idolatrous Cities to Be Destroyed
\p \v 12 \rb If,|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb regarding one|בְּאַחַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the cities|עָרֶ֗יךָ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֛\rb* \rb to inhabit,|לָשֶׁ֥בֶת\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb you hear|תִשְׁמַ֞ע\rb* \rb it said|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 13 \rb that wicked|בְלִיַּ֙עַל֙\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb have arisen|יָצְא֞וּ\rb* \rb from among you|מִקִּרְבֶּ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and have led the people|יֹשְׁבֵ֥י\rb* \rb of their city|עִירָ֖ם\rb* \rb astray,|וַיַּדִּ֛יחוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Let us go|נֵלְכָ֗ה\rb* \rb and serve|וְנַעַבְדָ֛ה\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֖ים\rb* \rb gods”|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \rb (which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have not|לֹא־\rb* \rb known),|יְדַעְתֶּֽם׃\rb* \v 14 \rb then you must inquire,|וְדָרַשְׁתָּ֧\rb* \rb investigate,|וְחָקַרְתָּ֧\rb* \rb and interrogate|וְשָׁאַלְתָּ֖\rb* \rb thoroughly.|הֵיטֵ֑ב\rb* \rb And if|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb it is established with certainty|אֱמֶת֙\rb*\rb |נָכ֣וֹן\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb that this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb abomination|הַתּוֹעֵבָ֥ה\rb* \rb has been committed|נֶעֶשְׂתָ֛ה\rb* \rb among you,|בְּקִרְבֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \v 15 \rb you must surely put|הַכֵּ֣ה\rb*\rb |תַכֶּ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the inhabitants|יֹֽשְׁבֵ֛י\rb* \rb of that|הַהוּא\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֥יר\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb to the sword.|חָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb Devote to destruction|הַחֲרֵ֨ם\rb*\f + \fr 13:15 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering; similarly in verse 17.\f*\rb |לְפִי־\rb*\rb |חָֽרֶב׃\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֧הּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all its people|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and livestock.|בְּהֶמְתָּ֖הּ\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb you are to gather|תִּקְבֹּץ֮\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its plunder|שְׁלָלָ֗הּ\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the middle|תּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the public square,|רְחֹבָהּ֒\rb* \rb and completely burn|וְשָׂרַפְתָּ֨\rb*\rb |בָאֵ֜שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֤יר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its plunder|שְׁלָלָהּ֙\rb* \rb as a whole burnt offering|כָּלִ֔יל\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb The city must remain|וְהָיְתָה֙\rb* \rb a mound of ruins|תֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb forever,|עוֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb never|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to be rebuilt.|תִבָּנֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |עֽוֹד׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Nothing|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |מְא֖וּמָה\rb* \rb devoted to destruction|הַחֵ֑רֶם\rb* \rb shall cling|יִדְבַּ֧ק\rb* \rb to your hands,|בְּיָדְךָ֛\rb* \rb so that|לְמַעַן֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb will turn|יָשׁ֨וּב\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb His fierce anger,|מֵחֲר֣וֹן\rb*\rb |אַפּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb grant|וְנָֽתַן־\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֤\rb* \rb mercy,|רַחֲמִים֙\rb* \rb show you compassion,|וְרִֽחַמְךָ֣\rb* \rb and multiply you|וְהִרְבֶּ֔ךָ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He swore|נִשְׁבַּ֖ע\rb* \rb to your fathers,|לַאֲבֹתֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 18 \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you obey|תִשְׁמַ֗ע\rb*\rb |בְּקוֹל֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb keeping|לִשְׁמֹר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb His commandments|מִצְוֺתָ֔יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb am giving you today|מְצַוְּךָ֖\rb*\rb |הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb and doing|לַעֲשׂוֹת֙\rb* \rb what is right|הַיָּשָׁ֔ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃ס\rb*
\c 14
\s1 Clean and Unclean Animals
