\p \v 22 \rb You must be sure to set aside a tenth|עַשֵּׂ֣ר\rb*\rb |תְּעַשֵּׂ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the produce|תְּבוּאַ֣ת\rb*\rb |זַרְעֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb brought forth|הַיֹּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb each year|שָׁנָ֥ה\rb*\rb |שָׁנָֽה׃\rb* \rb from your fields.|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \v 23 \rb And you are to eat|וְאָכַלְתָּ֞\rb* \rb a tenth|מַעְשַׂ֤ר\rb* \rb of your grain,|דְּגָֽנְךָ֙\rb* \rb new wine,|תִּֽירֹשְׁךָ֣\rb* \rb and oil,|וְיִצְהָרֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and the firstborn|וּבְכֹרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of your herds|בְּקָרְךָ֖\rb* \rb and flocks,|וְצֹאנֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb at the place|בַּמָּק֣וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He will choose|יִבְחַר֮\rb*\rb |שָׁם֒\rb* \rb as a dwelling|לְשַׁכֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb for His Name,|שְׁמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb you may learn|תִּלְמַ֗ד\rb* \rb to fear|לְיִרְאָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb always.|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb But if|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb the distance|הַדֶּ֗רֶךְ\rb* \rb is too great|יִרְבֶּ֨ה\rb* \rb for|מִמְּךָ֜\rb* \rb you to carry|שְׂאֵתוֹ֒\rb* \rb that with which|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb has blessed you,|יְבָרֶכְךָ֖\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |תוּכַ֘ל\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֔וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb will choose|יִבְחַר֙\rb* \rb to put|לָשׂ֥וּם\rb* \rb His Name|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |שָׁ֑ם\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb is too far away,|יִרְחַ֤ק\rb*\rb |מִמְּךָ֙\rb* \v 25 \rb then exchange|וְנָתַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb it for money,|בַּכָּ֑סֶף\rb* \rb take|וְצַרְתָּ֤\rb* \rb the money|הַכֶּ֙סֶף֙\rb* \rb in your hand,|בְּיָ֣דְךָ֔\rb* \rb and go|וְהָֽלַכְתָּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֔וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb will choose.|יִבְחַ֛ר\rb* \v 26 \rb Then you may spend|וְנָתַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb the money|הַכֶּ֡סֶף\rb* \rb on anything|בְּכֹל֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|נַפְשְׁךָ֜\rb* \rb desire:|תְּאַוֶּ֨ה\rb* \rb cattle,|בַּבָּקָ֣ר\rb* \rb sheep,|וּבַצֹּ֗אן\rb* \rb wine,|וּבַיַּ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb strong drink,|וּבַשֵּׁכָ֔ר\rb* \rb or anything|וּבְכֹ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you|נַפְשֶׁ֑ךָ\rb* \rb wish.|תִּֽשְׁאָלְךָ֖\rb* \rb You are to feast|וְאָכַ֣לְתָּ\rb* \rb there|שָּׁ֗ם\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and rejoice|וְשָׂמַחְתָּ֖\rb*\rb |אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb with your household.|וּבֵיתֶֽךָ׃\rb* \v 27 \rb And do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb neglect|תַֽעַזְבֶ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb the Levite|וְהַלֵּוִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb within your gates,|בִּשְׁעָרֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb since|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he has no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb portion|חֵ֥לֶק\rb* \rb or inheritance|וְנַחֲלָ֖ה\rb* \rb among you.|עִמָּֽךְ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb At the end|מִקְצֵ֣ה׀\rb* \rb of every three|שָׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb years,|שָׁנִ֗ים\rb* \rb bring|תּוֹצִיא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a tenth|מַעְשַׂר֙\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your produce|תְּבוּאָ֣תְךָ֔\rb* \rb for that|הַהִ֑וא\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb and lay it up|וְהִנַּחְתָּ֖\rb* \rb within your gates.|בִּשְׁעָרֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 29 \rb Then the Levite|הַלֵּוִ֡י\rb* \rb (because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he has no|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb portion|חֵ֨לֶק\rb* \rb or inheritance|וְנַחֲלָ֜ה\rb* \rb among you),|עִמָּ֗ךְ\rb* \rb the foreigner,|וְ֠הַגֵּר\rb* \rb the fatherless,|וְהַיָּת֤וֹם\rb* \rb and the widow|וְהָֽאַלְמָנָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb within your gates|בִּשְׁעָרֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb may come|וּבָ֣א\rb* \rb and eat|וְאָכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb and be satisfied.|וְשָׂבֵ֑עוּ\rb*\rb |לְמַ֤עַן\rb* \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb will bless|יְבָרֶכְךָ֙\rb* \rb you in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the work|מַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb of your hands.|יָדְךָ֖\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |תַּעֲשֶֽׂה׃ס\rb*
\c 15
\s1 The Seventh Year
\r \ref Exodus 23:10–13|EXO 23:10-13\ref*; \ref Leviticus 25:1–7|LEV 25:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb At the end|מִקֵּ֥ץ\rb* \rb of every seven|שֶֽׁבַע־\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |תַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb you must cancel debts.|שְׁמִטָּֽה׃\rb* \v 2 \rb This|וְזֶה֮\rb* \rb is the manner|דְּבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of remission:|הַשְּׁמִטָּה֒\rb* \rb Every|כָּל־\rb* \rb creditor|בַּ֙עַל֙\rb*\rb |מַשֵּׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |יָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb shall cancel|שָׁמ֗וֹט\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he has loaned|יַשֶּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb to his neighbor.|בְּרֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb He is not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to collect|יִגֹּ֤שׂ\rb* \rb anything|אֶת־\rb* \rb from his neighbor|רֵעֵ֙הוּ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb or brother,|אָחִ֔יו\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb time of release|שְׁמִטָּ֖ה\rb* \rb has been proclaimed.|קָרָ֥א\rb* \v 3 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb You may collect|תִּגֹּ֑שׂ\rb* \rb something from a foreigner,|הַנָּכְרִ֖י\rb* \rb but you must forgive|תַּשְׁמֵ֥ט\rb*\rb |יָדֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb whatever|וַאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb your brother|אָחִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb owes|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb you.|לְךָ֛\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb There will be|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb poor|אֶבְי֑וֹן\rb* \rb among you,|בְּךָ֖\rb* \rb however,|אֶ֕פֶס\rb*\rb |כִּ֛י\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb will surely bless you|בָרֵ֤ךְ\rb*\rb |יְבָֽרֶכְךָ֙\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֕רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹֽתֵן־\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֥\rb* \rb to possess|לְרִשְׁתָּֽהּ׃\rb* \rb as an inheritance,|נַחֲלָ֖ה\rb* \v 5 \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb only|רַ֚ק\rb* \rb you obey|שָׁמ֣וֹעַ\rb*\rb |תִּשְׁמַ֔ע\rb*\rb |בְּק֖וֹל\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb and are careful|לִשְׁמֹ֤ר\rb* \rb to follow|לַעֲשׂוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הַזֹּ֔את\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb commandments|הַמִּצְוָ֣ה\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb am giving you today.|מְצַוְּךָ֖\rb*\rb |הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb* \v 6 \rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb When the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb blesses you|בֵּֽרַכְךָ֔\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb He has promised,|דִּבֶּר־\rb* \rb you will lend|וְהַֽעֲבַטְתָּ֞\rb* \rb to many|רַבִּ֗ים\rb*\rb |וְאַתָּה֙\rb* \rb nations|גּוֹיִ֣ם\rb* \rb but borrow|תַעֲבֹ֔ט\rb* \rb from none;|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb you will rule|וּמָֽשַׁלְתָּ֙\rb* \rb over many|רַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb nations|בְּגוֹיִ֣ם\rb* \rb but be ruled|יִמְשֹֽׁלוּ׃ס\rb* \rb by none.|לֹ֥א\rb*
\s1 Generosity in Lending and Giving
\r \ref Matthew 6:1–4|MAT 6:1-4\ref*)
\p \v 7 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb there is|יִהְיֶה֩\rb* \rb a poor man|אֶבְי֜וֹן\rb* \rb among|בְךָ֨\rb*\rb |מֵאַחַ֤ד\rb* \rb your brothers|אַחֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb within any|בְּאַחַ֣ד\rb* \rb of the gates|שְׁעָרֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאַ֨רְצְךָ֔\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb you,|לָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb then you are not|לֹ֧א\rb* \rb to harden|תְאַמֵּ֣ץ\rb*\f + \fr 15:7 \ft Or \fqa make strong \ft or \fqa make courageous\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָבְךָ֗\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb shut|תִקְפֹּץ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your hand|יָ֣דְךָ֔\rb* \rb from your poor|הָאֶבְיֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb brother.|מֵאָחִ֖יךָ\rb* \v 8 \rb Instead,|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you are to open|פָתֹ֧חַ\rb*\rb |תִּפְתַּ֛ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your hand|יָדְךָ֖\rb* \rb to him|ל֑וֹ\rb* \rb and freely loan him|וְהַעֲבֵט֙\rb* \rb whatever|דֵּ֚י\rb* \rb he needs.|מַחְסֹר֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |יֶחְסַ֖ר\rb*\rb |לֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Be careful|הִשָּׁ֣מֶר\rb* \rb not to harbor|פֶּן־\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb this wicked|בְלִיַּ֜עַל\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb thought|דָבָר֩\rb* \rb in|עִם־\rb* \rb your heart:|לְבָבְךָ֨\rb* \rb “The seventh|הַשֶּׁבַע֮\rb* \rb year,|שְׁנַֽת־\rb* \rb the year|שְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of release,|הַשְּׁמִטָּה֒\rb* \rb is near,”|קָֽרְבָ֣ה\rb* \rb so that you look upon|עֵֽינְךָ֗\rb* \rb your poor|הָֽאֶבְי֔וֹן\rb* \rb brother|בְּאָחִ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb begrudgingly|וְרָעָ֣ה\rb* \rb and give him|תִתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb nothing.|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb He will cry out|וְקָרָ֤א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb against you,|עָלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb and you will be|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb guilty of sin.|חֵֽטְא׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Give generously|נָת֤וֹן\rb*\rb |תִּתֵּן֙\rb* \rb to him,|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb and do not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb let your heart|לְבָבְךָ֖\rb* \rb be grieved|יֵרַ֥ע\rb* \rb when you do so.|בְּתִתְּךָ֣\rb*\rb |ל֑וֹ\rb*\rb |כִּ֞י\rb* \rb And because of|בִּגְלַ֣ל׀\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb will bless|יְבָרֶכְךָ֙\rb* \rb you in all|בְּכָֽל־\rb* \rb your work|מַעֲשֶׂ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and in everything|וּבְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb to which you put|מִשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb your hand.|יָדֶֽךָ׃\rb* \v 11 \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb there will never|לֹא־\rb* \rb cease|יֶחְדַּ֥ל\rb* \rb to be poor|אֶבְי֖וֹן\rb* \rb in|מִקֶּ֣רֶב\rb* \rb the land;|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb that is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֞ן\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֤י\rb* \rb am commanding you|מְצַוְּךָ֙\rb* \rb to|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb open|פָּ֠תֹחַ\rb* \rb wide|תִּפְתַּ֨ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your hand|יָדְךָ֜\rb* \rb to your brother|לְאָחִ֧יךָ\rb* \rb and to the poor|לַעֲנִיֶּ֛ךָ\rb* \rb and needy|וּלְאֶבְיֹנְךָ֖\rb* \rb in your land.|בְּאַרְצֶֽךָ׃ס\rb*
\s1 Hebrew Servants
\r \ref Exodus 21:1–11|EXO 21:1-11\ref*)
\p \v 12 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a fellow|אָחִ֣יךָ\rb* \rb Hebrew,|הָֽעִבְרִ֗י\rb* \rb a man or|א֚וֹ\rb* \rb a woman,|הָֽעִבְרִיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb is sold|יִמָּכֵ֨ר\rb*\f + \fr 15:12 \ft Or \fqa sells himself\f* \rb to you|לְךָ֜\rb* \rb and serves you|וַעֲבָֽדְךָ֖\rb* \rb six|שֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb years,|שָׁנִ֑ים\rb* \rb then in the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔ת\rb* \rb year|וּבַשָּׁנָה֙\rb* \rb you must set him|תְּשַׁלְּחֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb free.|חָפְשִׁ֖י\rb*\rb |מֵעִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb And when|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb you release him,|תְשַׁלְּחֶ֥נּוּ\rb*\rb |חָפְשִׁ֖י\rb*\rb |מֵֽעִמָּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb send him away|תְשַׁלְּחֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb empty-handed.|רֵיקָֽם׃\rb* \v 14 \rb You are to furnish him liberally|הַעֲנֵ֤יק\rb*\rb |תַּעֲנִיק֙\rb* \rb from your flock,|מִצֹּ֣אנְךָ֔\rb* \rb your threshing floor,|וּמִֽגָּרְנְךָ֖\rb* \rb and your winepress.|וּמִיִּקְבֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb You shall give|תִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb to him|לֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb as|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb has blessed you.|בֵּרַכְךָ֛\rb* \v 15 \rb Remember|וְזָכַרְתָּ֗\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you were|הָיִ֙יתָ֙\rb* \rb slaves|עֶ֤בֶד\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb redeemed you;|וַֽיִּפְדְּךָ֖\rb* \rb that is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֞ן\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֧י\rb* \rb am giving|מְצַוְּךָ֛\rb* \rb you|אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb command|הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb today.|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb |וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb But if|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb your servant says|יֹאמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to you,|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb ‘I do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb want to leave|אֵצֵ֖א\rb* \rb you,’|מֵעִמָּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb he loves|אֲהֵֽבְךָ֙\rb* \rb you|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and your household|בֵּיתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and|כִּי־\rb* \rb is well off|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb with you,|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb* \v 17 \rb then take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb an awl|הַמַּרְצֵ֗עַ\rb* \rb and pierce it|וְנָתַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb through his ear|בְאָזְנוֹ֙\rb* \rb into the door,|וּבַדֶּ֔לֶת\rb* \rb and he will become|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb your|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb servant|עֶ֣בֶד\rb* \rb for life.|עוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb And|וְאַ֥ף\rb* \rb treat|תַּעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb your maidservant|לַאֲמָתְךָ֖\rb* \rb the same way.|כֵּֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb regard it|בְעֵינֶ֗ךָ\rb* \rb as a hardship|יִקְשֶׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |מֵֽעִמָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb to set|בְּשַׁלֵּֽחֲךָ֙\rb* \rb your servant|אֹת֤וֹ\rb* \rb free,|חָפְשִׁי֙\rb* \rb because|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb his six|שֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֑ים\rb* \rb of service|עֲבָֽדְךָ֖\rb* \rb were worth twice|מִשְׁנֶה֙\rb* \rb the wages|שְׂכַ֣ר\rb* \rb of a hired hand.|שָׂכִ֔יר\rb* \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb will bless you|וּבֵֽרַכְךָ֙\rb* \rb in all|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you do.|תַּעֲשֶֽׂה׃פ\rb*
\s1 Firstborn Animals
\r \ref Exodus 13:1–16|EXO 13:1-16\ref*)
\p \v 19 \rb You must set apart|תַּקְדִּ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb every|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb firstborn|הַבְּכ֡וֹר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb male|הַזָּכָ֔ר\rb* \rb produced|יִוָּלֵ֨ד\rb* \rb by your herds|בִּבְקָרְךָ֤\rb* \rb and flocks.|וּבְצֹֽאנְךָ֙\rb* \rb You are not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb to put the firstborn|בִּבְכֹ֣ר\rb* \rb of your oxen|שׁוֹרֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb to work,|תַעֲבֹד֙\rb* \rb nor|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb are you to shear|תָגֹ֖ז\rb* \rb the firstborn|בְּכ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of your flock.|צֹאנֶֽךָ׃\rb* \v 20 \rb Each year|שָׁנָ֣ה\rb*\rb |בְשָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and your household|וּבֵיתֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb are to eat it|תֹאכֲלֶ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵי֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֤יךָ\rb* \rb in the place|בַּמָּק֖וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb will choose.|יִבְחַ֣ר\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb But if|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb an animal has|יִהְיֶ֨ה\rb* \rb a defect,|מ֗וּם\rb* \rb is lame|פִּסֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb blind,|עִוֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb or has any|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb serious|רָ֑ע\rb* \rb flaw,|מ֣וּם\rb* \rb you must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb sacrifice|תִזְבָּחֶ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb it to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 22 \rb Eat it|תֹּאכֲלֶ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb within your gates;|בִּשְׁעָרֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb both|יַחְדָּ֔ו\rb* \rb the ceremonially unclean|הַטָּמֵ֤א\rb* \rb and clean may eat it|וְהַטָּהוֹר֙\rb* \rb as they would a gazelle|כַּצְּבִ֖י\rb* \rb or a deer.|וְכָאַיָּֽל׃\rb* \v 23 \rb But|רַ֥ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb you must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb eat|תֹאכֵ֑ל\rb* \rb the blood;|דָּמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb pour|תִּשְׁפְּכֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb like water.|כַּמָּֽיִם׃פ\rb*
\c 16
\s1 Passover and the Feast of Unleavened Bread
\r \ref Exodus 12:14–28|EXO 12:14-28\ref*; \ref Leviticus 23:4–8|LEV 23:4-8\ref*; \ref Numbers 28:16–25|NUM 28:16-25\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Observe|שָׁמוֹר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the month|חֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Abib|הָאָבִ֔יב\rb*\f + \fr 16:1 \fqa Abib \ft was the first month of the ancient Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of March and April; twice in this verse.\f* \rb and celebrate|וְעָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb* \rb the Passover|פֶּ֔סַח\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb because|כִּ֞י\rb* \rb in the month|בְּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Abib|הָֽאָבִ֗יב\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb brought you out|הוֹצִ֨יאֲךָ֜\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb by night.|לָֽיְלָה׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb You are to offer|וְזָבַ֥חְתָּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb the Passover sacrifice|פֶּ֛סַח\rb* \rb from the herd|וּבָקָ֑ר\rb* \rb or flock|צֹ֣אן\rb* \rb in the place|בַּמָּקוֹם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb will choose|יִבְחַ֣ר\rb* \rb as a dwelling|לְשַׁכֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb for His Name.|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb* \v 3 \rb You must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb eat|תֹאכַ֤ל\rb* \rb leavened bread|חָמֵ֔ץ\rb* \rb with it;|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֛ים\rb* \rb you are to eat|תֹּֽאכַל־\rb* \rb with it|עָלָ֥יו\rb* \rb unleavened bread,|מַצּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb the bread|לֶ֣חֶם\rb* \rb of affliction,|עֹ֑נִי\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you left|יָצָ֙אתָ֙\rb* \rb the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb in haste—|בְחִפָּז֗וֹן\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb you may remember|תִּזְכֹּר֔\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |י֤וֹם\rb* \rb for the rest|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb of your life|חַיֶּֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb the day|יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb you left|צֵֽאתְךָ֙\rb* \rb the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb No|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb leaven|שְׂאֹ֛ר\rb* \rb is to be found|יֵרָאֶ֨ה\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your land|גְּבֻלְךָ֖\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days,|יָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb and none|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the meat|הַבָּשָׂ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you sacrifice|תִּזְבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb in the evening|בָּעֶ֛רֶב\rb* \rb of the first|הָרִאשׁ֖וֹן\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb shall remain|יָלִ֣ין\rb* \rb until morning.|לַבֹּֽקֶר׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb You are not|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |תוּכַ֖ל\rb* \rb to sacrifice|לִזְבֹּ֣חַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Passover animal|הַפָּ֑סַח\rb* \rb in any|בְּאַחַ֣ד\rb* \rb of the towns|שְׁעָרֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you.|לָֽךְ׃\rb* \v 6 \rb You must only|כִּ֠י\rb*\rb |אִֽם־\rb* \rb offer|תִּזְבַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Passover sacrifice|הַפֶּ֖סַח\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֞וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb will choose|יִבְחַ֨ר\rb* \rb as a dwelling|לְשַׁכֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb for His Name.|שְׁמ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |שָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb Do this in the evening|בָּעָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb as the sun|הַשֶּׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb* \rb sets,|כְּב֣וֹא\rb* \rb at the same time|מוֹעֵ֖ד\rb* \rb you departed|צֵֽאתְךָ֥\rb* \rb from Egypt.|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 7 \rb And you shall roast it|וּבִשַּׁלְתָּ֙\rb* \rb and eat it|וְאָ֣כַלְתָּ֔\rb* \rb in the place|בַּמָּק֕וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |וּפָנִ֣יתָ\rb* \rb will choose,|יִבְחַ֛ר\rb* \rb and in the morning|בַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb you shall return|וְהָלַכְתָּ֖\rb* \rb to your tents.|לְאֹהָלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb For six|שֵׁ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb you must eat|תֹּאכַ֣ל\rb* \rb unleavened bread,|מַצּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb and on the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֗י\rb* \rb day|וּבַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb you shall hold a solemn assembly|עֲצֶ֙רֶת֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and you must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb do|תַעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb any work.|מְלָאכָֽה׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Feast of Weeks
\r \ref Numbers 28:26–31|NUM 28:26-31\ref*)
\p \v 9 \rb You are to count off|תִּסְפָּר־\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָ֥ה\rb* \rb weeks|שָׁבֻעֹ֖ת\rb* \rb from|לִסְפֹּ֔ר\rb*\rb |שִׁבְעָ֖ה\rb* \rb the time|שָׁבֻעֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb you first put the sickle|חֶרְמֵשׁ֙\rb*\rb |מֵהָחֵ֤ל\rb* \rb to the standing grain.|בַּקָּמָ֔ה\rb*\rb |תָּחֵ֣ל\rb* \v 10 \rb And you shall celebrate|וְעָשִׂ֜יתָ\rb* \rb the Feast|חַ֤ג\rb* \rb of Weeks|שָׁבֻעוֹת֙\rb*\f + \fr 16:10 \ft That is, Shavuot; see footnotes for verse 16.\f* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |מִסַּ֛ת\rb* \rb with a freewill offering|נִדְבַ֥ת\rb*\rb |יָדְךָ֖\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you give|תִּתֵּ֑ן\rb* \rb in proportion to how|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb has blessed you,|יְבָרֶכְךָ֖\rb* \v 11 \rb and you shall rejoice|וְשָׂמַחְתָּ֞\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb in the place|בַּמָּק֗וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb He|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb will choose|יִבְחַר֙\rb* \rb as a dwelling|לְשַׁכֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb for His Name—|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb*  \rb you,|אַתָּ֨ה\rb* \rb your sons|וּבִנְךָ֣\rb* \rb and daughters,|וּבִתֶּךָ֮\rb* \rb your menservants|וְעַבְדְּךָ֣\rb* \rb and maidservants,|וַאֲמָתֶךָ֒\rb* \rb and the Levite|וְהַלֵּוִי֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb within your gates,|בִּשְׁעָרֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb as well as the foreigner,|וְהַגֵּ֛ר\rb* \rb the fatherless,|וְהַיָּת֥וֹם\rb* \rb and the widows|וְהָאַלְמָנָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb among you.|בְּקִרְבֶּ֑ךָ\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb Remember|וְזָ֣כַרְתָּ֔\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb you were|הָיִ֖יתָ\rb* \rb slaves|עֶ֥בֶד\rb* \rb in Egypt,|בְּמִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and carefully|וְשָׁמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb follow|וְעָשִׂ֔יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃פ\rb* \rb statutes.|הַֽחֻקִּ֖ים\rb*
\s1 The Feast of Tabernacles
\r \ref Numbers 29:12–40|NUM 29:12-40\ref*)
\p \v 13 \rb You are to celebrate|תַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb the Feast|חַ֧ג\rb* \rb of Tabernacles|הַסֻּכֹּ֛ת\rb*\f + \fr 16:13 \ft Or \fqa Booths \ft or \fqa Shelters\ft ; see footnotes for verse 16.\f* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb after you have gathered|בְּאָ֨סְפְּךָ֔\rb* \rb the produce of your threshing floor|מִֽגָּרְנְךָ֖\rb* \rb and your winepress.|וּמִיִּקְבֶֽךָ׃\rb* \v 14 \rb And you shall rejoice|וְשָׂמַחְתָּ֖\rb* \rb in your feast—|בְּחַגֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb you,|אַתָּ֨ה\rb* \rb your sons|וּבִנְךָ֤\rb* \rb and daughters,|וּבִתֶּ֙ךָ֙\rb* \rb your menservants|וְעַבְדְּךָ֣\rb* \rb and maidservants,|וַאֲמָתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and the Levite,|וְהַלֵּוִ֗י\rb* \rb as well as the foreigner,|וְהַגֵּ֛ר\rb* \rb the fatherless,|וְהַיָּת֥וֹם\rb* \rb and the widows|וְהָאַלְמָנָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb among you.|בִּשְׁעָרֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb For seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֗ים\rb* \rb you shall celebrate a feast|תָּחֹג֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb in the place|בַּמָּק֖וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb will choose,|יִבְחַ֣ר\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb will bless|יְבָרֶכְךָ֞\rb* \rb you in all|בְּכֹ֤ל\rb* \rb your produce|תְּבוּאָֽתְךָ֙\rb* \rb and in all|וּבְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the work|מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb of your hands,|יָדֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb so that your joy|שָׂמֵֽחַ׃\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיִ֖יתָ\rb* \rb complete.|אַ֥ךְ\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb Three|שָׁל֣וֹשׁ\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb a year|בַּשָּׁנָ֡ה\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb your men|זְכוּרְךָ֜\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb are to appear|יֵרָאֶ֨ה\rb* \rb before|פְּנֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb in the place|בַּמָּקוֹם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He will choose:|יִבְחָ֔ר\rb* \rb at the Feast|בְּחַ֧ג\rb* \rb of Unleavened Bread,|הַמַּצּ֛וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 16:16 \ft That is, the seven-day period after the Passover during which no leaven may be eaten; see \ref Exodus 12:14–20|EXO 12:14-20\ref*.\f* \rb the Feast|וּבְחַ֥ג\rb* \rb of Weeks,|הַשָּׁבֻע֖וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 16:16 \ft That is, Shavuot, the late spring feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; it is also known as \fqa the Feast of Harvest\ft (see \ref Exodus 23:16|EXO 23:16\ref*) or \fqa the Feast of Pentecost\ft (see \ref Acts 2:1|ACT 2:1\ref*).\f* \rb and the Feast|וּבְחַ֣ג\rb* \rb of Tabernacles.|הַסֻּכּ֑וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 16:16 \ft That is, Sukkot, the autumn feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; also translated as \fqa the Feast of Booths \ft or \fqa the Feast of Shelters \ft and originally called \fqa the Feast of Ingathering\ft (see \ref Exodus 23:16|EXO 23:16\ref* and Exodus 34:22).\f* \rb No one|וְלֹ֧א\rb* \rb should appear|יֵרָאֶ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb before|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb empty-handed.|רֵיקָֽם׃\rb* \v 17 \rb Everyone|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb must appear with a gift|כְּמַתְּנַ֣ת\rb* \rb as he is able,|יָד֑וֹ\rb* \rb according to the blessing|כְּבִרְכַּ֛ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb has given|נָֽתַן־\rb* \rb you.|לָֽךְ׃ס\rb*
\s1 Judges and Justice
\p \v 18 \rb You are to appoint|תִּֽתֶּן־\rb* \rb judges|שֹׁפְטִ֣ים\rb* \rb and officials|וְשֹֽׁטְרִ֗ים\rb* \rb for your tribes|לִשְׁבָטֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb in every|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb town|שְׁעָרֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you.|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb They are to judge|וְשָׁפְט֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb with righteous|צֶֽדֶק׃\rb* \rb judgment.|מִשְׁפַּט־\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb deny|תַטֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפָּ֔ט\rb* \rb or show partiality.|תַכִּ֖יר\rb*\rb |פָּנִ֑ים\rb*\rb |וְלֹא־\rb* \rb Do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb accept|תִקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb a bribe,|שֹׁ֔חַד\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb a bribe|הַשֹּׁ֗חַד\rb* \rb blinds|יְעַוֵּר֙\rb* \rb the eyes|עֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the wise|חֲכָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb and twists|וִֽיסַלֵּ֖ף\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the righteous.|צַדִּיקִֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb Pursue|תִּרְדֹּ֑ף\rb* \rb justice,|צֶ֥דֶק\rb* \rb and justice alone,|צֶ֖דֶק\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֤עַן\rb* \rb you may live,|תִּֽחְיֶה֙\rb* \rb and you may possess|וְיָרַשְׁתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you.|לָֽךְ׃ס\rb*
\s1 Forbidden Forms of Worship
\p \v 21 \rb Do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb set up|תִטַּ֥ע\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb wooden|עֵ֑ץ\rb* \rb Asherah pole|אֲשֵׁרָ֖ה\rb* \rb next to|אֵ֗צֶל\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֛ח\rb* \rb you will build|תַּעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb for the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \v 22 \rb and do not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb set up|תָקִ֥ים\rb* \rb for yourselves|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb a sacred pillar,|מַצֵּבָ֑ה\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃ס\rb* \rb hates.|שָׂנֵ֖א\rb*
\c 17
\s1 Detestable Sacrifices
\p \v 1 \rb You shall not|לֹא־\rb* \rb sacrifice|תִזְבַּח֩\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb an ox|שׁ֣וֹר\rb* \rb or a sheep|וָשֶׂ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb with any defect|מ֔וּם\rb* \rb or|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb serious|רָ֑ע\rb* \rb flaw,|דָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb for|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb that|הֽוּא׃ס\rb* \rb is detestable|תוֹעֲבַ֛ת\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb*
\s1 Purge the Idolater
\p \v 2 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb woman|אִשָּׁ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb among you|בְקִרְבְּךָ֙\rb* \rb in one|בְּאַחַ֣ד\rb* \rb of the towns|שְׁעָרֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb gives|נֹתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb you|לָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb is found|יִמָּצֵ֤א\rb* \rb doing|יַעֲשֶׂ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֛ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה־\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb by transgressing|לַעֲבֹ֥ר\rb* \rb His covenant|בְּרִיתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 3 \rb and going|וַיֵּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb to worship|וַֽיַּעֲבֹד֙\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gods,|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb bowing down|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֖חוּ\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb or to the sun|וְלַשֶּׁ֣מֶשׁ׀\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb moon|לַיָּרֵ֗חַ\rb* \rb or|א֛וֹ\rb* \rb any|לְכָל־\rb* \rb of the host|צְבָ֥א\rb* \rb of heaven—|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have forbidden—|לֹא־\rb*\rb |צִוִּֽיתִי׃\rb* \v 4 \rb and if it is reported|וְהֻֽגַּד־\rb* \rb and you hear about it,|וְשָׁמָ֑עְתָּ\rb* \rb you must investigate it|וְדָרַשְׁתָּ֣\rb* \rb thoroughly.|הֵיטֵ֔ב\rb*
\p \rb If|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb the report|הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb is|נֶעֶשְׂתָ֛ה\rb* \rb true|אֱמֶת֙\rb*\rb |נָכ֣וֹן\rb* \rb and such|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb an abomination|הַתּוֹעֵבָ֥ה\rb* \rb has happened in Israel,|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 5 \rb you must bring out|וְהֽוֹצֵאתָ֣\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your gates|שְׁעָרֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הָאִ֕ישׁ\rb*\rb |א֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הָאִשָּׁ֑ה\rb*\rb |הַה֡וּא\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb or|אוֹ֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb woman|הָאִשָּׁ֨ה\rb*\rb |הַהִ֜וא\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb has done|עָ֠שׂוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb evil|הָרָ֤ע\rb* \rb thing,|הַדָּבָ֨ר\rb* \rb and you must stone that person|וּסְקַלְתָּ֥ם\rb*\rb |בָּאֲבָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to death.|וָמֵֽתוּ׃\rb* \v 6 \rb On|עַל־\rb* \rb the testimony|פִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb of two|שְׁנַ֣יִם\rb* \rb or|א֛וֹ\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb witnesses|עֵדִ֗ים\rb* \rb a man shall be put to death,|יוּמַ֣ת\rb*\rb |הַמֵּ֑ת\rb* \rb but he shall not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be executed|יוּמַ֔ת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the testimony|פִּ֖י\rb*\rb |עֵ֥ד\rb* \rb of a lone|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb witness.|עֵדִ֖ים\rb* \v 7 \rb The hands|יַ֣ד\rb* \rb of the witnesses|הָעֵדִ֞ים\rb* \rb shall be|תִּֽהְיֶה־\rb*\rb |בּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb the first|בָרִאשֹׁנָה֙\rb* \rb in putting him to death,|לַהֲמִית֔וֹ\rb* \rb and after that,|בָּאַחֲרֹנָ֑ה\rb* \rb the hands|וְיַ֥ד\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people.|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb So you must purge|וּבִֽעַרְתָּ֥\rb* \rb the evil|הָרָ֖ע\rb* \rb from among you.|מִקִּרְבֶּֽךָ׃פ\rb*\f + \fr 17:7 \ft Cited in \ref 1 Corinthians 5:13|1CO 5:13\ref*\f*
\s1 Courts of Law
\p \v 8 \rb If|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb a case|דָבָ֜ר\rb* \rb is too difficult|יִפָּלֵא֩\rb* \rb for you|מִמְּךָ֨\rb* \rb to judge,|לַמִּשְׁפָּ֗ט\rb* \rb whether|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb the controversy|רִיבֹ֖ת\rb* \rb within your gates|בִּשְׁעָרֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb is regarding|בֵּֽין־\rb* \rb bloodshed,|דָּ֨ם׀\rb*\rb |לְדָ֜ם\rb*\rb |בֵּֽין־\rb* \rb lawsuits,|דִּ֣ין\rb*\rb |לְדִ֗ין\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb or assaults,|נֶ֙גַע֙\rb*\rb |לָנֶ֔גַע\rb*\rb |וְקַמְתָּ֣\rb* \rb you must go up|וְעָלִ֔יתָ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֔וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |בּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb will choose.|יִבְחַ֛ר\rb* \v 9 \rb You are to go|וּבָאתָ֗\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Levitical|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb priests|הַכֹּהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the judge|הַשֹּׁפֵ֔ט\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb presides at that|הָהֵ֑ם\rb* \rb time.|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb Inquire of them,|וְדָרַשְׁתָּ֙\rb* \rb and they will give|וְהִגִּ֣ידוּ\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb a verdict|דְּבַ֥ר\rb* \rb in the case.|הַמִּשְׁפָּֽט׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb You must abide by|וְעָשִׂ֗יתָ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |פִּ֤י\rb* \rb the verdict|הַדָּבָר֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they give|יַגִּ֣ידֽוּ\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֔\rb* \rb at|מִן־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַה֔וּא\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb will choose.|יִבְחַ֣ר\rb* \rb Be careful|וְשָׁמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשׂ֔וֹת\rb* \rb everything|כְּכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they instruct you,|יוֹרֽוּךָ׃\rb* \v 11 \rb according|עַל־\rb* \rb to the terms|פִּ֨י\rb* \rb of law|הַתּוֹרָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they give|יוֹר֗וּךָ\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and the verdict|הַמִּשְׁפָּ֛ט\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they proclaim.|יֹאמְר֥וּ\rb*\rb |תַּעֲשֶׂ֑ה\rb* \rb Do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb turn aside|תָס֗וּר\rb* \rb to the right|יָמִ֥ין\rb* \rb or to the left|וּשְׂמֹֽאל׃\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the decision|הַדָּבָ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they declare|יַגִּ֥ידֽוּ\rb* \rb to you.|לְךָ֖\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb But the man|וְהָאִ֞ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb acts|יַעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb presumptuously,|בְזָד֗וֹן\rb* \rb refusing|לְבִלְתִּ֨י\rb* \rb to listen|שְׁמֹ֤עַ\rb* \rb either to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb* \rb who stands|הָעֹמֵ֞ד\rb* \rb there|שָׁם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to serve|לְשָׁ֤רֶת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb or|א֖וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the judge,|הַשֹּׁפֵ֑ט\rb* \rb must be put to death.|וּמֵת֙\rb*\rb |הָאִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb You must purge|וּבִֽעַרְתָּ֥\rb* \rb the evil|הָרָ֖ע\rb* \rb from Israel.|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 13 \rb Then all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb will hear|יִשְׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb and be afraid,|וְיִרָ֑אוּ\rb* \rb and will no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb longer|עֽוֹד׃ס\rb* \rb behave arrogantly.|יְזִיד֖וּן\rb*
\s1 Guidelines for a King
\r \ref 1 Samuel 8:1–9|1SA 8:1-9\ref*)
\p \v 14 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you enter|תָבֹ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb you|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and have taken possession of it|וִֽירִשְׁתָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb and settled|וְיָשַׁ֣בְתָּה\rb* \rb in it,|בָּ֑הּ\rb* \rb and you say,|וְאָמַרְתָּ֗\rb* \rb “Let us set|אָשִׂ֤ימָה\rb* \rb a king|מֶ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb over us|עָלַי֙\rb* \rb like all|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb around us,”|סְבִיבֹתָֽי׃\rb* \v 15 \rb you are to appoint|שׂ֣וֹם\rb* \rb over yourselves|עָלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb shall choose.|יִבְחַ֛ר\rb* \rb Appoint|תָּשִׂ֤ים\rb* \rb a king|מֶ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb from among|מִקֶּ֣רֶב\rb* \rb your brothers;|אַחֶ֗יךָ\rb*\rb |תָּשִׂ֤ים\rb* \rb you are not|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |תוּכַ֗ל\rb* \rb to set|לָתֵ֤ת\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb over yourselves|עָלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb a foreigner|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |נָכְרִ֔י\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb is|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb one of your brothers.|אָחִ֖יךָ\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb But|רַק֮\rb* \rb the king must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb acquire many|יַרְבֶּה־\rb* \rb horses|סוּסִים֒\rb* \rb for himself|לּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb or|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb send the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb back|יָשִׁ֤יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יְמָה\rb* \rb to|לְמַ֖עַן\rb* \rb acquire more|הַרְבּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb horses,|ס֑וּס\rb* \rb for the LORD|וַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb has said,|אָמַ֣ר\rb*\rb |לָכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb ‘You are|תֹסִפ֗וּן\rb* \rb never|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb to go back|לָשׁ֛וּב\rb* \rb that|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb way|בַּדֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb again.’|עֽוֹד׃\rb* \v 17 \rb He must not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb take many|יַרְבֶּה־\rb* \rb wives|נָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb for himself,|לּוֹ֙\rb* \rb lest|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb his heart|לְבָב֑וֹ\rb* \rb go astray.|יָס֖וּר\rb* \rb He must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb accumulate|יַרְבֶּה־\rb* \rb for himself|לּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb large amounts|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb of silver|וְכֶ֣סֶף\rb* \rb and gold.|וְזָהָ֔ב\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb |וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb When he is seated|כְשִׁבְתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb his royal|מַמְלַכְתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb throne,|כִּסֵּ֣א\rb* \rb he must write|וְכָ֨תַב\rb* \rb for himself|ל֜וֹ\rb* \rb a copy|מִשְׁנֵ֨ה\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּאת֙\rb* \rb instruction|הַתּוֹרָ֤ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb a scroll|סֵ֔פֶר\rb* \rb in the presence|מִלִּפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Levitical|הַלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb* \rb priests.|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \v 19 \rb It is to remain|וְהָיְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb with him,|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and he is to read|וְקָ֥רָא\rb* \rb from it|ב֖וֹ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of his life,|חַיָּ֑יו\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb he may learn|יִלְמַ֗ד\rb* \rb to fear|לְיִרְאָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָ֔יו\rb* \rb by carefully observing|לִ֠שְׁמֹר\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֞י\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֛את\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb instruction|הַתּוֹרָ֥ה\rb* \rb and these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb statutes.|הַחֻקִּ֥ים\rb*\rb |לַעֲשֹׂתָֽם׃\rb* \v 20 \rb Then his heart|לְבָבוֹ֙\rb* \rb will not|לְבִלְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb be exalted|רוּם־\rb* \rb above|מִן־\rb* \rb his countrymen,|מֵֽאֶחָ֔יו\rb* \rb and he will not|וּלְבִלְתִּ֛י\rb* \rb turn aside|ס֥וּר\rb* \rb from the commandment,|הַמִּצְוָ֖ה\rb* \rb to the right|יָמִ֣ין\rb* \rb or to the left,|וּשְׂמֹ֑אול\rb* \rb in order that|לְמַעַן֩\rb* \rb he|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb may reign|יַאֲרִ֨יךְ\rb* \rb many years|יָמִ֧ים\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb his kingdom|מַמְלַכְתּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb in|בְּקֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*
\c 18
\s1 Provision for Priests and Levites
\r \ref 1 Corinthians 9:1–18|1CO 9:1-18\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb The Levitical|הַלְוִיִּ֜ם\rb* \rb priests—|לַכֹּהֲנִ֨ים\rb*  \rb indeed the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb tribe|שֵׁ֧בֶט\rb* \rb of Levi—|לֵוִ֛י\rb*  \rb shall have|יִ֠הְיֶה\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb portion|חֵ֥לֶק\rb* \rb or inheritance|וְנַחֲלָ֖ה\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb They are to eat|יֹאכֵלֽוּן׃\rb* \rb the food offerings|אִשֵּׁ֧י\rb* \rb to the LORD;|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb that is their inheritance.|וְנַחֲלָת֖וֹ\rb* \v 2 \rb Although they have|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb inheritance|וְנַחֲלָ֥ה\rb* \rb among|בְּקֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb their brothers,|אֶחָ֑יו\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb is their inheritance,|נַחֲלָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb He promised|דִּבֶּר־\rb* \rb them.|לֽוֹ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb This|וְזֶ֡ה\rb* \rb shall be|יִהְיֶה֩\rb* \rb the priests’|הַכֹּהֲנִ֜ים\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb share|מִשְׁפַּ֨ט\rb* \rb from the people|הָעָ֗ם\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb who offer|זֹבְחֵ֥י\rb* \rb a sacrifice,|הַזֶּ֖בַח\rb* \rb whether|אִם־\rb* \rb a bull|שׁ֣וֹר\rb* \rb or|אִם־\rb* \rb a sheep:|שֶׂ֑ה\rb* \rb the priests|לַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb are to be given|וְנָתַן֙\rb* \rb the shoulder,|הַזְּרֹ֥עַ\rb* \rb the jowls,|וְהַלְּחָיַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and the stomach.|וְהַקֵּבָֽה׃\rb* \v 4 \rb You are to give|תִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb them|לּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb the firstfruits|רֵאשִׁ֨ית\rb* \rb of your grain,|דְּגָֽנְךָ֜\rb* \rb new wine,|תִּֽירֹשְׁךָ֣\rb* \rb and oil,|וְיִצְהָרֶ֗ךָ\rb* \rb and the first|וְרֵאשִׁ֛ית\rb* \rb wool sheared|גֵּ֥ז\rb* \rb from your flock.|צֹאנְךָ֖\rb* \v 5 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb has chosen|בָּחַ֛ר\rb* \rb Levi|ב֗וֹ\rb* \rb and his sons|וּבָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb out of all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb your tribes|שְׁבָטֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb to stand|לַעֲמֹ֨ד\rb* \rb and minister|לְשָׁרֵ֧ת\rb* \rb in His|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |ה֥וּא\rb* \rb name|בְּשֵׁם־\rb* \rb for all|כָּל־\rb* \rb time.|הַיָּמִֽים׃ס\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb Now if|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb a Levite|הַלֵּוִ֜י\rb* \rb moves|יָבֹ֨א\rb* \rb from any|מֵאַחַ֤ד\rb* \rb town|שְׁעָרֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |מִכָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb of residence|גָּ֣ר\rb* \rb throughout|שָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and comes|וּבָא֙\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb earnestness|אַוַּ֣ת\rb*\rb |נַפְשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb will choose,|יִבְחַ֥ר\rb* \v 7 \rb then he shall serve|וְשֵׁרֵ֕ת\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָ֑יו\rb* \rb like all|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb his fellow|אֶחָיו֙\rb* \rb Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb who stand|הָעֹמְדִ֥ים\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 8 \rb They shall eat|יֹאכֵ֑לוּ\rb* \rb equal portions,|חֵ֥לֶק\rb*\rb |כְּחֵ֖לֶק\rb* \rb even though|לְבַ֥ד\rb* \rb he has received money from|עַל־\rb* \rb the sale|מִמְכָּרָ֖יו\rb* \rb of his father’s estate.|הָאָבֽוֹת׃ס\rb*
\s1 Sorcery Forbidden
\r \ref Acts 8:9–25|ACT 8:9-25\ref*)
\p \v 9 \rb When|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb enter|בָּ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb you,|לָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb do not|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |תִלְמַ֣ד\rb* \rb imitate|לַעֲשׂ֔וֹת\rb* \rb the detestable ways|כְּתוֹעֲבֹ֖ת\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֥ם\rb* \rb there.|הָהֵֽם׃\rb* \v 10 \rb Let no one|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb be found|יִמָּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb among you|בְךָ֔\rb* \rb who sacrifices|מַעֲבִ֥יר\rb* \rb his son|בְּנֽוֹ־\rb* \rb or daughter|וּבִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb in the fire,|בָּאֵ֑שׁ\rb*\f + \fr 18:10 \ft Literally \fqa makes his son or his daughter pass through the fire\f* \rb practices divination|קְסָמִ֔ים\rb*\rb |קֹסֵ֣ם\rb* \rb or conjury,|מְעוֹנֵ֥ן\rb* \rb interprets omens,|וּמְנַחֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb practices sorcery,|וּמְכַשֵּֽׁף׃\rb* \v 11 \rb casts spells,|וְחֹבֵ֖ר\rb*\rb |חָ֑בֶר\rb* \rb consults|וְשֹׁאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb a medium|אוֹב֙\rb* \rb or spiritist,|וְיִדְּעֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb or inquires|וְדֹרֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb of|אֶל־\rb* \rb the dead.|הַמֵּתִֽים׃\rb* \v 12 \rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb For whoever|כָּל־\rb* \rb does|עֹ֣שֵׂה\rb* \rb these things|אֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb is detestable|תוֹעֲבַ֥ת\rb* \rb to the LORD.|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb And because|וּבִגְלַל֙\rb* \rb of these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb detestable things,|הַתּוֹעֵבֹ֣ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb is driving out|מוֹרִ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb the nations before you.|מִפָּנֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb You must be|תִּֽהְיֶ֔ה\rb* \rb blameless|תָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb before|עִ֖ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃ס\rb* \v 14 \rb Though|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb nations,|הַגּוֹיִ֣ם\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb will dispossess,|יוֹרֵ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb listen|יִשְׁמָ֑עוּ\rb*\rb |וְאַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb conjurers|מְעֹנְנִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and diviners,|קֹסְמִ֖ים\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb has not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb permitted you|נָ֛תַן\rb* \rb to do so.|כֵ֔ן\rb*
\s1 A Prophet Like Moses
\r \ref Acts 3:11–26|ACT 3:11-26\ref*)
\p \v 15 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb will raise up|יָקִ֥ים\rb* \rb for you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb a prophet|נָבִ֨יא\rb* \rb like me|כָּמֹ֔נִי\rb* \rb from among|מִקִּרְבְּךָ֤\rb* \rb your brothers.|מֵאַחֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb You must listen|תִּשְׁמָעֽוּן׃\rb* \rb to him.|אֵלָ֖יו\rb*\f + \fr 18:15 \ft Cited in \ref Acts 3:22|ACT 3:22\ref*\f* \v 16 \rb This is what|כְּכֹ֨ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you asked|שָׁאַ֜לְתָּ\rb* \rb of|מֵעִ֨ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb at Horeb|בְּחֹרֵ֔ב\rb*\f + \fr 18:16 \ft That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai\f* \rb on the day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb of the assembly,|הַקָּהָ֖ל\rb* \rb when you said,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Let us not|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |אֹסֵ֗ף\rb* \rb hear|לִשְׁמֹ֙עַ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the voice|קוֹל֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהָ֔י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb or see|אֶרְאֶ֥ה\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֛את\rb* \rb great|הַגְּדֹלָ֥ה\rb* \rb fire|הָאֵ֨שׁ\rb* \rb anymore,|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb so that we will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb die!”|אָמֽוּת׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלָ֑י\rb* \rb “They have spoken|דִּבֵּֽרוּ׃\rb* \rb well.|הֵיטִ֖יבוּ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \v 18 \rb I will raise up|אָקִ֥ים\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb for them a prophet|נָבִ֨יא\rb* \rb like you|כָּמ֑וֹךָ\rb* \rb from among|מִקֶּ֥רֶב\rb* \rb their brothers.|אֲחֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb I will put|וְנָתַתִּ֤י\rb* \rb My words|דְבָרַי֙\rb* \rb in his mouth,|בְּפִ֔יו\rb* \rb and he will tell|וְדִבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I command him.|אֲצַוֶּֽנּוּ׃\rb* \v 19 \rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb And I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb will hold accountable|אֶדְרֹ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵעִמּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb anyone|הָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb does not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb listen|יִשְׁמַע֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb My words|דְּבָרַ֔י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the prophet speaks|יְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb in My name.|בִּשְׁמִ֑י\rb*\f + \fr 18:19 \ft See \ref Acts 3:23|ACT 3:23\ref*.\f* \v 20 \rb But|אַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb if any prophet|הַנָּבִ֡יא\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb dares|יָזִיד֩\rb* \rb to speak|לְדַבֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb a message|דָּבָ֜ר\rb* \rb in My name|בִּשְׁמִ֗י\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb commanded him|צִוִּיתִיו֙\rb* \rb to speak,|לְדַבֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb or|וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb to speak|יְדַבֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb of other|אֲחֵרִ֑ים\rb* \rb gods,|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb that|הַהֽוּא׃\rb* \rb prophet|הַנָּבִ֥יא\rb* \rb must be put to death.”|וּמֵ֖ת\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb |וְכִ֥י\rb* \rb You may ask|תֹאמַ֖ר\rb* \rb in your heart,|בִּלְבָבֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb “How|אֵיכָה֙\rb* \rb can we recognize|נֵדַ֣ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a message|הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has not|לֹא־\rb* \rb spoken?”|דִבְּר֖וֹ\rb* \v 22 \rb When|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb a prophet|הַנָּבִ֜יא\rb* \rb speaks|יְדַבֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and the message|הַדָּבָר֙\rb* \rb does not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb come to pass|יִהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb come true,|יָב֔וֹא\rb* \rb that|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb is a message|הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb has not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb spoken.|דִבְּר֖וֹ\rb* \rb The prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb* \rb has spoken|דִּבְּר֣וֹ\rb* \rb presumptuously.|בְּזָדוֹן֙\rb* \rb Do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb be afraid|תָג֖וּר\rb* \rb of him.|מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃ס\rb*
\c 19
\s1 Cities of Refuge
\r \ref Numbers 35:9–34|NUM 35:9-34\ref*; \ref Deuteronomy 4:41–43|DEU 4:41-43\ref*; \ref Joshua 20:1–9|JOS 20:1-9\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has cut off|יַכְרִ֞ית\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb whose land|אַרְצָ֑ם\rb* \rb He|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you,|לְךָ֖\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and when you have driven them out|וִֽירִשְׁתָּ֕ם\rb* \rb and settled|וְיָשַׁבְתָּ֥\rb* \rb in their cities|בְעָרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and houses,|וּבְבָתֵּיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 2 \rb then you are to set apart|תַּבְדִּ֣יל\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb three|שָׁל֥וֹשׁ\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb within|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the land|אַרְצְךָ֔\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb to possess.|לְרִשְׁתָּֽהּ׃\rb* \v 3 \rb You are to build|תָּכִ֣ין\rb* \rb roads|הַדֶּרֶךְ֒\rb* \rb for yourselves|לְךָ֮\rb*\f + \fr 19:3 \ft Or \fqa You are to survey the way\f* \rb and divide into three regions|וְשִׁלַּשְׁתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb the land|אַרְצְךָ֔\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֕ה\rb* \rb is giving you as an inheritance,|יַנְחִֽילְךָ֖\rb* \rb so that any|כָּל־\rb* \rb manslayer|רֹצֵֽחַ׃\rb* \rb can flee|לָנ֥וּס\rb* \rb to these cities.|שָׁ֖מָּה\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Now this|וְזֶה֙\rb* \rb is the situation|דְּבַ֣ר\rb* \rb regarding the manslayer|הָרֹצֵ֔חַ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb flees|יָנ֥וּס\rb* \rb to one of these cities|שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb to save his life,|וָחָ֑י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb having killed|יַכֶּ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his neighbor|רֵעֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb accidentally,|בִּבְלִי־\rb*\rb |דַ֔עַת\rb*\rb |וְה֛וּא\rb* \rb without|לֹא־\rb* \rb intending to harm|שֹׂנֵ֥א\rb* \rb him:|ל֖וֹ\rb*\rb |מִתְּמֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |שִׁלְשֹֽׁם׃\rb* \v 5 \rb If|וַאֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb he goes|יָבֹ֨א\rb* \rb into the forest|בַיַּעַר֮\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb his neighbor|רֵעֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb to cut|לַחְטֹ֣ב\rb* \rb timber|עֵצִים֒\rb*\rb |יָד֤וֹ\rb* \rb and swings|וְנִדְּחָ֨ה\rb* \rb his axe|בַגַּרְזֶן֙\rb* \rb to chop down|לִכְרֹ֣ת\rb* \rb a tree,|הָעֵ֔ץ\rb* \rb but the blade flies off|וְנָשַׁ֤ל\rb*\rb |הַבַּרְזֶל֙\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the handle|הָעֵ֔ץ\rb* \rb and strikes|וּמָצָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and kills|וָמֵ֑ת\rb* \rb his neighbor,|רֵעֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb he|ה֗וּא\rb* \rb may flee|יָנ֛וּס\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֥ת\rb* \rb of these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb cities|הֶעָרִים־\rb* \rb to save his life.|וָחָֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb Otherwise,|פֶּן־\rb* \rb the avenger|גֹּאֵ֨ל\rb* \rb of blood|הַדָּ֜ם\rb* \rb might pursue|יִרְדֹּף֩\rb* \rb the manslayer|הָרֹצֵ֗חַ\rb* \rb in a rage,|לְבָבוֹ֒\rb*\rb |כִּי־\rb*\rb |יֵחַם֮\rb* \rb overtake him|וְהִשִּׂיג֛וֹ\rb* \rb if|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the distance|הַדֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb is great,|יִרְבֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb and strike him|וְהִכָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb dead|נָ֑פֶשׁ\rb* \rb though he|וְלוֹ֙\rb* \rb did not|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb deserve|מִשְׁפַּט־\rb* \rb to die,|מָ֔וֶת\rb* \rb since|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb he|ה֛וּא\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb intend any harm.|שֹׂנֵ֥א\rb*\rb |מִתְּמ֥וֹל\rb*\rb |שִׁלְשֽׁוֹם׃\rb* \v 7 \rb This is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb am commanding|מְצַוְּךָ֖\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb you to set apart|תַּבְדִּ֥יל\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָֽךְ׃ס\rb* \rb three|שָׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb cities.|עָרִ֖ים\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb And if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb enlarges|יַרְחִ֞יב\rb* \rb your territory,|גְּבֻ֣לְךָ֔\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He swore|נִשְׁבַּ֖ע\rb* \rb to your fathers,|לַאֲבֹתֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb and gives|וְנָ֤תַן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He promised|דִּבֶּ֖ר\rb*\rb |לָתֵ֥ת\rb* \rb them,|לַאֲבֹתֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 9 \rb and if|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you carefully keep|תִשְׁמֹר֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |לַעֲשֹׂתָ֗הּ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הַזֹּ֜את\rb* \rb commandments|הַמִּצְוָ֨ה\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb am giving you|מְצַוְּךָ֮\rb* \rb today,|הַיּוֹם֒\rb* \rb loving|לְאַהֲבָ֞ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb and walking|וְלָלֶ֥כֶת\rb* \rb in His ways|בִּדְרָכָ֖יו\rb* \rb at all times,|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֑ים\rb* \rb then you are to add|וְיָסַפְתָּ֨\rb* \rb three|שָׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb more|עוֹד֙\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb three.|הַשָּׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Thus innocent|נָקִ֔י\rb* \rb blood|דָּ֣ם\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb be shed|יִשָּׁפֵךְ֙\rb* \rb in|בְּקֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb the land|אַרְצְךָ֔\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb as an inheritance,|נַחֲלָ֑ה\rb* \rb so that you will not be|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb guilty of bloodshed.|דָּמִֽים׃ס\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb If, however,|וְכִֽי־\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a man|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb hates|שֹׂנֵ֣א\rb* \rb his neighbor|לְרֵעֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb and lies in wait,|וְאָ֤רַב\rb* \rb attacks|וְקָ֣ם\rb* \rb him|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and kills him,|וְהִכָּ֥הוּ\rb*\rb |נֶ֖פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |וָמֵ֑ת\rb* \rb and then flees|וְנָ֕ס\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb of these|הָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb cities,|הֶעָרִ֥ים\rb* \v 12 \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of his city|עִיר֔וֹ\rb* \rb must send for him,|וְשָֽׁלְחוּ֙\rb* \rb bring|וְלָקְח֥וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb back,|מִשָּׁ֑ם\rb* \rb and hand him over to|וְנָתְנ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֗וֹ\rb*\rb |בְּיַ֛ד\rb* \rb the avenger|גֹּאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb of blood|הַדָּ֖ם\rb* \rb to die.|וָמֵֽת׃\rb* \v 13 \rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb You must show him no pity.|תָח֥וֹס\rb*\rb |עָלָ֑יו\rb*\rb |עֵֽינְךָ֖\rb* \rb You are to purge|וּבִֽעַרְתָּ֧\rb* \rb from Israel|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb the guilt of shedding innocent|הַנָּקִ֛י\rb* \rb blood,|דַֽם־\rb* \rb that it may go well|וְט֥וֹב\rb* \rb with you.|לָֽךְ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb You must not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb move|תַסִּיג֙\rb* \rb your neighbor’s|רֵֽעֲךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb boundary marker,|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb which was set up|גָּבְל֖וּ\rb* \rb by your ancestors|רִאשֹׁנִ֑ים\rb* \rb to mark the inheritance|בְּנַחֲלָֽתְךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you shall receive|תִּנְחַ֔ל\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֕רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb to possess.|לְרִשְׁתָּֽהּ׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Testimony of Two or Three Witnesses
\r \ref Matthew 18:15–20|MAT 18:15-20\ref*)
\p \v 15 \rb A lone|אֶחָ֜ד\rb* \rb witness|עֵ֨ד\rb* \rb is not sufficient|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to establish|יָקוּם֩\rb* \rb any|לְכָל־\rb* \rb wrongdoing|עָוֺן֙\rb* \rb or|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb sin|חַטָּ֔את\rb* \rb against a man,|בְּאִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb regardless of what|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb offense|חֵ֖טְא\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he may have committed.|יֶֽחֱטָ֑א\rb* \rb A matter|דָּבָֽר׃\rb* \rb must be established|יָק֥וּם\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the testimony|פִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb of two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb or|א֛וֹ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |פִּ֥י\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָֽׁה־\rb*\rb |עֵדִ֖ים\rb* \rb witnesses.|עֵדִ֗ים\rb*\f + \fr 19:15 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 18:16|MAT 18:16\ref* and 2 Corinthians 13:1\f*
\p \v 16 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |יָק֥וּם\rb* \rb a false|חָמָ֖ס\rb* \rb witness|עֵד־\rb* \rb testifies|לַעֲנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb against|בּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb someone,|בְּאִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb accusing him of a crime,|סָרָֽה׃\rb* \v 17 \rb both|שְׁנֵֽי־\rb* \rb parties|הָאֲנָשִׁ֛ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb to the dispute|הָרִ֖יב\rb* \rb must stand|וְעָמְד֧וּ\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb and judges|וְהַשֹּׁ֣פְטִ֔ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb are in office|יִהְי֖וּ\rb* \rb at that|הָהֵֽם׃\rb* \rb time.|בַּיָּמִ֥ים\rb* \v 18 \rb The judges|הַשֹּׁפְטִ֖ים\rb* \rb shall investigate|וְדָרְשׁ֥וּ\rb* \rb thoroughly,|הֵיטֵ֑ב\rb* \rb and if|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb the witness|עֵֽד־\rb* \rb is proven to be a liar|שֶׁ֙קֶר֙\rb*\rb |הָעֵ֔ד\rb* \rb who has falsely|שֶׁ֖קֶר\rb* \rb accused|עָנָ֥ה\rb* \rb his brother,|בְאָחִֽיו׃\rb* \v 19 \rb you must do|וַעֲשִׂ֣יתֶם\rb* \rb to him|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he intended|זָמַ֖ם\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb to his brother.|לְאָחִ֑יו\rb* \rb So you must purge|וּבִֽעַרְתָּ֥\rb* \rb the evil|הָרָ֖ע\rb* \rb from among you.|מִקִּרְבֶּֽךָ׃\rb*\f + \fr 19:19 \ft Cited in \ref 1 Corinthians 5:13|1CO 5:13\ref*\f* \v 20 \rb Then the rest of the people|וְהַנִּשְׁאָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb will hear|יִשְׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb and be afraid,|וְיִרָ֑אוּ\rb* \rb and they will never|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb again|יֹסִ֨פוּ\rb*\rb |ע֗וֹד\rb* \rb do|לַעֲשׂ֜וֹת\rb* \rb anything|כַּדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb so|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb evil|הָרָ֛ע\rb* \rb among you.|בְּקִרְבֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \v 21 \rb You must show no pity:|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |תָח֖וֹס\rb*\rb |עֵינֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb life|נֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb* \rb for life,|בְּנֶ֗פֶשׁ\rb* \rb eye|עַ֤יִן\rb* \rb for eye,|בְּעַ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb tooth|שֵׁ֣ן\rb* \rb for tooth,|בְּשֵׁ֔ן\rb*\f + \fr 19:21 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 5:38|MAT 5:38\ref*\f* \rb hand|יָ֥ד\rb* \rb for hand,|בְּיָ֖ד\rb* \rb and foot|רֶ֥גֶל\rb* \rb for foot.|בְּרָֽגֶל׃ס\rb*
\c 20
\s1 Laws of Warfare
\p \v 1 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you go out|תֵצֵ֨א\rb* \rb to war|לַמִּלְחָמָ֜ה\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb your enemies|אֹיְבֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb and see|וְֽרָאִ֜יתָ\rb* \rb horses,|ס֤וּס\rb* \rb chariots,|וָרֶ֙כֶב֙\rb* \rb and an army|עַ֚ם\rb* \rb larger|רַ֣ב\rb* \rb than yours,|מִמְּךָ֔\rb* \rb do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be afraid|תִירָ֖א\rb* \rb of them;|מֵהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb who brought you|הַמַּֽעַלְךָ֖\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb is with you.|עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb* \v 2 \rb When you are about to|וְהָיָ֕ה\rb* \rb go|כְּקָֽרָבְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb battle,|הַמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb is to come forward|וְנִגַּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb and address|וְדִבֶּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the army,|הָעָֽם׃\rb* \v 3 \rb saying|וְאָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb “Hear,|שְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb O Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֛וֹם\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֨ם\rb* \rb are going|קְרֵבִ֥ים\rb* \rb into battle|לַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb your enemies.|אֹיְבֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be fainthearted|יֵרַ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |לְבַבְכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb or|אַל־\rb* \rb afraid;|תִּֽירְא֧וּ\rb* \rb do not|וְאַֽל־\rb* \rb be alarmed|תַּחְפְּז֛וּ\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb or terrified|תַּֽעַרְצ֖וּ\rb* \rb because of them.|מִפְּנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 4 \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb goes|הַהֹלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵ֥ם\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb your enemies,|אֹיְבֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to give you the victory.”|לְהוֹשִׁ֥יעַ\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Furthermore, the officers|הַשֹּֽׁטְרִים֮\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb are to address|וְדִבְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb the army,|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹר֒\rb* \rb “Has any|מִֽי־\rb* \rb man|הָאִ֞ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb built|בָּנָ֤ה\rb* \rb a new|חָדָשׁ֙\rb* \rb house|בַֽיִת־\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb dedicated it?|חֲנָכ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Let him return|יֵלֵ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |וְיָשֹׁ֣ב\rb* \rb home,|לְבֵית֑וֹ\rb* \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb he may die|יָמוּת֙\rb* \rb in battle|בַּמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb and another|אַחֵ֖ר\rb* \rb man|וְאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb dedicate it.|יַחְנְכֶֽנּוּ׃\rb* \v 6 \rb Has any|וּמִֽי־\rb* \rb man|הָאִ֞ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb planted|נָטַ֥ע\rb* \rb a vineyard|כֶּ֙רֶם֙\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb begun to enjoy its fruit?|חִלְּל֔וֹ\rb* \rb Let him return|יֵלֵ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |וְיָשֹׁ֣ב\rb* \rb home,|לְבֵית֑וֹ\rb* \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb he may die|יָמוּת֙\rb* \rb in battle|בַּמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb and another|אַחֵ֖ר\rb* \rb man|וְאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb enjoy its fruit.|יְחַלְּלֶֽנּוּ׃\rb* \v 7 \rb Has any|וּמִֽי־\rb* \rb man|הָאִ֞ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb become pledged|אֵרַ֤שׂ\rb* \rb to a woman|אִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb married her?|לְקָחָ֔הּ\rb* \rb Let him return|יֵלֵ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |וְיָשֹׁ֣ב\rb* \rb home,|לְבֵית֑וֹ\rb* \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb he may die|יָמוּת֙\rb* \rb in battle|בַּמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb and another|אַחֵ֖ר\rb* \rb man|וְאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb marry her.”|יִקָּחֶֽנָּה׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Then the officers|הַשֹּׁטְרִים֮\rb* \rb shall speak|לְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb further|וְיָסְפ֣וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the army,|הָעָם֒\rb* \rb saying,|וְאָמְר֗וּ\rb* \rb “Is any|מִי־\rb* \rb man|הָאִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb afraid|הַיָּרֵא֙\rb* \rb or fainthearted?|וְרַ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |הַלֵּבָ֔ב\rb* \rb Let him return|יֵלֵ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |וְיָשֹׁ֣ב\rb* \rb home,|לְבֵית֑וֹ\rb* \rb so that the hearts|לְבַ֥ב\rb* \rb of his brothers|אֶחָ֖יו\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb melt|יִמַּ֛ס\rb* \rb like his own.”|כִּלְבָבֽוֹ׃\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb |וְהָיָ֛ה\rb* \rb When the officers|הַשֹּׁטְרִ֖ים\rb* \rb have finished|כְּכַלֹּ֥ת\rb* \rb addressing|לְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the army,|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb they are to appoint|וּפָֽקְד֛וּ\rb*\rb |צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb commanders|שָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb to lead it.|בְּרֹ֥אשׁ\rb*\rb |הָעָֽם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you approach|תִקְרַ֣ב\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb a city|עִ֔יר\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵ֖ם\rb* \rb against it,|עָלֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb you are to make an offer|וְקָרָ֥אתָ\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb of peace.|לְשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb* \v 11 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb they accept|תַּֽעַנְךָ֔\rb* \rb your offer of peace|שָׁל֣וֹם\rb* \rb and open their gates,|וּפָתְחָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb there|הַנִּמְצָא־\rb* \rb will become|יִהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb forced laborers|לָמַ֖ס\rb* \rb to serve|וַעֲבָדֽוּךָ׃\rb* \rb you.|לְךָ֛\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb they refuse|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb to make peace|תַשְׁלִים֙\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and wage|וְעָשְׂתָ֥ה\rb* \rb war|מִלְחָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb against you,|עִמְּךָ֖\rb* \rb lay siege|וְצַרְתָּ֖\rb* \rb to that city.|עָלֶֽיהָּ׃\rb* \v 13 \rb When the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb has delivered it|וּנְתָנָ֛הּ\rb* \rb into your hand,|בְּיָדֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb you must put|וְהִכִּיתָ֥\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb male|זְכוּרָ֖הּ\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb to the sword.|חָֽרֶב׃\rb* \v 14 \rb But|רַ֣ק\rb* \rb the women,|הַ֠נָּשִׁים\rb* \rb children,|וְהַטַּ֨ף\rb* \rb livestock,|וְהַבְּהֵמָ֜ה\rb* \rb and whatever|וְכֹל֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb else is|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb in the city—|בָעִ֛יר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its spoil—|שְׁלָלָ֖הּ\rb* \rb you may take as plunder,|תָּבֹ֣ז\rb* \rb and you shall use|וְאָֽכַלְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the spoil|שְׁלַ֣ל\rb* \rb of your enemies|אֹיְבֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb gives|נָתַ֛ן\rb* \rb you.|לָֽךְ׃\rb* \v 15 \rb This is how|כֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb you are to treat|תַּעֲשֶׂה֙\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the cities|הֶ֣עָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb that are far away|הָרְחֹקֹ֥ת\rb* \rb from you|מִמְּךָ֖\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb and do not|לֹא־\rb*\rb |מֵעָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb belong to the|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb*\rb |הֵֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb nations nearby.|הַגּֽוֹיִם־\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb However,|רַ֗ק\rb* \rb in the cities|מֵעָרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb nations|הָֽעַמִּים֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb as an inheritance,|נַחֲלָ֑ה\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb you must not leave alive|תְחַיֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb anything|כָּל־\rb* \rb that breathes.|נְשָׁמָֽה׃\rb* \v 17 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you must devote them to complete destruction—|הַחֲרֵ֣ם\rb*\f + \fr 20:17 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering.\f*\rb |תַּחֲרִימֵ֗ם\rb* \rb the Hittites,|הַחִתִּ֤י\rb* \rb Amorites,|וְהָאֱמֹרִי֙\rb* \rb Canaanites,|הַכְּנַעֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb Perizzites,|וְהַפְּרִזִּ֔י\rb* \rb Hivites,|הַחִוִּ֖י\rb* \rb and Jebusites—|וְהַיְבוּסִ֑י\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb has commanded you,|צִוְּךָ֖\rb* \v 18 \rb so that|לְמַ֗עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb they cannot|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb teach|יְלַמְּד֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb you to do|לַעֲשׂ֔וֹת\rb* \rb all|כְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb the detestable things|תּֽוֹעֲבֹתָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they do|עָשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb for their gods,|לֵֽאלֹהֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and so cause you to sin|וַחֲטָאתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb against the LORD|לַיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you lay siege|תָצ֣וּר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a city|עִיר֩\rb* \rb for an extended|רַבִּ֜ים\rb* \rb time|יָמִ֨ים\rb* \rb while fighting|לְֽהִלָּחֵ֧ם\rb* \rb against it|עָלֶ֣יהָ\rb* \rb to capture it,|לְתָפְשָׂ֗הּ\rb* \rb you must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb destroy|תַשְׁחִ֤ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its trees|עֵצָהּ֙\rb* \rb by putting|לִנְדֹּ֤חַ\rb* \rb an axe|גַּרְזֶ֔ן\rb* \rb to them,|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb because|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb you can eat their fruit.|תֹאכֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |וְאֹת֖וֹ\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb You must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb cut them down.|תִכְרֹ֑ת\rb*\rb |כִּ֤י\rb* \rb Are the trees|עֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb human,|הָֽאָדָם֙\rb*\rb |לָבֹ֥א\rb*\rb |מִפָּנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb that you should besiege them?|בַּמָּצֽוֹר׃\rb* \v 20 \rb But|רַ֞ק\rb* \rb you may destroy|תַשְׁחִ֖ית\rb* \rb the trees|עֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you know|תֵּדַ֗ע\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb do not|לֹא־\rb*\rb |עֵ֤ץ\rb* \rb produce fruit.|מַאֲכָל֙\rb*\rb |ה֔וּא\rb*\rb |אֹת֥וֹ\rb* \rb Use them|וְכָרָ֑תָּ\rb* \rb to build|וּבָנִ֣יתָ\rb* \rb siege works|מָצ֗וֹר\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |הִ֨וא\rb* \rb is waging|עֹשָׂ֧ה\rb* \rb war|מִלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb against you,|עִמְּךָ֛\rb* \rb until|עַ֥ד\rb* \rb it falls.|רִדְתָּֽהּ׃פ\rb*
\c 21
\s1 Atonement for an Unsolved Murder
\p \v 1 \rb If|כִּי־\rb* \rb one is found|יִמָּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb slain,|חָלָ֗ל\rb* \rb lying|נֹפֵ֖ל\rb* \rb in a field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֑ה\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאֲדָמָה֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֤ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb to possess,|לְרִשְׁתָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb and it is not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb known|נוֹדַ֖ע\rb* \rb who|מִ֥י\rb* \rb killed him,|הִכָּֽהוּ׃\rb* \v 2 \rb your elders|זְקֵנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and judges|וְשֹׁפְטֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb must come out|וְיָצְא֥וּ\rb* \rb and measure the distance|וּמָדְדוּ֙\rb* \rb from the victim|הֶחָלָֽל׃\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the neighboring|סְבִיבֹ֥ת\rb* \rb cities.|הֶ֣עָרִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Then|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵי֩\rb*\rb |הָעִ֨יר\rb*\rb |הַהִ֜וא\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb nearest|הַקְּרֹבָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the victim|הֶחָלָ֑ל\rb* \rb shall take|וְלָֽקְח֡וּ\rb* \rb a heifer|עֶגְלַ֣ת\rb*\rb |בָּקָ֗ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb has never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb been yoked|בְּעֹֽל׃\rb* \rb or used for work,|עֻבַּד֙\rb* \v 4 \rb bring|וְהוֹרִ֡דוּ\rb*\rb |זִקְנֵי֩\rb*\rb |הַהִ֤וא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הָעִ֨יר\rb* \rb the heifer|הָֽעֶגְלָה֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a valley|נַ֣חַל\rb* \rb with running water|אֵיתָ֔ן\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb has not|לֹא־\rb* \rb been plowed|יֵעָבֵ֥ד\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb or sown,|יִזָּרֵ֑עַ\rb* \rb and break its|הָעֶגְלָ֖ה\rb* \rb neck|וְעָֽרְפוּ־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb by the stream.|בַּנָּֽחַל׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb And the priests,|הַכֹּהֲנִים֮\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Levi,|לֵוִי֒\rb* \rb shall come forward,|וְנִגְּשׁ֣וּ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb has chosen them|בָּחַ֞ר\rb* \rb to serve Him|לְשָׁ֣רְת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and pronounce blessings|וּלְבָרֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in His|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb name|בְּשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb and to give a ruling|וְעַל־\rb*\rb |פִּיהֶ֥ם\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb in every|כָּל־\rb* \rb dispute|רִ֥יב\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb* \rb and case of assault.|נָֽגַע׃\rb* \v 6 \rb Then all|וְכֹ֗ל\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵי֙\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֣יר\rb*\rb |הַהִ֔וא\rb* \rb nearest|הַקְּרֹבִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the victim|הֶחָלָ֑ל\rb* \rb shall wash|יִרְחֲצוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their hands|יְדֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb by the stream|בַנָּֽחַל׃\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the heifer|הָעֶגְלָ֖ה\rb* \rb whose neck has been broken,|הָעֲרוּפָ֥ה\rb* \v 7 \rb and they shall declare,|וְעָנ֖וּ\rb*\rb |וְאָמְר֑וּ\rb* \rb “Our hands|יָדֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb shed|שָׁפְכָה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb blood,|הַדָּ֣ם\rb* \rb nor did|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb our eyes|וְעֵינֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb see it.|רָאֽוּ׃\rb* \v 8 \rb Accept this atonement,|כַּפֵּר֩\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb for Your people|לְעַמְּךָ֨\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb You have redeemed,|פָּדִ֙יתָ֙\rb* \rb and do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb hold|תִּתֵּן֙\rb* \rb the shedding of innocent|נָקִ֔י\rb* \rb blood|דָּ֣ם\rb* \rb against|בְּקֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb them.”|עַמְּךָ֣\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֖ם\rb*
\p \rb And the bloodshed|הַדָּֽם׃\rb* \rb will be atoned for.|וְנִכַּפֵּ֥ר\rb* \v 9 \rb So you|וְאַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb shall purge|תְּבַעֵ֛ר\rb* \rb from among you|מִקִּרְבֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb the guilt of shedding innocent|הַנָּקִ֖י\rb* \rb blood,|הַדָּ֥ם\rb* \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have done|תַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb what is right|הַיָּשָׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*
\s1 Marrying a Captive Woman
\p \v 10 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you go|תֵצֵ֥א\rb* \rb to war|לַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb your enemies|אֹיְבֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb delivers them|וּנְתָנ֞וֹ\rb* \rb into your hand|בְּיָדֶ֖ךָ\rb* \rb and you take them|וְשָׁבִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb captive,|שִׁבְיֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 11 \rb if you see|וְרָאִיתָ֙\rb* \rb a beautiful|יְפַת־\rb*\rb |תֹּ֑אַר\rb* \rb woman|אֵ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb among them,|בַּשִּׁבְיָ֔ה\rb* \rb and you desire|וְחָשַׁקְתָּ֣\rb* \rb her|בָ֔הּ\rb* \rb and want to take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֥\rb* \rb her|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb as your wife,|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb* \v 12 \rb then you shall bring her|וַהֲבֵאתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb*\rb |תּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb your house.|בֵּיתֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb She must shave|וְגִלְּחָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her head,|רֹאשָׁ֔הּ\rb* \rb trim|וְעָשְׂתָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her nails,|צִפָּרְנֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \v 13 \rb and put aside|וְהֵסִ֩ירָה֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the clothing|שִׂמְלַ֨ת\rb* \rb of her captivity.|שִׁבְיָ֜הּ\rb*
\p \rb After|וְאַ֨חַר\rb* \rb she has lived|וְיָֽשְׁבָה֙\rb* \rb in your house|בְּבֵיתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb a full month|יֶ֣רַח\rb*\rb |יָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb and mourned|וּבָֽכְתָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her father|אָבִ֥יהָ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and mother,|אִמָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb you may have relations with|תָּב֤וֹא\rb* \rb her|אֵלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb and be her husband,|וּבְעַלְתָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb and she shall be|וְהָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb your wife.|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb* \v 14 \rb And|וְהָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you are not|לֹ֧א\rb* \rb pleased|חָפַ֣צְתָּ\rb* \rb with her,|בָּ֗הּ\rb* \rb you are to let her go|וְשִׁלַּחְתָּהּ֙\rb* \rb wherever she wishes.|לְנַפְשָׁ֔הּ\rb* \rb But you must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb sell her|וּמָכֹ֥ר\rb*\rb |תִמְכְּרֶ֖נָּה\rb* \rb for money|בַּכָּ֑סֶף\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb or treat her as a slave,|תִתְעַמֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb since|תַּ֖חַת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have dishonored her.|עִנִּיתָֽהּ׃ס\rb*
\s1 Inheritance Rights of the Firstborn
\p \v 15 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a man|לְאִ֜ישׁ\rb* \rb has|תִהְיֶ֨יןָ\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb wives,|נָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb one|הָאַחַ֤ת\rb* \rb beloved|אֲהוּבָה֙\rb* \rb and the other|וְהָאַחַ֣ת\rb* \rb unloved,|שְׂנוּאָ֔ה\rb* \rb and both|הָאֲהוּבָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְהַשְּׂנוּאָ֑ה\rb* \rb bear|וְיָֽלְדוּ־\rb* \rb him|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb sons,|בָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb but the unloved|לַשְּׂנִיאָֽה׃\rb* \rb wife has|וְהָיָ֛ה\rb* \rb the firstborn|הַבְּכ֖וֹר\rb* \rb son,|הַבֵּ֥ן\rb* \v 16 \rb when|בְּיוֹם֙\rb* \rb that man|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb assigns his inheritance|הַנְחִיל֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to his sons|בָּנָ֔יו\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb he must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb appoint|יוּכַ֗ל\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of the beloved wife|הָ֣אֲהוּבָ֔ה\rb* \rb as|עַל־\rb* \rb the firstborn|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb over|בֶן־\rb* \rb the son|לְבַכֵּר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of the unloved wife.|הַשְּׂנוּאָ֖ה\rb*\rb |הַבְּכֹֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Instead,|כִּי֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he must acknowledge|יַכִּ֗יר\rb* \rb the firstborn,|הַבְּכֹ֨ר\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of his unloved wife,|הַשְּׂנוּאָ֜ה\rb* \rb by giving|לָ֤תֶת\rb* \rb him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb a double|שְׁנַ֔יִם\rb* \rb portion|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb of all|בְּכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he has.|יִמָּצֵ֖א\rb* \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb that son|הוּא֙\rb* \rb is the firstfruits|רֵאשִׁ֣ית\rb* \rb of his father’s strength;|אֹנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb the right|מִשְׁפַּ֥ט\rb* \rb of the firstborn|הַבְּכֹרָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb belongs to him.|ל֖וֹ\rb*
\s1 A Rebellious Son
\r \ref Luke 15:11–32|LUK 15:11-32\ref*)
\p \v 18 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a man|לְאִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb has|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb a stubborn|סוֹרֵ֣ר\rb* \rb and rebellious|וּמוֹרֶ֔ה\rb* \rb son|בֵּ֚ן\rb* \rb who does not|אֵינֶ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb obey|שֹׁמֵ֔עַ\rb*\rb |בְּק֥וֹל\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb*\rb |וּבְק֣וֹל\rb* \rb and mother|אִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb does not listen|יִשְׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb when disciplined,|וְיסְּר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \v 19 \rb his father|אָבִ֣יו\rb* \rb and mother|וְאִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb are to lay hold|וְתָ֥פְשׂוּ\rb* \rb of him|ב֖וֹ\rb* \rb and bring|וְהוֹצִ֧יאוּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of his city,|עִיר֖וֹ\rb* \rb to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the gate|שַׁ֥עַר\rb* \rb of his hometown,|מְקֹמֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 20 \rb and say|וְאָמְר֞וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the elders,|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עִיר֗וֹ\rb* \rb “This|זֶה֙\rb* \rb son of ours|בְּנֵ֤נוּ\rb* \rb is stubborn|סוֹרֵ֣ר\rb* \rb and rebellious;|וּמֹרֶ֔ה\rb* \rb he does not|אֵינֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb obey us.|שֹׁמֵ֖עַ\rb*\rb |בְּקֹלֵ֑נוּ\rb* \rb He is a glutton|זוֹלֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and a drunkard.”|וְסֹבֵֽא׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb Then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb of his city|עִיר֤וֹ\rb* \rb will stone him|וּ֠רְגָמֻהוּ\rb*\rb |בָֽאֲבָנִים֙\rb* \rb to death.|וָמֵ֔ת\rb* \rb So you must purge|וּבִֽעַרְתָּ֥\rb* \rb the evil|הָרָ֖ע\rb* \rb from among you,|מִקִּרְבֶּ֑ךָ\rb*\f + \fr 21:21 \ft Cited in \ref 1 Corinthians 5:13|1CO 5:13\ref*\f* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb will hear|יִשְׁמְע֥וּ\rb* \rb and be afraid.|וְיִרָֽאוּ׃ס\rb*
\s1 Cursed Is Anyone Hung on a Tree
\p \v 22 \rb If|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb a man|בְאִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb has committed|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb a sin|חֵ֛טְא\rb* \rb worthy|מִשְׁפַּט־\rb* \rb of death,|מָ֖וֶת\rb* \rb and he is executed,|וְהוּמָ֑ת\rb* \rb and you hang|וְתָלִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb his body|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb a tree,|עֵֽץ׃\rb*\f + \fr 21:22 \ft Or \fqa impale his body on a pole\ft ; similarly in verse 23\f* \v 23 \rb you must not leave|לֹא־\rb* \rb the body|נִבְלָת֜וֹ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the tree|הָעֵ֗ץ\rb* \rb overnight,|תָלִ֨ין\rb* \rb but|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you must be sure to bury|קָב֤וֹר\rb*\rb |תִּקְבְּרֶ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb him|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb that day,|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb anyone who is hung on a tree|תָּל֑וּי\rb* \rb is under God’s|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb curse.|קִלְלַ֥ת\rb*\f + \fr 21:23 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa anyone who is hanged is under God’s curse\ft ; cited in \ref Galatians 3:13|GAL 3:13\ref*\f* \rb You must not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb defile|תְטַמֵּא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|אַדְמָ֣תְךָ֔\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb as an inheritance.|נַחֲלָֽה׃ס\rb*
\c 22
\s1 Various Laws
\p \v 1 \rb If you see|תִרְאֶה֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your brother’s|אָחִ֜יךָ\rb* \rb ox|שׁ֨וֹר\rb* \rb or|א֤וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sheep|שֵׂיוֹ֙\rb* \rb straying,|נִדָּחִ֔ים\rb* \rb you must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb ignore it;|וְהִתְעַלַּמְתָּ֖\rb*\f + \fr 22:1 \ft Or \fqa you must not hide yourself\f*\rb |מֵהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb be sure to return it|הָשֵׁ֥ב\rb*\rb |תְּשִׁיבֵ֖ם\rb* \rb to your brother.|לְאָחִֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 2 \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb your brother|אָחִ֛יךָ\rb* \rb does not|לֹ֨א\rb* \rb live near you,|קָר֥וֹב\rb* \rb or if you do not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb know who he is,|יְדַעְתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb you are to take|וַאֲסַפְתּוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the animal|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |תּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb home|בֵּיתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb to remain|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb with you|עִמְּךָ֗\rb* \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb* \rb your brother|אָחִ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb comes seeking it;|דְּרֹ֤שׁ\rb* \rb then you can return it|וַהֲשֵׁבֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb to him.|לֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 3 \rb And you shall do|תַּעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb the same|וְכֵ֧ן\rb* \rb for his donkey,|לַחֲמֹר֗וֹ\rb*\rb |וְכֵ֣ן\rb*\rb |תַּעֲשֶׂה֮\rb* \rb his cloak,|לְשִׂמְלָתוֹ֒\rb*\rb |וְכֵ֣ן\rb*\rb |תַּעֲשֶׂ֜ה\rb* \rb or anything|לְכָל־\rb* \rb your brother|אָחִ֛יךָ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |תֹּאבַ֥ד\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb has lost|אֲבֵדַ֥ת\rb* \rb and you have found.|וּמְצָאתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb You must|תוּכַ֖ל\rb* \rb not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb ignore it.|לְהִתְעַלֵּֽם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb If you see|תִרְאֶה֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your brother’s|אָחִ֜יךָ\rb* \rb donkey|חֲמ֨וֹר\rb* \rb or|א֤וֹ\rb* \rb ox|שׁוֹרוֹ֙\rb* \rb fallen|נֹפְלִ֣ים\rb* \rb on the road,|בַּדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb you must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb ignore it;|וְהִתְעַלַּמְתָּ֖\rb*\rb |מֵהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb you must help him lift it up.|הָקֵ֥ם\rb*\rb |תָּקִ֖ים\rb*\rb |עִמּֽוֹ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb A woman|אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb wear|יִהְיֶ֤ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb men’s|גֶ֙בֶר֙\rb* \rb clothing,|כְלִי־\rb* \rb and a man|גֶּ֖בֶר\rb* \rb must not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb wear|יִלְבַּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb women’s|אִשָּׁ֑ה\rb* \rb clothing,|שִׂמְלַ֣ת\rb* \rb for|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb whoever|כָּל־\rb* \rb does|עֹ֥שֵׂה\rb* \rb these things|אֵֽלֶּה׃פ\rb* \rb is detestable|תוֹעֲבַ֛ת\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb If|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you come across|יִקָּרֵ֣א\rb* \rb a bird’s|צִפּ֣וֹר׀\rb*\rb |לְפָנֶ֡יךָ\rb* \rb nest|קַן־\rb* \rb with chicks|אֶפְרֹחִים֙\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb eggs,|בֵיצִ֔ים\rb* \rb either in a tree|עֵ֣ץ׀\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb along the road,|בַּדֶּ֜רֶךְ\rb*\rb |בְּכָל־\rb* \rb and the mother|וְהָאֵ֤ם\rb* \rb is sitting|רֹבֶ֙צֶת֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the chicks|הָֽאֶפְרֹחִ֔ים\rb* \rb or|א֖וֹ\rb* \rb eggs,|הַבֵּיצִ֑ים\rb* \rb you must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb take|תִקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb the mother|הָאֵ֖ם\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb along with|עַל־\rb* \rb the young.|הַבָּנִֽים׃\rb* \v 7 \rb You may take|תִּֽקַּֽח־\rb* \rb the young,|הַבָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb but be sure to let the mother|הָאֵ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb go,|שַׁלֵּ֤חַ\rb*\rb |תְּשַׁלַּח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb it may be well|יִ֣יטַב\rb* \rb with you|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and that you may prolong|וְהַאֲרַכְתָּ֖\rb* \rb your days.|יָמִֽים׃ס\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb If|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you build|תִבְנֶה֙\rb* \rb a new|חָדָ֔שׁ\rb* \rb house,|בַּ֣יִת\rb* \rb you are to construct|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb* \rb a railing|מַעֲקֶ֖ה\rb* \rb around your roof,|לְגַגֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb so that you do not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb bring|תָשִׂ֤ים\rb* \rb bloodguilt|דָּמִים֙\rb* \rb on your house|בְּבֵיתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb if|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb someone falls|יִפֹּ֥ל\rb*\rb |הַנֹּפֵ֖ל\rb* \rb from it.|מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb plant|תִזְרַ֥ע\rb* \rb your vineyard|כַּרְמְךָ֖\rb* \rb with two types of seed;|כִּלְאָ֑יִם\rb* \rb if you do,|פֶּן־\rb* \rb the entire harvest|הַֽמְלֵאָ֤ה\rb* \rb will be defiled|תִּקְדַּ֗שׁ\rb*\f + \fr 22:9 \ft Or \fqa will be forfeited to the sanctuary\f* — \rb both the crop|הַזֶּ֙רַע֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you plant|תִּזְרָ֔ע\rb* \rb and the fruit|וּתְבוּאַ֖ת\rb* \rb of your vineyard.|הַכָּֽרֶם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb plow|תַחֲרֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb with an ox|בְּשׁוֹר־\rb* \rb and a donkey|וּבַחֲמֹ֖ר\rb* \rb yoked together.|יַחְדָּֽו׃ס\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Do not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb wear|תִלְבַּשׁ֙\rb* \rb clothes|שַֽׁעַטְנֵ֔ז\rb* \rb of wool|צֶ֥מֶר\rb* \rb and linen|וּפִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb woven together.|יַחְדָּֽו׃ס\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb You are to make|תַּעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb tassels|גְּדִלִ֖ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the four|אַרְבַּ֛ע\rb* \rb corners|כַּנְפ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the cloak|כְּסוּתְךָ֖\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you wear.|תְּכַסֶּה־\rb*
\s1 Marriage Violations
\p \v 13 \rb Suppose|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb marries|יִקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb a woman,|אִשָּׁ֑ה\rb* \rb has relations with|וּבָ֥א\rb* \rb her,|אֵלֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb and comes to hate her,|וּשְׂנֵאָֽהּ׃\rb* \v 14 \rb and he then accuses|וְשָׂ֥ם\rb* \rb her|לָהּ֙\rb* \rb of shameful conduct|עֲלִילֹ֣ת\rb*\rb |דְּבָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb and gives her|וְהוֹצִ֥יא\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb a bad|רָ֑ע\rb* \rb name,|שֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb saying,|וְאָמַ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb “I married|לָקַ֔חְתִּי\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּאת֙\rb* \rb woman|הָאִשָּׁ֤ה\rb* \rb and had relations with|וָאֶקְרַ֣ב\rb* \rb her,|אֵלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb but I discovered|מָצָ֥אתִי\rb* \rb she was not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb a virgin.”|בְּתוּלִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb Then the young woman’s|הַנַּעַר\rb* \rb father|אֲבִ֥י\rb* \rb and mother|וְאִמָּ֑הּ\rb*\rb |וְלָקַ֛ח\rb* \rb shall bring|וְהוֹצִ֜יאוּ\rb* \rb the proof of her|הַנַּעַר\rb* \rb virginity|בְּתוּלֵ֧י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb elders|זִקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb at the gate|הַשָּֽׁעְרָה׃\rb* \v 16 \rb and|הַנַּעַר\rb*\rb |אֲבִ֥י\rb* \rb say|וְאָמַ֛ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the elders,|הַזְּקֵנִ֑ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb “I gave|נָתַ֜תִּי\rb* \rb my daughter|בִּתִּ֗י\rb* \rb in marriage|לְאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb to this|הַזֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb man,|לָאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb but he has come to hate her.|וַיִּשְׂנָאֶֽהָ׃\rb* \v 17 \rb And now|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb he|ה֡וּא\rb* \rb has accused her|שָׂם֩\rb* \rb of shameful conduct,|עֲלִילֹ֨ת\rb*\rb |דְּבָרִ֜ים\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb ‘I discovered that|מָצָ֤אתִי\rb* \rb your daughter|לְבִתְּךָ֙\rb* \rb was not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb a virgin.’|בְּתוּלִ֔ים\rb* \rb But here is the proof|וְאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb of her|בִתִּ֑י\rb* \rb virginity.”|בְּתוּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb And they shall spread out|וּפָֽרְשׂוּ֙\rb* \rb the cloth|הַשִּׂמְלָ֔ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb* \rb elders.|זִקְנֵ֥י\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Then the elders|זִקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of that|הַהִ֖וא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb city|הָֽעִיר־\rb* \rb shall take|וְלָֽקְח֛וּ\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb and punish him.|וְיִסְּר֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 19 \rb They are also to fine|וְעָנְשׁ֨וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb a hundred shekels|מֵ֣אָה\rb* \rb of silver|כֶ֗סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 22:19 \fqa 100 shekels \ft is approximately 2.5 pounds or 1.1 kilograms of silver.\f* \rb and give them|וְנָתְנוּ֙\rb* \rb to the young woman’s|הַֽנַּעֲרָ֔ה\rb* \rb father,|לַאֲבִ֣י\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb this man has given|הוֹצִיא֙\rb* \rb a virgin|בְּתוּלַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb a bad|רָ֔ע\rb*\rb |עַ֖ל\rb* \rb name.|שֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb And she shall remain|תִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb his|וְלֽוֹ־\rb* \rb wife;|לְאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb he must not|לֹא־\rb*\rb |יוּכַ֥ל\rb* \rb divorce her|לְשַּׁלְּחָ֖הּ\rb* \rb as|כָּל־\rb* \rb long as he lives.|יָמָֽיו׃ס\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb If, however,|וְאִם־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb accusation|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb is|הָיָ֔ה\rb* \rb true,|אֱמֶ֣ת\rb* \rb and no|לֹא־\rb* \rb proof of the young woman’s|לַנַּעַר׃\rb* \rb virginity|בְתוּלִ֖ים\rb* \rb can be found,|נִמְצְא֥וּ\rb* \v 21 \rb she|הַנַּעַר\rb* \rb shall be brought|וְהוֹצִ֨יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the door|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb of her father’s|אָבִ֗יהָ\rb* \rb house,|בֵּית־\rb* \rb and there the men|אַנְשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb of her city|עִירָ֤הּ\rb* \rb will stone her|וּסְקָלוּהָ֩\rb*\rb |בָּאֲבָנִים֙\rb* \rb to death.|וָמֵ֔תָה\rb* \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb she has committed|עָשְׂתָ֤ה\rb* \rb an outrage|נְבָלָה֙\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb by being promiscuous|לִזְנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb in her father’s|אָבִ֑יהָ\rb* \rb house.|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb So you must purge|וּבִֽעַרְתָּ֥\rb* \rb the evil|הָרָ֖ע\rb* \rb from among you.|מִקִּרְבֶּֽךָ׃ס\rb*\f + \fr 22:21 \ft Here and in verse 24; cited in \ref 1 Corinthians 5:13|1CO 5:13\ref*\f*
\p \v 22 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֜ישׁ\rb* \rb is found|יִמָּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb lying|שֹׁכֵ֣ב׀\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb another man’s|בַּ֗עַל\rb* \rb wife,|אִשָּׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |בְעֻֽלַת־\rb* \rb both|גַּם־\rb*\rb |שְׁנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb who slept|הַשֹּׁכֵ֥ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb her|הָאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb and the woman|וְהָאִשָּׁ֑ה\rb* \rb must die.|וּמֵ֙תוּ֙\rb* \rb You must purge|וּבִֽעַרְתָּ֥\rb* \rb the evil|הָרָ֖ע\rb* \rb from Israel.|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb If|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb there is|יִהְיֶה֙\rb*\rb |נַעַר\rb* \rb a virgin|בְתוּלָ֔ה\rb* \rb pledged in marriage|מְאֹרָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb to a man,|לְאִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb and another man|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb encounters her|וּמְצָאָ֥הּ\rb* \rb in the city|בָּעִ֖יר\rb* \rb and sleeps|וְשָׁכַ֥ב\rb* \rb with her,|עִמָּֽהּ׃\rb* \v 24 \rb you must take both|שְׁנֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb of them out|וְהוֹצֵאתֶ֨ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the gate|שַׁ֣עַר׀\rb* \rb of that|הַהִ֗וא\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb and stone|וּסְקַלְתֶּ֨ם\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֥ם\rb* \rb them|בָּאֲבָנִים֮\rb* \rb to death—|וָמֵתוּ֒\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the young woman|הַנַּעַר\rb* \rb because|עַל־\rb*\rb |דְּבַר֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb she did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb cry out|צָעֲקָ֣ה\rb* \rb in the city,|בָעִ֔יר\rb*\rb |וְאֶ֨ת־\rb* \rb and the man|הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb because|עַל־\rb*\rb |דְּבַ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he has violated|עִנָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his neighbor’s|רֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb wife.|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb So you must purge|וּבִֽעַרְתָּ֥\rb* \rb the evil|הָרָ֖ע\rb* \rb from among you.|מִקִּרְבֶּֽךָ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb But if|וְֽאִם־\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֗ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb encounters|יִמְצָ֣א\rb* \rb a betrothed|הַמְאֹ֣רָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb woman|הַנַּעַר\rb* \rb in the open country,|בַּשָּׂדֶ֞ה\rb* \rb and he|הָאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb overpowers|וְהֶחֱזִֽיק־\rb* \rb her|בָּ֥הּ\rb* \rb and lies|וְשָׁכַ֣ב\rb* \rb with her,|עִמָּ֑הּ\rb* \rb only|לְבַדּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has done this|שָׁכַ֥ב\rb*\rb |עִמָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb must die.|וּמֵ֗ת\rb* \v 26 \rb Do|תַעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb nothing|לֹא־\rb*\rb |דָבָ֔ר\rb* \rb to the young woman,|וְלַנַּעַר\rb* \rb because|כִּ֡י\rb* \rb she|לַנַּעַר\rb* \rb has committed no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb sin|חֵ֣טְא\rb* \rb worthy of death.|מָ֑וֶת\rb* \rb This|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb case|הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb is just like|כַּאֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb one in which a man|אִ֤ישׁ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb attacks|יָק֨וּם\rb* \rb his neighbor|רֵעֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb and murders him.|וּרְצָח֣וֹ\rb*\rb |נֶ֔פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |כֵּ֖ן\rb* \v 27 \rb When|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he found her|מְצָאָ֑הּ\rb* \rb in the field,|בַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb the betrothed|הַמְאֹ֣רָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb woman|הַנַּעַר\rb* \rb cried out,|צָעֲקָ֗ה\rb* \rb but there was no one|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb to save|מוֹשִׁ֖יעַ\rb* \rb her.|לָֽהּ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb encounters|יִמְצָ֣א\rb*\rb |נַעַר\rb* \rb a virgin|בְתוּלָה֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb is not|לֹא־\rb* \rb pledged in marriage,|אֹרָ֔שָׂה\rb* \rb and he seizes her|וּתְפָשָׂ֖הּ\rb* \rb and lies|וְשָׁכַ֣ב\rb* \rb with her,|עִמָּ֑הּ\rb* \rb and they are discovered,|וְנִמְצָֽאוּ׃\rb* \v 29 \rb then the man|הָאִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb who lay|הַשֹּׁכֵ֥ב\rb* \rb with her|עִמָּ֛הּ\rb* \rb must pay|וְ֠נָתַן\rb* \rb the young woman’s|הַנַּעַר\rb* \rb father|לַאֲבִ֥י\rb* \rb fifty shekels|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb of silver,|כָּ֑סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 22:29 \fqa 50 shekels \ft is approximately 1.26 pounds or 569.8 grams of silver.\f* \rb and|וְלֽוֹ־\rb* \rb she must become|תִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb his wife|לְאִשָּׁ֗ה\rb* \rb because|תַּ֚חַת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he has violated her.|עִנָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb He must not|לֹא־\rb*\rb |יוּכַ֥ל\rb* \rb divorce her|שַׁלְּחָ֖ה\rb* \rb as|כָּל־\rb* \rb long as he lives.|יָמָֽיו׃ס\rb*
