\p \v 7 \rb Do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb despise|תְתַעֵ֣ב\rb* \rb an Edomite,|אֲדֹמִ֔י\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he|ה֑וּאס\rb* \rb is your brother.|אָחִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb Do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb despise|תְתַעֵ֣ב\rb* \rb an Egyptian,|מִצְרִ֔י\rb* \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb you lived|הָיִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb as a foreigner|גֵ֖ר\rb* \rb in his land.|בְאַרְצֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 8 \rb The third|שְׁלִישִׁ֑י\rb* \rb generation|דּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb of children|בָּנִ֛ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb born|יִוָּלְד֥וּ\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb may enter|יָבֹ֥א\rb* \rb the assembly|בִּקְהַ֥ל\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*
\s1 Uncleanness in the Camp
\r \ref Leviticus 15:1–12|LEV 15:1-12\ref*)
\p \v 9 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you are encamped|תֵצֵ֥א\rb*\rb |מַחֲנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb your enemies,|אֹיְבֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb then you shall keep yourself|וְנִ֨שְׁמַרְתָּ֔\rb* \rb from every|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb wicked|רָֽע׃\rb* \rb thing.|דָּבָ֥ר\rb* \v 10 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb any man|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb among you|בְךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb becomes|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb unclean|טָה֖וֹר\rb* \rb because of a nocturnal|לָ֑יְלָה\rb* \rb emission,|מִקְּרֵה־\rb* \rb he must leave|וְיָצָא֙\rb* \rb the camp|לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb and stay|יָבֹ֖א\rb* \rb outside.|מִח֣וּץ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |תּ֥וֹךְ\rb*\rb |הַֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃\rb* \v 11 \rb |וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb When evening|עֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb approaches,|לִפְנֽוֹת־\rb* \rb he must wash|יִרְחַ֣ץ\rb* \rb with water,|בַּמָּ֑יִם\rb* \rb and when the sun|הַשֶּׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb* \rb sets|וּכְבֹ֣א\rb* \rb he may return|יָבֹ֖א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |תּ֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the camp.|הַֽמַּחֲנֶה׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb You must have|תִּהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb a place|וְיָד֙\rb* \rb outside|מִח֖וּץ\rb* \rb the camp|לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֑ה\rb* \rb to go|וְיָצָ֥אתָ\rb* \rb and relieve yourself.|שָׁ֖מָּה\rb*\rb |חֽוּץ׃\rb* \v 13 \rb And you must have|תִּהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a digging tool|וְיָתֵ֛ד\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb your equipment|אֲזֵנֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb so that|וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb when you relieve yourself|בְּשִׁבְתְּךָ֣\rb*\rb |ח֔וּץ\rb* \rb you can dig a hole|וְחָפַרְתָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְשַׁבְתָּ֖\rb* \rb and cover up|וְכִסִּ֥יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your excrement.|צֵאָתֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb walks|מִתְהַלֵּ֣ךְ׀\rb* \rb throughout|בְּקֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb your camp|מַחֲנֶ֗ךָ\rb* \rb to protect you|לְהַצִּֽילְךָ֙\rb* \rb and deliver|וְלָתֵ֤ת\rb* \rb your enemies|אֹיְבֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb to you.|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb Your camp|מַחֲנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb must be|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb holy,|קָד֑וֹשׁ\rb* \rb lest|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb He see|יִרְאֶ֤ה\rb* \rb anything|דָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb unclean|עֶרְוַ֣ת\rb* \rb among you|בְךָ֙\rb* \rb and turn away|וְשָׁ֖ב\rb* \rb from you.|מֵאַחֲרֶֽיךָ׃ס\rb*
\s1 Miscellaneous Laws
\p \v 15 \rb Do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb return|תַסְגִּ֥יר\rb* \rb a slave|עֶ֖בֶד\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his master|אֲדֹנָ֑יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb if he has taken refuge|יִנָּצֵ֥ל\rb*\rb |מֵעִ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֲדֹנָֽיו׃\rb* \rb with you.|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \v 16 \rb |עִמְּךָ֞\rb* \rb Let him live|יֵשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb among you|בְּקִרְבְּךָ֗\rb* \rb wherever|בַּמָּק֧וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he chooses,|יִבְחַ֛ר\rb* \rb in|בְּאַחַ֥ד\rb* \rb the town|שְׁעָרֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb of his pleasing.|בַּטּ֣וֹב\rb*\rb |ל֑וֹ\rb* \rb Do not|לֹ֖א\rb* \rb oppress him.|תּוֹנֶֽנּוּ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb No|לֹא־\rb* \rb daughter|מִבְּנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb or|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל׃\rb* \rb son|מִבְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb is to be|תִהְיֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |קְדֵשָׁ֖ה\rb* \rb a shrine prostitute.|קָדֵ֖שׁ\rb* \v 18 \rb You must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb bring|תָבִיא֩\rb* \rb the wages|אֶתְנַ֨ן\rb* \rb of a prostitute, whether female|זוֹנָ֜ה\rb* \rb or male,|כֶּ֗לֶב\rb*\f + \fr 23:18 \ft Hebrew \fqa or a dog\f*\rb |וּמְחִ֣יר\rb* \rb into the house|בֵּ֛ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb to fulfill any|לְכָל־\rb* \rb vow,|נֶ֑דֶר\rb* \rb because|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb both|שְׁנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb are detestable|תוֹעֲבַ֛ת\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb charge|תַשִּׁ֣יךְ\rb* \rb your brother|לְאָחִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb interest|נֶ֥שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb on money,|כֶּ֖סֶף\rb*\rb |נֶ֣שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb food,|אֹ֑כֶל\rb*\rb |נֶ֕שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb or any|כָּל־\rb* \rb other|דָּבָ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb type of loan.|יִשָּֽׁךְ׃\rb* \v 20 \rb You may charge a foreigner|לַנָּכְרִ֣י\rb* \rb interest,|תַשִּׁ֔יךְ\rb* \rb but not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb your brother,|וּלְאָחִ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |תַשִּׁ֑יךְ\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb may bless you|יְבָרֶכְךָ֜\rb* \rb in everything|בְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb to which you put|מִשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb your hand|יָדֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֕רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb are entering|בָא־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb to possess.|לְרִשְׁתָּֽהּ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you make|תִדֹּ֥ר\rb* \rb a vow|נֶ֙דֶר֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be slow to keep it,|תְאַחֵ֖ר\rb*\rb |לְשַׁלְּמ֑וֹ\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb He|יְהוָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb will surely require it|דָּרֹ֨שׁ\rb*\rb |יִדְרְשֶׁ֜נּוּ\rb* \rb of you,|מֵֽעִמָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and you will be|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb guilty of sin.|חֵֽטְא׃\rb* \v 22 \rb But if|וְכִ֥י\rb* \rb you refrain|תֶחְדַּ֖ל\rb* \rb from making a vow,|לִנְדֹּ֑ר\rb* \rb you will not|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |בְךָ֖\rb* \rb be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb guilty of sin.|חֵֽטְא׃\rb* \v 23 \rb Be careful|תִּשְׁמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb to follow through|וְעָשִׂ֑יתָ\rb* \rb on what comes|מוֹצָ֥א\rb* \rb from your lips,|שְׂפָתֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb because|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you have freely|נְדָבָ֔ה\rb* \rb vowed|נָדַ֜רְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |דִּבַּ֖רְתָּ\rb* \rb with your own mouth.|בְּפִֽיךָ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb When|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you enter|תָבֹא֙\rb* \rb your neighbor’s|רֵעֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb vineyard,|בְּכֶ֣רֶם\rb* \rb you may eat|וְאָכַלְתָּ֧\rb* \rb your|כְּנַפְשְׁךָ֖\rb* \rb fill of|שָׂבְעֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb grapes,|עֲנָבִ֛ים\rb* \rb but you must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb put|תִתֵּֽן׃ס\rb* \rb any in|וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb your basket.|כֶּלְיְךָ֖\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb When|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you enter|תָבֹא֙\rb* \rb your neighbor’s|רֵעֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb grainfield,|בְּקָמַ֣ת\rb* \rb you may pluck|וְקָטַפְתָּ֥\rb* \rb the heads of grain|מְלִילֹ֖ת\rb* \rb with your hand,|בְּיָדֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb but you must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb put|תָנִ֔יף\rb* \rb a sickle|וְחֶרְמֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb your neighbor’s|רֵעֶֽךָ׃ס\rb* \rb grain.|קָמַ֥ת\rb*
\c 24
\s1 Marriage and Divorce Laws
\r \ref Matthew 5:31–32|MAT 5:31-32\ref*; \ref Luke 16:18|LUK 16:18\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |יִקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb a man|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb marries|וּבְעָלָ֑הּ\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb a woman,|אִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb but|אִם־\rb* \rb she becomes displeasing|לֹ֧א\rb*\rb |תִמְצָא־\rb*\rb |חֵ֣ן\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינָ֗יו\rb* \rb to him because|כִּי־\rb* \rb he finds|מָ֤צָא\rb* \rb some|דָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb indecency|עֶרְוַ֣ת\rb* \rb in her,|בָהּ֙\rb* \rb he may write|וְכָ֨תַב\rb* \rb her|לָ֜הּ\rb* \rb a certificate|סֵ֤פֶר\rb* \rb of divorce,|כְּרִיתֻת֙\rb*\f + \fr 24:1 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 5:31|MAT 5:31\ref*; see also Mark 10:4.\f* \rb hand it to|וְנָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb her,|בְּיָדָ֔הּ\rb* \rb and send her away|וְשִׁלְּחָ֖הּ\rb* \rb from his house.|מִבֵּיתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb If, after leaving|וְיָצְאָ֖ה\rb* \rb his house,|מִבֵּית֑וֹ\rb* \rb she goes|וְהָלְכָ֖ה\rb* \rb and becomes|וְהָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb another|אַחֵֽר׃\rb* \rb man’s wife,|לְאִישׁ־\rb* \v 3 \rb and the second|הָאַחֲרוֹן֒\rb* \rb man|הָאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb hates her,|וּשְׂנֵאָהּ֮\rb* \rb writes|וְכָ֨תַב\rb* \rb her|לָ֜הּ\rb* \rb a certificate|סֵ֤פֶר\rb* \rb of divorce,|כְּרִיתֻת֙\rb* \rb hands it to|וְנָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb her,|בְּיָדָ֔הּ\rb* \rb and sends her away|וְשִׁלְּחָ֖הּ\rb* \rb from his house,|מִבֵּית֑וֹ\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb if|כִ֤י\rb* \rb he dies,|יָמוּת֙\rb*\rb |הָאִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |הָאַחֲר֔וֹן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |לְקָחָ֥הּ\rb*\rb |לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb* \v 4 \rb then the husband|בַּעְלָ֣הּ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb divorced her|שִׁ֠לְּחָהּ\rb* \rb first|הָרִאשׁ֣וֹן\rb* \rb may|יוּכַ֣ל\rb* \rb not|לֹא־\rb*\rb |לָשׁ֨וּב\rb* \rb remarry|לְקַחְתָּ֜הּ\rb*\rb |לִהְי֧וֹת\rb*\rb |ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb her|לְאִשָּׁ֗ה\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵי֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb she has been defiled,|הֻטַּמָּ֔אָה\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb that is|הִ֖וא\rb* \rb an abomination|תוֹעֵבָ֥ה\rb* \rb to|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb You must not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb bring sin|תַחֲטִיא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb upon the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb as an inheritance.|נַחֲלָֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a man|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb is newly|חֲדָשָׁ֔ה\rb* \rb married,|יִקַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb he must not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb be sent|יֵצֵא֙\rb* \rb to war|בַּצָּבָ֔א\rb* \rb or|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb be pressed into|יַעֲבֹ֥ר\rb* \rb any|לְכָל־\rb* \rb duty.|דָּבָ֑ר\rb* \rb For one|אֶחָ֔ת\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb he is|יִהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb free|נָקִ֞י\rb* \rb to stay at home|לְבֵיתוֹ֙\rb* \rb and bring joy|וְשִׂמַּ֖ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the wife|אִשְׁתּ֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he has married.|לָקָֽח׃ס\rb*
\s1 Additional Laws
\p \v 6 \rb Do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb take a pair of millstones|רֵחַ֖יִם\rb* \rb or even an upper millstone|וָרָ֑כֶב\rb* \rb as security for a debt,|יַחֲבֹ֥ל\rb* \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb that would be|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb taking one’s livelihood|נֶ֖פֶשׁ\rb* \rb as security.|חֹבֵֽל׃ס\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb If|כִּי־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb is caught|יִמָּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb kidnapping|גֹּנֵ֨ב\rb* \rb one|נֶ֤פֶשׁ\rb* \rb of his Israelite|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb brothers,|מֵאֶחָיו֙\rb* \rb whether he treats him as a slave|וְהִתְעַמֶּר־\rb* \rb or sells him,|וּמְכָר֑וֹ\rb* \rb the|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb kidnapper|הַגַּנָּ֣ב\rb* \rb must die.|וּמֵת֙\rb* \rb So you must purge|וּבִֽעַרְתָּ֥\rb* \rb the evil|הָרָ֖ע\rb* \rb from among you.|מִקִּרְבֶּֽךָ׃\rb*\f + \fr 24:7 \ft Cited in \ref 1 Corinthians 5:13|1CO 5:13\ref*\f*
\p \v 8 \rb In cases of infectious|בְּנֶֽגַע־\rb* \rb skin diseases,|הַצָּרַ֛עַת\rb*\f + \fr 24:8 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa tzaraath\ft , traditionally translated as \fqa leprosy\ft , were used for various skin diseases; see Leviticus 13.\f* \rb be careful|הִשָּׁ֧מֶר\rb* \rb to diligently|לִשְׁמֹ֥ר\rb* \rb follow|וְלַעֲשׂ֑וֹת\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֖ד\rb* \rb everything|כְּכֹל֩\rb* \rb the Levitical|הַלְוִיִּ֛ם\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֧ים\rb* \rb instruct|יוֹר֨וּ\rb* \rb you.|אֶתְכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb Be careful|תִּשְׁמְר֥וּ\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשֽׂוֹת׃ס\rb* \rb as I have commanded them.|צִוִּיתִ֖ם\rb* \v 9 \rb Remember|זָכ֕וֹר\rb*\rb |אֵ֧ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb did|עָשָׂ֛ה\rb* \rb to Miriam|לְמִרְיָ֑ם\rb* \rb on the journey|בַּדֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb after you came out|בְּצֵאתְכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you lend|תַשֶּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb anything|מַשַּׁ֣את\rb*\rb |מְא֑וּמָה\rb* \rb to your neighbor,|בְרֵֽעֲךָ\rb* \rb do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb enter|תָבֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb his house|בֵּית֖וֹ\rb* \rb to collect|לַעֲבֹ֥ט\rb* \rb security.|עֲבֹטֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 11 \rb You are to stand|תַּעֲמֹ֑ד\rb* \rb outside|בַּח֖וּץ\rb* \rb while the man|וְהָאִ֗ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb to whom|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb you are lending|נֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb brings|יוֹצִ֥יא\rb* \rb the security|הַעֲב֖וֹט\rb* \rb out|הַחֽוּצָה׃\rb* \rb to you.|אֵלֶ֛יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \v 12 \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb he|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb is a poor|עָנִ֖י\rb* \rb man,|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb you must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb go to sleep|תִשְׁכַּ֖ב\rb* \rb with the security in your possession;|בַּעֲבֹטֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 13 \rb be sure to return|הָשֵׁב֩\rb*\rb |תָּשִׁ֨יב\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb it|הַעֲבוֹט֙\rb* \rb to him|ל֤וֹ\rb* \rb by sunset,|כְּבֹ֣א\rb*\rb |הַשֶּׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb* \rb so that he may sleep|וְשָׁכַ֥ב\rb* \rb in his own cloak|בְּשַׂלְמָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb and bless you,|וּבֵֽרֲכֶ֑ךָּ\rb* \rb and this will be|תִּהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb credited to you as righteousness|צְדָקָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וּלְךָ֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb oppress|תַעֲשֹׁ֥ק\rb* \rb a hired hand|שָׂכִ֖יר\rb* \rb who is poor|עָנִ֣י\rb* \rb and needy,|וְאֶבְי֑וֹן\rb* \rb whether he is a brother|מֵאַחֶ֕יךָ\rb* \rb or|א֧וֹ\rb* \rb a foreigner residing|מִגֵּרְךָ֛\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in one of your towns.|בִּשְׁעָרֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 15 \rb You are to pay|תִתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb his wages|שְׂכָר֜וֹ\rb* \rb each day|בְּיוֹמוֹ֩\rb* \rb before|וְֽלֹא־\rb* \rb sunset,|הַשֶּׁ֗מֶשׁ\rb*\rb |תָב֧וֹא\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb he|ה֔וּא\rb*\rb |וְאֵלָ֕יו\rb*\rb |ה֥וּא\rb* \rb is poor|עָנִי֙\rb* \rb and depends|נֹשֵׂ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |נַפְשׁ֑וֹ\rb* \rb on them.|אֶל־\rb* \rb Otherwise|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb he may cry out|יִקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb against you,|עָלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb and you will be guilty of sin.|חֵֽטְא׃ס\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb Fathers|אָבוֹת֙\rb* \rb shall not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb be put to death|יוּמְת֤וּ\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb their children,|בָּנִ֔ים\rb* \rb nor children|וּבָנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb*\rb |יוּמְת֣וּ\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb their fathers;|אָב֑וֹת\rb* \rb each|אִ֥יש\rb* \rb is to die|יוּמָֽתוּ׃ס\rb* \rb for his own sin.|בְּחֶטְא֖וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 24:16 \ft Cited in \ref 2 Kings 14:6|2KI 14:6\ref* and 2 Chronicles 25:4\f*
