\s1 Widowhood and Marriage
\p \v 5 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb brothers|אַחִ֜ים\rb* \rb dwell|יֵשְׁב֨וּ\rb* \rb together|יַחְדָּ֗ו\rb* \rb and one|אַחַ֤ד\rb* \rb of them|מֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb dies|וּמֵ֨ת\rb* \rb without|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb a son,|וּבֵ֣ן\rb* \rb the widow|אֵֽשֶׁת־\rb*\rb |הַמֵּ֛ת\rb* \rb must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb marry|תִהְיֶ֧ה\rb*\rb |לְאִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |זָ֑ר\rb* \rb outside the family.|הַח֖וּצָה\rb* \rb Her husband’s brother|יְבָמָהּ֙\rb* \rb is to take her|וּלְקָחָ֥הּ\rb* \rb as his|ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb wife|לְאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |יָבֹ֣א\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb and fulfill the duty of a brother-in-law for her.|וְיִבְּמָֽהּ׃\rb*\f + \fr 25:5 \ft Cited in \ref Matthew 22:24|MAT 22:24\ref*, Mark 12:19, and Luke 20:28\f* \v 6 \rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb The first son|הַבְּכוֹר֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb she bears|תֵּלֵ֔ד\rb* \rb will carry|יָק֕וּם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the name|שֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of the dead|הַמֵּ֑ת\rb* \rb brother,|אָחִ֖יו\rb* \rb so that his name|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb be blotted out|יִמָּחֶ֥ה\rb* \rb from Israel.|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb does not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb want|יַחְפֹּץ֙\rb* \rb to marry|לָקַ֖חַת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his brother’s widow,|יְבִמְתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb she|יְבִמְתּ֨וֹ\rb* \rb is to go|וְעָלְתָה֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the elders|הַזְּקֵנִ֗ים\rb* \rb at the city gate|הַשַּׁ֜עְרָה\rb* \rb and say,|וְאָֽמְרָה֙\rb* \rb “My husband’s brother|יְבָמִ֜י\rb* \rb refuses|מֵאֵ֨ין\rb* \rb to preserve|לְהָקִ֨ים\rb* \rb his brother’s|לְאָחִ֥יו\rb* \rb name|שֵׁם֙\rb* \rb in Israel.|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb He is not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb willing|אָבָ֖ה\rb* \rb to perform the duty of a brother-in-law for me.”|יַבְּמִֽי׃\rb*
