\s1 Revenge on the Amalekites
\p \v 17 \rb Remember|זָכ֕וֹר\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the Amalekites|עֲמָלֵ֑ק\rb* \rb did|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb along your way|בַּדֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb from|בְּצֵאתְכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb Egypt,|מִמִּצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 18 \rb how|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb they met you|קָֽרְךָ֜\rb* \rb on your journey|בַּדֶּ֗רֶךְ\rb* \rb when you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb were tired|וְיָגֵ֑עַ\rb* \rb and weary,|עָיֵ֣ף\rb* \rb and they attacked|וַיְזַנֵּ֤ב\rb*\rb |בְּךָ֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your stragglers;|הַנֶּחֱשָׁלִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אַֽחַרֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb they had no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb fear|יָרֵ֖א\rb* \rb of God.|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb |וְהָיָ֡ה\rb* \rb When the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֣יךָ׀\rb* \rb gives you rest|בְּהָנִ֣יחַ\rb* \rb from|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the enemies|אֹ֨יְבֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb around you|מִסָּבִ֗יב\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He|יְהוָֽה־\rb*\rb |אֱ֠לֹהֶיךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֨ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֤\rb* \rb to possess|לְרִשְׁתָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb as an inheritance,|נַחֲלָה֙\rb* \rb you are to blot out|תִּמְחֶה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the memory|זֵ֣כֶר\rb* \rb of Amalek|עֲמָלֵ֔ק\rb* \rb from under|מִתַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb heaven.|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb Do not|לֹ֖א\rb* \rb forget!|תִּשְׁכָּֽח׃פ\rb*
\c 26
\s1 Offering Firstfruits and Tithes
\r \ref Leviticus 27:30–34|LEV 27:30-34\ref*; \ref Deuteronomy 14:22–29|DEU 14:22-29\ref*; \ref Nehemiah 13:10–14|NEH 13:10-14\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb |וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you enter|תָב֣וֹא\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb as an inheritance,|נַחֲלָ֑ה\rb* \rb and you take possession of it|וִֽירִשְׁתָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb and settle|וְיָשַׁ֥בְתָּ\rb* \rb in it,|בָּֽהּ׃\rb* \v 2 \rb you are to take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֞\rb* \rb some of the firstfruits|מֵרֵאשִׁ֣ית׀\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your produce|פְּרִ֣י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*\rb |תָּבִ֧יא\rb* \rb from the soil|הָאֲדָמָ֗ה\rb* \rb of the land|מֵֽאַרְצְךָ֛\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb and put them|וְשַׂמְתָּ֣\rb* \rb in a basket.|בַטֶּ֑נֶא\rb* \rb Then go|וְהָֽלַכְתָּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֔וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb will choose|יִבְחַר֙\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb* \rb as a dwelling|לְשַׁכֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb for His Name,|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \v 3 \rb |וּבָאתָ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb is|יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb serving at that|הָהֵ֑ם\rb* \rb time,|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb and say|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb to him,|אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb “I declare|הִגַּ֤דְתִּי\rb* \rb today|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb I have entered|בָ֙אתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb swore|נִשְׁבַּ֧ע\rb* \rb to our fathers|לַאֲבֹתֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb to give|לָ֥תֶת\rb* \rb us.”|לָֽנוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Then the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb shall take|וְלָקַ֧ח\rb* \rb the basket|הַטֶּ֖נֶא\rb* \rb from your hands|מִיָּדֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb and place it|וְהִ֨נִּיח֔וֹ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֕י\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֖ח\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 5 \rb and you are to declare|וְעָנִ֨יתָ\rb*\rb |וְאָמַרְתָּ֜\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb “My father|אָבִ֔י\rb* \rb was a wandering|אֹבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb Aramean,|אֲרַמִּי֙\rb* \rb and he went down|וַיֵּ֣רֶד\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יְמָה\rb* \rb few in number|מְעָ֑ט\rb* \rb and lived|וַיָּ֥גָר\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb*\rb |בִּמְתֵ֣י\rb*\rb |שָׁ֕ם\rb* \rb and became|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb a great|גָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb nation,|לְג֥וֹי\rb* \rb mighty|עָצ֥וּם\rb* \rb and numerous.|וָרָֽב׃\rb* \v 6 \rb But the Egyptians|הַמִּצְרִ֖ים\rb* \rb mistreated us|וַיָּרֵ֧עוּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֛נוּ\rb* \rb and afflicted us,|וַיְעַנּ֑וּנוּ\rb* \rb putting us|וַיִּתְּנ֥וּ\rb*\rb |עָלֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb to hard|קָשָֽׁה׃\rb* \rb labor.|עֲבֹדָ֥ה\rb* \v 7 \rb So we called out|וַנִּצְעַ֕ק\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of our fathers;|אֲבֹתֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb and the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb our voice|קֹלֵ֔נוּ\rb* \rb and saw|וַיַּ֧רְא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our affliction,|עָנְיֵ֛נוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb toil,|עֲמָלֵ֖נוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and oppression.|לַחֲצֵֽנוּ׃\rb* \v 8 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb brought us|וַיּוֹצִאֵ֤נוּ\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb with a mighty|חֲזָקָה֙\rb* \rb hand|בְּיָ֤ד\rb* \rb and an outstretched|נְטוּיָ֔ה\rb* \rb arm,|וּבִזְרֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb with great|גָּדֹ֑ל\rb* \rb terror,|וּבְמֹרָ֖א\rb* \rb signs,|וּבְאֹת֖וֹת\rb* \rb and wonders.|וּבְמֹפְתִֽים׃\rb* \v 9 \rb And He brought us|וַיְבִאֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֣וֹם\rb* \rb and gave|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb us|לָ֙נוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb land,|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb flowing|זָבַ֥ת\rb* \rb with milk|חָלָ֖ב\rb* \rb and honey.|וּדְבָֽשׁ׃\rb* \v 10 \rb And now,|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb behold,|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb I have brought|הֵבֵ֙אתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |רֵאשִׁית֙\rb* \rb the firstfruits|פְּרִ֣י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb You, O LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb have given|נָתַ֥תָּה\rb* \rb me.”|לִּ֖י\rb*
\p \rb Then you are to place the basket|וְהִנַּחְתּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and bow down|וְהִֽשְׁתַּחֲוִ֔יתָ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb Him.|יְהוָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 11 \rb So you shall rejoice—|וְשָׂמַחְתָּ֣\rb*  \rb you,|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb the Levite,|וְהַלֵּוִ֔י\rb* \rb and the foreigner dwelling|וְהַגֵּ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb among you—|בְּקִרְבֶּֽךָ׃ס\rb*  \rb in all|בְכָל־\rb* \rb the good|הַטּ֗וֹב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb things the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb has given|נָֽתַן־\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֛\rb* \rb and your household.|וּלְבֵיתֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb When|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you have finished laying aside|תְכַלֶּ֞ה\rb*\rb |לַ֠עְשֵׂר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a tenth|מַעְשַׂ֧ר\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your produce|תְּבוּאָתְךָ֛\rb* \rb in the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֖ת\rb* \rb year,|בַּשָּׁנָ֥ה\rb* \rb the year|שְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the tithe,|הַֽמַּעֲשֵׂ֑ר\rb* \rb you are to give|וְנָתַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb it to the Levite,|לַלֵּוִ֗י\rb* \rb the foreigner,|לַגֵּר֙\rb* \rb the fatherless,|לַיָּת֣וֹם\rb* \rb and the widow,|וְלָֽאַלְמָנָ֔ה\rb* \rb that they may eat|וְאָכְל֥וּ\rb* \rb and be filled|וְשָׂבֵֽעוּ׃\rb* \rb within your gates.|בִשְׁעָרֶ֖יךָ\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb Then you shall declare|וְאָמַרְתָּ֡\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵי֩\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb “I have removed|בִּעַ֧רְתִּי\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb my house|הַבַּ֗יִת\rb* \rb the sacred portion|הַקֹּ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb and|וְגַ֨ם\rb* \rb have given it|נְתַתִּ֤יו\rb* \rb to the Levite,|לַלֵּוִי֙\rb* \rb the foreigner,|וְלַגֵּר֙\rb* \rb the fatherless,|לַיָּת֣וֹם\rb* \rb and the widow,|וְלָאַלְמָנָ֔ה\rb* \rb according to all|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb the commandments|מִצְוָתְךָ֖\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb You have given me.|צִוִּיתָ֑נִי\rb* \rb I have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb transgressed|עָבַ֥רְתִּי\rb* \rb or forgotten|שָׁכָֽחְתִּי׃\rb* \rb Your commandments.|מִמִּצְוֺתֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \v 14 \rb I have not|לֹא־\rb* \rb eaten|אָכַ֨לְתִּי\rb* \rb any of the sacred portion|מִמֶּ֗נּוּ\rb*\rb |וְלֹא־\rb* \rb while in mourning,|בְאֹנִ֜י\rb* \rb or removed|בִעַ֤רְתִּי\rb* \rb any of it|מִמֶּ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb while unclean,|בְּטָמֵ֔א\rb*\rb |וְלֹא־\rb* \rb or offered|נָתַ֥תִּי\rb* \rb any of|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb it for the dead.|לְמֵ֑ת\rb* \rb I have obeyed|שָׁמַ֗עְתִּי\rb*\rb |בְּקוֹל֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb my God;|אֱלֹהָ֔י\rb* \rb I have done|עָשִׂ֕יתִי\rb* \rb everything|כְּכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb You commanded me.|צִוִּיתָֽנִי׃\rb* \v 15 \rb Look down|הַשְׁקִיפָה֩\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Your holy|קָדְשְׁךָ֜\rb* \rb habitation,|מִמְּע֨וֹן\rb* \rb from heaven,|הַשָּׁמַ֗יִם\rb* \rb and bless|וּבָרֵ֤ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Your people|עַמְּךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and the land|הָאֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb You have given|נָתַ֖תָּה\rb* \rb us|לָ֑נוּ\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb as|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb You swore|נִשְׁבַּ֙עְתָּ֙\rb* \rb to our fathers—|לַאֲבֹתֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb flowing|זָבַ֥ת\rb* \rb with milk|חָלָ֖ב\rb* \rb and honey.”|וּדְבָֽשׁ׃ס\rb*
\s1 Obey the LORD’s Commands
\p \v 16 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb commands you|מְצַוְּךָ֧\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb to follow|לַעֲשׂ֛וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb statutes|הַחֻקִּ֥ים\rb* \rb and ordinances.|הַמִּשְׁפָּטִ֑ים\rb* \rb You must be careful|וְשָׁמַרְתָּ֤\rb* \rb to follow|וְעָשִׂ֙יתָ֙\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָבְךָ֖\rb* \rb and with all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb your soul.|נַפְשֶֽׁךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Today|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb you have proclaimed|הֶאֱמַ֖רְתָּ\rb* \rb that the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb is|לִהְיוֹת֩\rb* \rb your|לְךָ֨\rb* \rb God|לֵֽאלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb and that you will walk|וְלָלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb in His ways,|בִּדְרָכָ֗יו\rb* \rb keep|וְלִשְׁמֹ֨ר\rb* \rb His statutes|חֻקָּ֧יו\rb* \rb and commandments|וּמִצְוֺתָ֛יו\rb* \rb and ordinances,|וּמִשְׁפָּטָ֖יו\rb* \rb and listen|וְלִשְׁמֹ֥עַ\rb* \rb to His voice.|בְּקֹלֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb And today|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb has proclaimed that|הֶאֱמִֽירְךָ֣\rb* \rb you are|לִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb His|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb people|לְעַ֣ם\rb* \rb and treasured possession|סְגֻלָּ֔ה\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb He promised,|דִּבֶּר־\rb* \rb that you are to keep|וְלִשְׁמֹ֖ר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb His commandments,|מִצְוֺתָֽיו׃\rb* \v 19 \rb that He will set you|וּֽלְתִתְּךָ֣\rb* \rb high|עֶלְי֗וֹן\rb* \rb in praise|לִתְהִלָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and name|וּלְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb and honor|וּלְתִפְאָ֑רֶת\rb* \rb above|עַ֤ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He has made,|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb and that you will be|וְלִֽהְיֹתְךָ֧\rb* \rb a holy|קָדֹ֛שׁ\rb* \rb people|עַם־\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He has promised.|דִּבֵּֽר׃ס\rb*
\c 27
\s1 The Altar on Mount Ebal
\r \ref Joshua 8:30–35|JOS 8:30-35\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb and the elders|וְזִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb commanded|וַיְצַ֤ו\rb* \rb the people:|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Keep|שָׁמֹר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the commandments|הַמִּצְוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb am giving|מְצַוֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb today.|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb And|וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb on the day|בַּיּוֹם֮\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you cross|תַּעַבְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּן֒\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֕רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb you,|לָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb set up|וַהֲקֵמֹתָ֤\rb* \rb large|גְּדֹל֔וֹת\rb* \rb stones|אֲבָנִ֣ים\rb* \rb and coat|וְשַׂדְתָּ֥\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb with plaster.|בַּשִּֽׂיד׃\rb* \v 3 \rb Write|וְכָתַבְתָּ֣\rb* \rb on them|עֲלֵיהֶ֗ן\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֛י\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb law|הַתּוֹרָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb when you have crossed over|בְּעָבְרֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb to|לְמַ֡עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb enter|תָּבֹ֨א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲ‍ֽשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֣יךָ׀\rb* \rb is giving|נֹתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb you,|לְךָ֗\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb flowing|זָבַ֤ת\rb* \rb with milk|חָלָב֙\rb* \rb and honey,|וּדְבַ֔שׁ\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵֽי־\rb* \rb of your fathers,|אֲבֹתֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb has promised you.|דִּבֶּ֛ר\rb* \v 4 \rb And|וְהָיָה֮\rb* \rb when you have crossed|בְּעָבְרְכֶ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan,|הַיַּרְדֵּן֒\rb* \rb you are to set up|תָּקִ֜ימוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb stones|הָאֲבָנִ֣ים\rb* \rb on Mount|בְּהַ֣ר\rb* \rb Ebal,|עֵיבָ֑ל\rb* \rb as|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֜י\rb* \rb am commanding you today,|מְצַוֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |הַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb and you are to coat|וְשַׂדְתָּ֥\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb with plaster.|בַּשִּֽׂיד׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Moreover, you are to build|וּבָנִ֤יתָ\rb* \rb there|שָּׁם֙\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb an altar of|מִזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb stones.|אֲבָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb You must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb use|תָנִ֥יף\rb* \rb any iron tool|בַּרְזֶֽל׃\rb* \rb on them.|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \v 6 \rb You shall build|תִּבְנֶ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֖ח\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb with uncut|שְׁלֵמוֹת֙\rb* \rb stones|אֲבָנִ֤ים\rb* \rb and offer|וְהַעֲלִ֤יתָ\rb* \rb upon it|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עוֹלֹ֔ת\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 7 \rb There|שָּׁ֑ם\rb* \rb you are to sacrifice|וְזָבַחְתָּ֥\rb* \rb your peace offerings,|שְׁלָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb eating them|וְאָכַ֣לְתָּ\rb* \rb and rejoicing|וְשָׂ֣מַחְתָּ֔\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 8 \rb And you shall write|וְכָתַבְתָּ֣\rb* \rb distinctly|בַּאֵ֥ר\rb*\rb |הֵיטֵֽב׃ס\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb these stones|הָאֲבָנִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֛י\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb law.”|הַתּוֹרָ֥ה\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb and the Levitical|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb priests|וְהַכֹּהֲנִ֣ים\rb* \rb spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶ֥ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel:|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Be silent,|הַסְכֵּ֤ת׀\rb* \rb O Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and listen!|וּשְׁמַע֙\rb* \rb This|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֤וֹם\rb* \rb you have become|נִהְיֵ֣יתָֽ\rb* \rb the people|לְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 10 \rb You shall therefore obey|וְשָׁ֣מַעְתָּ֔\rb* \rb the voice|בְּק֖וֹל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb and follow|וְעָשִׂ֤יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His commandments|מִצְוֺתָו֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and statutes|חֻקָּ֔יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb am giving you today.”|מְצַוְּךָ֖\rb*\rb |הַיּֽוֹם׃ס\rb*
\s1 Curses Pronounced from Ebal
\p \v 11 \rb On that|הַה֖וּא\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb commanded|וַיְצַ֤ו\rb* \rb the people:|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \v 12 \rb “When you have crossed|בְּעָבְרְכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan,|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb* \rb these tribes|אֵ֠לֶּה\rb* \rb shall stand|יַֽעַמְד֞וּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Mount|הַ֣ר\rb* \rb Gerizim|גְּרִזִ֔ים\rb* \rb to bless|לְבָרֵ֤ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people:|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb Simeon,|שִׁמְעוֹן֙\rb* \rb Levi,|וְלֵוִ֣י\rb* \rb Judah,|וִֽיהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb Issachar,|וְיִשָּׂשכָ֖ר\rb* \rb Joseph,|וְיוֹסֵ֥ף\rb* \rb and Benjamin.|וּבִנְיָמִֽן׃\rb* \v 13 \rb And these tribes|וְאֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb shall stand|יַֽעַמְד֥וּ\rb* \rb on Mount|בְּהַ֣ר\rb* \rb Ebal|עֵיבָ֑ל\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb deliver the curse:|הַקְּלָלָ֖ה\rb* \rb Reuben,|רְאוּבֵן֙\rb* \rb Gad,|גָּ֣ד\rb* \rb Asher,|וְאָשֵׁ֔ר\rb* \rb Zebulun,|וּזְבוּלֻ֖ן\rb* \rb Dan,|דָּ֥ן\rb* \rb and Naphtali.|וְנַפְתָּלִֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Then|וְעָנ֣וּ\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֗ם\rb* \rb shall proclaim|וְאָֽמְר֛וּ\rb* \rb in a loud|רָֽם׃ס\rb* \rb voice|ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israelite:|אִ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*
\li1 \v 15 \rb ‘Cursed is|אָר֣וּר\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֡ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb makes|יַעֲשֶׂה֩\rb* \rb a carved idol|פֶ֨סֶל\rb* \rb or molten image—|וּמַסֵּכָ֜ה\rb*  \rb an abomination|תּוֹעֲבַ֣ת\rb* \rb to the LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb the work of|מַעֲשֵׂ֛ה\rb* \rb the hands|יְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb of a craftsman—|חָרָ֖שׁ\rb*  \rb and sets it up|וְשָׂ֣ם\rb* \rb in secret.’|בַּסָּ֑תֶר\rb*
\qr \rb And let all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb*\rb |וְאָמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb say,|וְעָנ֧וּ\rb* \rb ‘Amen!’|אָמֵֽן׃ס\rb*
\li1 \v 16 \rb ‘Cursed is|אָר֕וּר\rb* \rb he who dishonors|מַקְלֶ֥ה\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb or mother.’|וְאִמּ֑וֹ\rb*
\qr \rb And let all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb say,|וְאָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb ‘Amen!’|אָמֵֽן׃ס\rb*
\li1 \v 17 \rb ‘Cursed is|אָר֕וּר\rb* \rb he who moves|מַסִּ֖יג\rb* \rb his neighbor’s|רֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb boundary stone.’|גְּב֣וּל\rb*
\qr \rb And let all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb say,|וְאָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb ‘Amen!’|אָמֵֽן׃ס\rb*
\li1 \v 18 \rb ‘Cursed is|אָר֕וּר\rb* \rb he who lets a blind man|עִוֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb wander|מַשְׁגֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb in the road.’|בַּדָּ֑רֶךְ\rb*
\qr \rb And let all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb say,|וְאָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb ‘Amen!’|אָמֵֽן׃ס\rb*
\li1 \v 19 \rb ‘Cursed is|אָר֗וּר\rb* \rb he who withholds|מַטֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפַּ֥ט\rb* \rb from the foreigner,|גֵּר־\rb* \rb the fatherless,|יָת֖וֹם\rb* \rb or the widow.’|וְאַלְמָנָ֑ה\rb*
\qr \rb And let all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb say,|וְאָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb ‘Amen!’|אָמֵֽן׃ס\rb*
\li1 \v 20 \rb ‘Cursed is|אָר֗וּר\rb* \rb he who sleeps|שֹׁכֵב֙\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his father’s|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb wife,|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he has violated|גִלָּ֖ה\rb* \rb his father’s|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb marriage bed.’|כְּנַ֣ף\rb*\f + \fr 27:20 \ft Or \fqa uncovered his father’s skirt\f*
\qr \rb And let all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb say,|וְאָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb ‘Amen!’|אָמֵֽן׃ס\rb*
\li1 \v 21 \rb ‘Cursed is|אָר֕וּר\rb* \rb he who lies|שֹׁכֵ֖ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb animal.’|בְּהֵמָ֑ה\rb*
\qr \rb And let all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb say,|וְאָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb ‘Amen!’|אָמֵֽן׃ס\rb*
\li1 \v 22 \rb ‘Cursed is|אָר֗וּר\rb* \rb he who sleeps|שֹׁכֵב֙\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his sister,|אֲחֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb the daughter of|בַּת־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb or|א֣וֹ\rb* \rb the daughter of|בַת־\rb* \rb his mother.’|אִמּ֑וֹ\rb*
\qr \rb And let all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb say,|וְאָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb ‘Amen!’|אָמֵֽן׃ס\rb*
\li1 \v 23 \rb ‘Cursed is|אָר֕וּר\rb* \rb he who sleeps|שֹׁכֵ֖ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his mother-in-law.’|חֹֽתַנְתּ֑וֹ\rb*
\qr \rb And let all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb say,|וְאָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb ‘Amen!’|אָמֵֽן׃ס\rb*
\li1 \v 24 \rb ‘Cursed is|אָר֕וּר\rb* \rb he who strikes down|מַכֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb his neighbor|רֵעֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb in secret.’|בַּסָּ֑תֶר\rb*
\qr \rb And let all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb say,|וְאָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb ‘Amen!’|אָמֵֽן׃ס\rb*
\li1 \v 25 \rb ‘Cursed is|אָרוּר֙\rb* \rb he who accepts|לֹקֵ֣חַ\rb* \rb a bribe|שֹׁ֔חַד\rb* \rb to kill|לְהַכּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb an innocent|נָקִ֑י\rb* \rb person.’|נֶ֖פֶשׁ\rb*\rb |דָּ֣ם\rb*
\qr \rb And let all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb say,|וְאָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb ‘Amen!’|אָמֵֽן׃ס\rb*
\li1 \v 26 \rb ‘Cursed is|אָר֗וּר\rb* \rb he who|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb does not|לֹא־\rb* \rb put|יָקִ֛ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb law|הַתּוֹרָֽה־\rb* \rb into practice.’|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 27:26 \ft LXX \fqa Cursed is every man who does not continue in all the words of this law\ft ; cited in \ref Galatians 3:10|GAL 3:10\ref*\f*\rb |אוֹתָ֑ם\rb*
\qr \rb And let all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb say,|וְאָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb ‘Amen!’|אָמֵֽן׃פ\rb*[’’]
\c 28
\s1 The Blessings of Obedience
\r \ref Leviticus 25:18–22|LEV 25:18-22\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb “Now|וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you faithfully obey|שָׁמ֤וֹעַ\rb*\rb |תִּשְׁמַע֙\rb* \rb the voice of|בְּקוֹל֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and are careful|לִשְׁמֹ֤ר\rb* \rb to follow|לַעֲשׂוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb His commandments|מִצְוֺתָ֔יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb am giving you today,|מְצַוְּךָ֖\rb*\rb |הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |עֶלְי֔וֹן\rb* \rb will set you|וּנְתָ֨נְךָ֜\rb* \rb high above|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|גּוֹיֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the earth.|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \v 2 \rb And all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb blessings|הַבְּרָכ֥וֹת\rb* \rb will come|וּבָ֧אוּ\rb* \rb upon you|עָלֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb and overtake you,|וְהִשִּׂיגֻ֑ךָ\rb* \rb if|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you will obey|תִשְׁמַ֔ע\rb* \rb the voice of|בְּק֖וֹל\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God:|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb You|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb will be blessed|בָּר֥וּךְ\rb* \rb in the city|בָּעִ֑יר\rb*
\q2 \rb and blessed|וּבָר֥וּךְ\rb*\rb |אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb in the country.|בַּשָּׂדֶֽה׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb The fruit of|פְּרִֽי־\rb* \rb your womb|בִטְנְךָ֛\rb* \rb will be blessed,|בָּר֧וּךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb as well as the produce|וּפְרִ֥י\rb* \rb of your land|אַדְמָתְךָ֖\rb*
\q1 \rb and the offspring|וּפְרִ֣י\rb* \rb of your livestock—|בְהֶמְתֶּ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb the calves|שְׁגַ֥ר\rb* \rb of your herds|אֲלָפֶ֖יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and the lambs|וְעַשְׁתְּר֥וֹת\rb* \rb of your flocks.|צֹאנֶֽךָ׃\rb*
