\p \v 49 \rb The LORD|יְהוָה֩\rb* \rb will bring|יִשָּׂ֣א\rb* \rb a nation|גּ֤וֹי\rb* \rb from afar,|מֵרָחוֹק֙\rb* \rb from the ends of|מִקְצֵ֣ה\rb* \rb the earth,|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb to swoop down|יִדְאֶ֖ה\rb* \rb upon you|עָלֶ֨יךָ\rb* \rb like|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb an eagle—|הַנָּ֑שֶׁר\rb*  \rb a nation|גּ֕וֹי\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb language|לְשֹׁנֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb you will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb understand,|תִשְׁמַ֖ע\rb* \v 50 \rb a ruthless|עַ֣ז\rb*\rb |פָּנִ֑ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb nation|גּ֖וֹי\rb* \rb with no|לֹא־\rb* \rb respect|יִשָּׂ֤א\rb*\rb |פָנִים֙\rb* \rb for the old|לְזָקֵ֔ן\rb* \rb and no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb pity|יָחֹֽן׃\rb* \rb for the young.|וְנַ֖עַר\rb* \v 51 \rb They will eat|וְ֠אָכַל\rb* \rb the offspring|פְּרִ֨י\rb* \rb of your livestock|בְהֶמְתְּךָ֥\rb* \rb and the produce|וּפְרִֽי־\rb* \rb of your land|אַדְמָתְךָ֮\rb* \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb* \rb you are destroyed.|הִשָּֽׁמְדָךְ֒\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb They will leave|יַשְׁאִ֜יר\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֗\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb grain|דָּגָן֙\rb* \rb or new wine|תִּיר֣וֹשׁ\rb* \rb or oil,|וְיִצְהָ֔ר\rb* \rb no calves|שְׁגַ֥ר\rb* \rb of your herds|אֲלָפֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb or lambs|וְעַשְׁתְּרֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of your flocks,|צֹאנֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb until|עַ֥ד\rb* \rb they have caused you to perish.|הַאֲבִיד֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽךְ׃\rb* \v 52 \rb They will besiege|וְהֵצַ֨ר\rb*\rb |לְךָ֜\rb* \rb all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the cities|שְׁעָרֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your land,|אַרְצֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb* \rb the high|הַגְּבֹה֣וֹת\rb* \rb and fortified|וְהַבְּצֻר֔וֹת\rb* \rb walls|חֹמֹתֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb in which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb trust|בֹּטֵ֥חַ\rb* \rb have fallen.|רֶ֤דֶת\rb* \rb They will besiege|וְהֵצַ֤ר\rb* \rb all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your cities|שְׁעָרֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָ֨ל־\rb* \rb the land|אַרְצְךָ֔\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb has given|נָתַ֛ן\rb* \rb you.|לָֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 53 \rb Then you will eat|וְאָכַלְתָּ֣\rb* \rb the fruit|פְרִֽי־\rb* \rb of your womb,|בִטְנְךָ֗\rb* \rb the flesh|בְּשַׂ֤ר\rb* \rb of the sons|בָּנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבְנֹתֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb has given|נָֽתַן־\rb* \rb you,|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb in the siege|בְּמָצוֹר֙\rb* \rb and distress|וּבְמָצ֔וֹק\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb your enemy|אֹיְבֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb will inflict|יָצִ֥יק\rb* \rb on you.|לְךָ֖\rb*
\p \v 54 \rb The most|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb gentle|הָרַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb and refined|וְהֶעָנֹ֖ג\rb* \rb man|הָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb among you|בְּךָ֔\rb* \rb will begrudge|תֵּרַ֨ע\rb*\rb |עֵינ֤וֹ\rb* \rb his brother,|בְאָחִיו֙\rb* \rb the wife|וּבְאֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb he embraces,|חֵיק֔וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 28:54 \ft Hebrew \fqa the wife of his bosom\f* \rb and the rest|וּבְיֶ֥תֶר\rb* \rb of his children|בָּנָ֖יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb who have survived,|יוֹתִֽיר׃\rb* \v 55 \rb refusing to share|מִתֵּ֣ת׀\rb* \rb with any|לְאַחַ֣ד\rb* \rb of them|מֵהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb the flesh|מִבְּשַׂ֤ר\rb* \rb of his children|בָּנָיו֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he will eat|יֹאכֵ֔ל\rb* \rb because he has nothing|מִבְּלִ֥י\rb*\rb |ל֖וֹ\rb*\rb |כֹּ֑ל\rb* \rb left|הִשְׁאִֽיר־\rb* \rb in the siege|בְּמָצוֹר֙\rb* \rb and distress|וּבְמָצ֔וֹק\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb your enemy|אֹיִבְךָ֖\rb* \rb will inflict|יָצִ֥יק\rb* \rb on you|לְךָ֛\rb* \rb within all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your gates.|שְׁעָרֶֽיךָ׃\rb*\f + \fr 28:55 \ft Or \fqa within all your cities\ft ; similarly in verse 57\f*
\p \v 56 \rb The most gentle|הָרַכָּ֨ה\rb* \rb and refined woman|וְהָעֲנֻגָּ֗ה\rb* \rb among you,|בְךָ֜\rb* \rb so gentle|וּמֵרֹ֑ךְ\rb* \rb and refined|מֵהִתְעַנֵּ֖ג\rb* \rb she would not|לֹא־\rb* \rb venture|נִסְּתָ֤ה\rb* \rb to set|הַצֵּ֣ג\rb* \rb the sole|כַף־\rb* \rb of her foot|רַגְלָהּ֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the ground,|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb will begrudge|תֵּרַ֤ע\rb*\rb |עֵינָהּ֙\rb* \rb the husband|בְּאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb she embraces|חֵיקָ֔הּ\rb*\f + \fr 28:56 \ft Hebrew \fqa the husband of her bosom\f* \rb and her son|וּבִבְנָ֖הּ\rb* \rb and daughter|וּבְבִתָּֽהּ׃\rb* \v 57 \rb the afterbirth|וּֽבְשִׁלְיָתָ֞הּ\rb* \rb that comes|הַיּוֹצֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb from between|מִבֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb her legs|רַגְלֶ֗יהָ\rb* \rb and the children|וּבְבָנֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb she bears,|תֵּלֵ֔ד\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb she will secretly|בַּסָּ֑תֶר\rb* \rb eat them|תֹאכְלֵ֥ם\rb* \rb for lack|בְּחֹֽסֶר־\rb* \rb of anything else|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb in the siege|בְּמָצוֹר֙\rb* \rb and distress|וּבְמָצ֔וֹק\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb your enemy|אֹיִבְךָ֖\rb* \rb will inflict|יָצִ֥יק\rb* \rb on you|לְךָ֛\rb* \rb within your gates.|בִּשְׁעָרֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 58 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you are not|לֹ֨א\rb* \rb careful|תִשְׁמֹ֜ר\rb* \rb to observe|לַעֲשׂ֗וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵי֙\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb law|הַתּוֹרָ֣ה\rb* \rb which are written|הַכְּתוּבִ֖ים\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb book,|בַּסֵּ֣פֶר\rb* \rb that you may fear|לְ֠יִרְאָה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this glorious|הַנִּכְבָּ֤ד\rb* \rb and awesome|וְהַנּוֹרָא֙\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb name—|הַשֵּׁ֞ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God—|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 59 \rb He|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb will bring upon you and your descendants|זַרְעֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb extraordinary|וְהִפְלָ֤א\rb* \rb disasters,|מַכֹּ֣תְךָ֔\rb*\rb |מַכּ֤וֹת\rb* \rb severe|גְּדֹלוֹת֙\rb* \rb and lasting|וְנֶ֣אֱמָנ֔וֹת\rb* \rb plagues,|מַכּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb and terrible|רָעִ֖ים\rb* \rb and chronic|וְנֶאֱמָנִֽים׃\rb* \rb sicknesses.|וָחֳלָיִ֥ם\rb* \v 60 \rb He will afflict you again|וְהֵשִׁ֣יב\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb with all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the diseases|מַדְוֵ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you dreaded|יָגֹ֖רְתָּ\rb* \rb in Egypt,|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and they will cling|וְדָבְק֖וּ\rb* \rb to you.|בָּֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 61 \rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb will also|גַּ֤ם\rb* \rb bring|יַעְלֵ֤ם\rb* \rb upon you|עָלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb sickness|חֳלִי֙\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb* \rb and plague|מַכָּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb recorded|כָת֔וּב\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb Book|בְּסֵ֖פֶר\rb* \rb of the Law,|הַתּוֹרָ֣ה\rb* \rb until|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb you are destroyed.|הִשָּׁמְדָֽךְ׃\rb* \v 62 \rb |תַּ֚חַת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb You who were|הֱיִיתֶ֔ם\rb* \rb as numerous|לָרֹ֑ב\rb* \rb as the stars|כְּכוֹכְבֵ֥י\rb* \rb in the sky|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb will be left|וְנִשְׁאַרְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb few|מְעָ֔ט\rb* \rb in number,|בִּמְתֵ֣י\rb* \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb you would not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb obey|שָׁמַ֔עְתָּ\rb* \rb the voice of|בְּק֖וֹל\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 63 \rb |וְ֠הָיָה\rb* \rb Just as|כַּאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb it pleased|שָׂ֨שׂ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb to make you prosper|לְהֵיטִ֣יב\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֮\rb* \rb and multiply,|וּלְהַרְבּ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֒\rb* \rb so also|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb it will please|יָשִׂ֤ישׂ\rb* \rb Him|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to annihilate|לְהַאֲבִ֥יד\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and destroy|וּלְהַשְׁמִ֣יד\rb* \rb you.|אֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb And you will be uprooted|וְנִסַּחְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the land|הָֽאֲדָמָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb are entering|בָא־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb to possess.|לְרִשְׁתָּֽהּ׃\rb*
\p \v 64 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb will scatter|וֶהֱפִֽיצְךָ֤\rb* \rb you among all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the nations,|הָ֣עַמִּ֔ים\rb* \rb from one end|מִקְצֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the other,|קְצֵ֣ה\rb*\rb |הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb and there|שָּׁ֜ם\rb* \rb you will worship|וְעָבַ֨דְתָּ\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֗ים\rb* \rb gods,|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb gods of wood|עֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb and stone,|וָאָֽבֶן׃\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb neither you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb nor|לֹא־\rb* \rb your fathers|וַאֲבֹתֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb have known.|יָדַ֛עְתָּ\rb* \v 65 \rb Among those|הָהֵם֙\rb* \rb nations|וּבַגּוֹיִ֤ם\rb* \rb you will find no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb repose,|תַרְגִּ֔יעַ\rb* \rb not even|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb a resting place|מָנ֖וֹחַ\rb* \rb for the sole|לְכַף־\rb* \rb of your foot.|רַגְלֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb There|שָׁם֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb will give|וְנָתַן֩\rb* \rb you a trembling|רַגָּ֔ז\rb* \rb heart,|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb failing|וְכִלְי֥וֹן\rb* \rb eyes,|עֵינַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and a despairing|וְדַֽאֲב֥וֹן\rb* \rb soul.|נָֽפֶשׁ׃\rb*
\p \v 66 \rb |וְהָי֣וּ\rb* \rb So your life|חַיֶּ֔יךָ\rb* \rb will hang in doubt|תְּלֻאִ֥ים\rb* \rb before you,|מִנֶּ֑גֶד\rb* \rb and you will be afraid|וּפָֽחַדְתָּ֙\rb* \rb night|לַ֣יְלָה\rb* \rb and day,|וְיוֹמָ֔ם\rb* \rb never|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb certain|תַאֲמִ֖ין\rb* \rb of survival.|בְּחַיֶּֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 67 \rb In the morning|בַּבֹּ֤קֶר\rb* \rb you will say,|תֹּאמַר֙\rb* \rb ‘If only|מִֽי־\rb*\rb |יִתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb it were evening!’|עֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb and in the evening|וּבָעֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb you will say,|תֹּאמַ֖ר\rb* \rb ‘If only|מִֽי־\rb*\rb |יִתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb it were morning!’—|בֹּ֑קֶר\rb* \rb because of the dread|מִפַּ֤חַד\rb* \rb in your hearts|לְבָֽבְךָ֙\rb* \rb of|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the terrifying|תִּפְחָ֔ד\rb* \rb sights|וּמִמַּרְאֵ֥ה\rb*\rb |עֵינֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you will see.|תִּרְאֶֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 68 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֥ה׀\rb* \rb will return you|וֶֽהֱשִֽׁיבְךָ֨\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרַיִם֮\rb* \rb in ships|בָּאֳנִיּוֹת֒\rb* \rb by a route|בַּדֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I said|אָמַ֣רְתִּֽי\rb* \rb you should|לְךָ֔\rb* \rb never|לֹא־\rb* \rb see|לִרְאֹתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb again.|תֹסִ֥יף\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb There|שָׁ֧ם\rb* \rb you will sell|וְהִתְמַכַּרְתֶּ֨ם\rb* \rb yourselves to your enemies|לְאֹיְבֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb as male|לַעֲבָדִ֥ים\rb* \rb and female slaves,|וְלִשְׁפָח֖וֹת\rb* \rb but no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb one will buy you.”|קֹנֶֽה׃ס\rb*
\c 29
\s1 The Covenant in Moab
\p \v 1 \rb These|אֵלֶּה֩\rb* \rb are the words|דִבְרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the covenant|הַבְּרִ֜ית\rb* \rb that|אֲ‍ֽשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb commanded|צִוָּ֧ה\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb to make|לִכְרֹ֛ת\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Moab,|מוֹאָ֑ב\rb* \rb in addition to|מִלְּבַ֣ד\rb* \rb the covenant|הַבְּרִ֔ית\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He had made|כָּרַ֥ת\rb* \rb with them|אִתָּ֖ם\rb* \rb at Horeb.|בְּחֹרֵֽב׃פ\rb*\f + \fr 29:1 \ft That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai\f*
