\p \v 16 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you yourselves|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb know|יְדַעְתֶּ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb how|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb we lived|יָשַׁ֖בְנוּ\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֧ת\rb* \rb how|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb we passed|עָבַ֛רְנוּ\rb* \rb through|בְּקֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb on the way here.|עֲבַרְתֶּֽם׃\rb* \v 17 \rb You saw|וַתִּרְאוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the abominations|שִׁקּ֣וּצֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and idols|גִּלֻּלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb among them|עִמָּהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb made of wood|עֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb and stone,|וָאֶ֔בֶן\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֥סֶף\rb* \rb and gold.|וְזָהָ֖ב\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Make sure there is|יֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb no|פֶּן־\rb* \rb man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb or woman,|אִשָּׁ֞ה\rb*\rb |א֧וֹ\rb* \rb clan|מִשְׁפָּחָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אוֹ־\rb* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb tribe|שֵׁ֗בֶט\rb* \rb among you|בָּ֠כֶם\rb* \rb today|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb heart|לְבָב֨וֹ\rb* \rb turns away|פֹנֶ֤ה\rb* \rb from|מֵעִם֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb to go|לָלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb and worship|לַעֲבֹ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֖י\rb* \rb of those|הָהֵ֑ם\rb* \rb nations.|הַגּוֹיִ֣ם\rb* \rb Make sure there is|יֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb no|פֶּן־\rb* \rb root|שֹׁ֛רֶשׁ\rb* \rb among you|בָּכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb that bears|פֹּרֶ֥ה\rb* \rb such poisonous|רֹ֖אשׁ\rb* \rb and bitter fruit,|וְלַעֲנָֽה׃\rb*\f + \fr 29:18 \ft See \ref Hebrews 12:15|HEB 12:15\ref*\f* \v 19 \rb |וְהָיָ֡ה\rb* \rb because when such a person hears|בְּשָׁמְעוֹ֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֗את\rb* \rb oath,|הָֽאָלָ֜ה\rb*\f + \fr 29:19 \ft Or \fqa curse\f* \rb he invokes a blessing|וְהִתְבָּרֵ֨ךְ\rb* \rb on himself,|בִּלְבָב֤וֹ\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹר֙\rb* \rb ‘I|לִּ֔י\rb* \rb will have|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb peace,|שָׁל֣וֹם\rb* \rb even though|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I walk|אֵלֵ֑ךְ\rb*\rb |לְמַ֛עַן\rb* \rb in the stubbornness|בִּשְׁרִר֥וּת\rb* \rb of my own heart.’|לִבִּ֖י\rb*
\p \rb This will bring disaster|סְפ֥וֹת\rb* \rb on the watered land|הָרָוָ֖ה\rb* \rb as well as|אֶת־\rb* \rb the dry.|הַצְּמֵאָֽה׃\rb* \v 20 \rb The LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb will never|לֹא־\rb* \rb be willing|יֹאבֶ֣ה\rb* \rb to forgive|סְלֹ֣חַֽ\rb* \rb him.|לוֹ֒\rb* \rb Instead,|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אָ֠ז\rb* \rb His|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb anger|אַף־\rb* \rb and jealousy|וְקִנְאָתוֹ֙\rb* \rb will burn|יֶעְשַׁ֨ן\rb* \rb against that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb man,|בָּאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb and every|כָּל־\rb* \rb curse|הָ֣אָלָ֔ה\rb* \rb written|הַכְּתוּבָ֖ה\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb book|בַּסֵּ֣פֶר\rb* \rb will fall|וְרָ֤בְצָה\rb* \rb upon him.|בּוֹ֙\rb* \rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will blot out|וּמָחָ֤ה\rb* \rb his name|שְׁמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb from under|מִתַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb heaven|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 21 \rb and single him out|וְהִבְדִּיל֤וֹ\rb*\rb |יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb from all|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb for disaster,|לְרָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb according to all|כְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb the curses|אָל֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the covenant|הַבְּרִ֔ית\rb* \rb written|הַכְּתוּבָ֕ה\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb Book|בְּסֵ֥פֶר\rb* \rb of the Law.|הַתּוֹרָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb |וְאָמַ֞ר\rb* \rb Then the generation|הַדּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb to come—|הָֽאַחֲר֗וֹן\rb*  \rb your sons|בְּנֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb follow|יָק֙וּמוּ֙\rb* \rb you|מֵאַ֣חֲרֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and the foreigner|וְהַ֨נָּכְרִ֔י\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb comes|יָבֹ֖א\rb* \rb from a distant|רְחוֹקָ֑ה\rb* \rb land—|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb*  \rb will see|וְ֠רָאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the plagues|מַכּ֞וֹת\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֤רֶץ\rb*\rb |הַהִוא֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the sicknesses|תַּ֣חֲלֻאֶ֔יהָ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has inflicted|חִלָּ֥ה\rb* \rb on it.|בָּֽהּ׃\rb* \v 23 \rb All|כָל־\rb* \rb its soil|אַרְצָהּ֒\rb* \rb will be a burning waste|שְׂרֵפָ֣ה\rb* \rb of sulfur|גָּפְרִ֣ית\rb* \rb and salt,|וָמֶלַח֮\rb* \rb unsown|לֹ֤א\rb*\rb |תִזָּרַע֙\rb* \rb and unproductive,|תַצְמִ֔חַ\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb with no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb plant|עֵ֑שֶׂב\rb* \rb growing|יַעֲלֶ֥ה\rb* \rb on it,|בָ֖הּ\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb just like the destruction|כְּֽמַהְפֵּכַ֞ת\rb* \rb of Sodom|סְדֹ֤ם\rb* \rb and Gomorrah,|וַעֲמֹרָה֙\rb* \rb Admah|אַדְמָ֣ה\rb* \rb and Zeboiim,|וּצְבֹיִּים\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb overthrew|הָפַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb in His fierce anger.|בְּאַפּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וּבַחֲמָתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb So all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb will ask,|וְאָֽמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb ‘Why|עַל־\rb*\rb |מֶ֨ה\rb* \rb has the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb done|עָשָׂ֧ה\rb* \rb such a thing|כָּ֖כָה\rb* \rb to this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb land?|לָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb Why|מֶ֥ה\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb great|הַגָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb outburst|חֳרִ֛י\rb* \rb of anger?’|הָאַ֥ף\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb And the people will answer,|וְאָ֣מְר֔וּ\rb* \rb ‘It is because|עַ֚ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they abandoned|עָֽזְב֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the covenant|בְּרִ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of their fathers,|אֲבֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb He made|כָּרַ֣ת\rb* \rb with them|עִמָּ֔ם\rb* \rb when He brought|בְּהוֹצִיא֥וֹ\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 26 \rb They went|וַיֵּלְכ֗וּ\rb* \rb and served|וַיַּֽעַבְדוּ֙\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gods,|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb and they worshiped|וַיִּֽשְׁתַּחֲוּ֖וּ\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they had not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb known—|יְדָע֔וּם\rb* \rb gods that the LORD had not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb given|חָלַ֖ק\rb* \rb to them.|לָהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 27 \rb Therefore the anger|אַ֥ף\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb against this|הַהִ֑וא\rb* \rb land,|בָּאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb and He brought|לְהָבִ֤יא\rb* \rb upon it|עָלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb curse|הַקְּלָלָ֔ה\rb* \rb written|הַכְּתוּבָ֖ה\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb book.|בַּסֵּ֥פֶר\rb* \v 28 \rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb uprooted them|וַיִּתְּשֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb their land|אַדְמָתָ֔ם\rb* \rb in His anger,|בְּאַ֥ף\rb* \rb rage,|וּבְחֵמָ֖ה\rb* \rb and great|גָּד֑וֹל\rb* \rb wrath,|וּבְקֶ֣צֶף\rb* \rb and He cast them|וַיַּשְׁלִכֵ֛ם\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb another|אַחֶ֖רֶת\rb* \rb land,|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb where they are today.’|כַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb The secret things belong|הַ֨נִּסְתָּרֹ֔ת\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb our God,|אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb but the things revealed|וְהַנִּגְלֹ֞ת\rb* \rb belong to us|לָ֤ׄנׄוּׄ\rb* \rb and to our children|וּׄלְׄבָׄנֵׄ֙יׄנׄוּׄ֙\rb* \rb forever,|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb so that we may follow|לַעֲשׂ֕וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּֽאת׃ס\rb* \rb law.|הַתּוֹרָ֥ה\rb*[’’]
\c 30
\s1 The Promise of Restoration
\r \ref Nehemiah 1:1–11|NEH 1:1-11\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb |וְהָיָה֩\rb* \rb “When|כִֽי־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb things|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb come|יָבֹ֨אוּ\rb* \rb upon you—|עָלֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb the blessings|הַבְּרָכָה֙\rb* \rb and curses|וְהַקְּלָלָ֔ה\rb* \rb I have set|נָתַ֖תִּי\rb* \rb before you—|לְפָנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb and you call them|וַהֲשֵׁבֹתָ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb mind|לְבָבֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb* \rb has banished you,|הִדִּיחֲךָ֛\rb* \v 2 \rb and when you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and your children|וּבָנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb return|וְשַׁבְתָּ֞\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb and obey|וְשָׁמַעְתָּ֣\rb* \rb His voice|בְקֹל֔וֹ\rb* \rb with all|כְּכֹ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָבְךָ֖\rb* \rb and all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your soul|נַפְשֶֽׁךָ׃\rb* \rb according to everything|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb am giving you|מְצַוְּךָ֖\rb* \rb today,|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \v 3 \rb then He|יְהוָ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will restore|וְשָׁ֨ב\rb* \rb you from captivity|שְׁבוּתְךָ֖\rb*\f + \fr 30:3 \ft Or \fqa restore your fortunes\f* \rb and have compassion on you|וְרִחֲמֶ֑ךָ\rb*\rb |וְשָׁ֗ב\rb* \rb and gather you|וְקִבֶּצְךָ֙\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|הָ֣עַמִּ֔ים\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb* \rb has scattered you.|הֱפִֽיצְךָ֛\rb* \v 4 \rb Even if|אִם־\rb* \rb you have been banished|נִֽדַּחֲךָ֖\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb to the farthest|בִּקְצֵ֣ה\rb* \rb horizon,|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb*\f + \fr 30:4 \ft Or \fqa to the extremity of the heavens\f* \rb He|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |וּמִשָּׁ֖ם\rb* \rb will gather you|יְקַבֶּצְךָ֙\rb* \rb and return you|יִקָּחֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb from there.|מִשָּׁ֗ם\rb*\f + \fr 30:4 \ft Cited in \ref Nehemiah 1:8–9|NEH 1:8-9\ref*\f*
\p \v 5 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb will bring you|וֶהֱבִֽיאֲךָ֞\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֛רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֹתֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb possessed,|יָרְשׁ֥וּ\rb* \rb and you will take possession of it.|וִֽירִשְׁתָּ֑הּ\rb* \rb He will cause you to prosper|וְהֵיטִֽבְךָ֥\rb* \rb and multiply|וְהִרְבְּךָ֖\rb* \rb more than your fathers.|מֵאֲבֹתֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 6 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will circumcise|וּמָ֨ל\rb* \rb your hearts|לְבָבְךָ֖\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the hearts|לְבַ֣ב\rb* \rb of your descendants,|זַרְעֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb and you will love|לְאַהֲבָ֞ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Him|יְהוָ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָבְךָ֥\rb* \rb and with all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb your soul,|נַפְשְׁךָ֖\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֥עַן\rb* \rb you may live.|חַיֶּֽיךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb will put|וְנָתַן֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb curses|הָאָל֖וֹת\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb your enemies|אֹיְבֶ֥יךָ\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb hate you|שֹׂנְאֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and persecute you.|רְדָפֽוּךָ׃\rb* \v 8 \rb And you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb will again|תָשׁ֔וּב\rb* \rb obey|וְשָׁמַעְתָּ֖\rb* \rb the voice|בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and follow|וְעָשִׂ֙יתָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb His commandments|מִצְוֺתָ֔יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb am giving you today.|מְצַוְּךָ֖\rb*\rb |הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb* \v 9 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb will make you abound|וְהוֹתִֽירְךָ֩\rb* \rb in all|בְּכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the work|מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb of your hands|יָדֶ֗ךָ\rb* \rb and in the fruit|בִּפְרִ֨י\rb* \rb of your womb,|בִטְנְךָ֜\rb* \rb the offspring|וּבִפְרִ֧י\rb* \rb of your livestock,|בְהֶמְתְּךָ֛\rb* \rb and the produce|וּבִפְרִ֥י\rb* \rb of your land.|אַדְמָתְךָ֖\rb*\rb |לְטוֹבָ֑ה\rb* \rb Indeed,|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb will again|יָשׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb delight|לָשׂ֤וּשׂ\rb* \rb in|עָלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb your prosperity,|לְט֔וֹב\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He delighted|שָׂ֖שׂ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb that of your fathers,|אֲבֹתֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 10 \rb if|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you obey|תִשְׁמַ֗ע\rb*\rb |בְּקוֹל֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb by keeping|לִשְׁמֹ֤ר\rb* \rb His commandments|מִצְוֺתָיו֙\rb* \rb and statutes|וְחֻקֹּתָ֔יו\rb* \rb that are written|הַכְּתוּבָ֕ה\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb Book|בְּסֵ֥פֶר\rb* \rb of the Law,|הַתּוֹרָ֖ה\rb* \rb and if|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you turn|תָשׁוּב֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Him|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָבְךָ֖\rb* \rb and with all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb your soul.|נַפְשֶֽׁךָ׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Choice of Life or Death
\p \v 11 \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb commandment|הַמִּצְוָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb give|מְצַוְּךָ֖\rb* \rb you today|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb is not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb too difficult|נִפְלֵ֥את\rb*\rb |הִוא֙\rb* \rb for you|מִמְּךָ֔\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb beyond your reach.|רְחֹקָ֖ה\rb*\rb |הִֽוא׃\rb* \v 12 \rb It|הִ֑וא\rb* \rb is not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb in heaven,|בַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb that you should need to ask,|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb ‘Who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb will ascend|יַעֲלֶה־\rb* \rb into|לָּ֤נוּ\rb* \rb heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֙יְמָה֙\rb*\f + \fr 30:12 \ft Cited in \ref Romans 10:6|ROM 10:6\ref*\f* \rb to get it|וְיִקָּחֶ֣הָ\rb* \rb for us|לָּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb and proclaim|וְיַשְׁמִעֵ֥נוּ\rb* \rb it,|אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb that we may obey it?’|וְנַעֲשֶֽׂנָּה׃\rb* \v 13 \rb And it|הִ֑וא\rb* \rb is not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb beyond|מֵעֵ֥בֶר\rb* \rb the sea,|לַיָּ֖ם\rb* \rb that you should need to ask,|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb ‘Who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb will cross|יַעֲבָר־\rb*\rb |לָ֜נוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |עֵ֤בֶר\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּם֙\rb*\f + \fr 30:13 \ft See \ref Romans 10:7|ROM 10:7\ref*.\f* \rb to get it|וְיִקָּחֶ֣הָ\rb* \rb for us|לָּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb and proclaim|וְיַשְׁמִעֵ֥נוּ\rb* \rb it,|אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb that we may obey it?’|וְנַעֲשֶֽׂנָּה׃\rb* \v 14 \rb But|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the word is|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb very|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb near|קָר֥וֹב\rb* \rb you;|אֵלֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb it is in your mouth|בְּפִ֥יךָ\rb* \rb and in your heart,|וּבִֽלְבָבְךָ֖\rb*\f + \fr 30:14 \ft Cited in \ref Romans 10:8|ROM 10:8\ref*\f* \rb so that you may obey it.|לַעֲשֹׂתֽוֹ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb See,|רְאֵ֨ה\rb* \rb I have set|נָתַ֤תִּי\rb* \rb before you|לְפָנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb life|הַֽחַיִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and prosperity,|הַטּ֑וֹב\rb* \rb as well as|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb death|הַמָּ֖וֶת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and disaster.|הָרָֽע׃\rb* \v 16 \rb For|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb am commanding|מְצַוְּךָ֮\rb* \rb you today|הַיּוֹם֒\rb* \rb to love|לְאַהֲבָ֞ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb to walk|לָלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb in His ways,|בִּדְרָכָ֔יו\rb* \rb and to keep|וְלִשְׁמֹ֛ר\rb* \rb His commandments,|מִצְוֺתָ֥יו\rb* \rb statutes,|וְחֻקֹּתָ֖יו\rb* \rb and ordinances,|וּמִשְׁפָּטָ֑יו\rb* \rb so that you may live|וְחָיִ֣יתָ\rb* \rb and increase,|וְרָבִ֔יתָ\rb* \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb may bless|וּבֵֽרַכְךָ֙\rb* \rb you in the land|בָּאָ֕רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb are entering|בָא־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb to possess.|לְרִשְׁתָּֽהּ׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָבְךָ֖\rb* \rb turns away|יִפְנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb and you do not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb listen,|תִשְׁמָ֑ע\rb* \rb but are drawn away|וְנִדַּחְתָּ֗\rb* \rb to bow down|וְהִֽשְׁתַּחֲוִ֛יתָ\rb* \rb to other|אֲחֵרִ֖ים\rb* \rb gods|לֵאלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \rb and worship them,|וַעֲבַדְתָּֽם׃\rb* \v 18 \rb I declare|הִגַּ֤דְתִּי\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you will surely perish;|אָבֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |תֹּאבֵד֑וּן\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb you shall not prolong|תַאֲרִיכֻ֤ן\rb* \rb your days|יָמִים֙\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|הָ֣אֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb are crossing|עֹבֵר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb*\rb |לָבֹ֥א\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb to possess.|לְרִשְׁתָּֽהּ׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb I call heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֣יִם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and earth|הָאָרֶץ֒\rb* \rb as witnesses|הַעִידֹ֨תִי\rb* \rb against you|בָכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb today|הַיּוֹם֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb that I have set|נָתַ֣תִּי\rb* \rb before|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb you life|הַחַיִּ֤ים\rb* \rb and death,|וְהַמָּ֙וֶת֙\rb* \rb blessing|הַבְּרָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb and cursing.|וְהַקְּלָלָ֑ה\rb* \rb Therefore choose|וּבָֽחַרְתָּ֙\rb* \rb life,|בַּֽחַיִּ֔ים\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֥עַן\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and your descendants|וְזַרְעֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb may live,|תִּחְיֶ֖ה\rb* \v 20 \rb and that you may love|לְאַֽהֲבָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb obey Him,|לִשְׁמֹ֥עַ\rb*\rb |בְּקֹל֖וֹ\rb* \rb and hold fast|וּלְדָבְקָה־\rb* \rb to Him.|ב֑וֹ\rb* \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb He is|ה֤וּא\rb* \rb your life,|חַיֶּ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb and He will prolong|וְאֹ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb your life|יָמֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |לָשֶׁ֣בֶת\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאֲדָמָ֗ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb swore|נִשְׁבַּ֨ע\rb* \rb to give|לָתֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |לָהֶֽם׃פ\rb* \rb to your fathers,|לַאֲבֹתֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb to Abraham,|לְאַבְרָהָ֛ם\rb* \rb Isaac,|לְיִצְחָ֥ק\rb* \rb and Jacob.”|וּֽלְיַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb*
\c 31
\s1 Joshua to Succeed Moses
\r \ref Numbers 27:18–23|NUM 27:18-23\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb When Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb had finished|וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb speaking|וַיְדַבֵּ֛ר\rb*\f + \fr 31:1 \ft DSS and LXX; MT \fqa When Moses went out and spoke\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 2 \rb he said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb “I|אָנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb am now|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb a hundred|מֵאָה֩\rb* \rb and twenty|וְעֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb* \rb years old;|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֤ה\rb* \rb I am|אוּכַ֥ל\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb able to come|לָצֵ֣את\rb* \rb and go,|וְלָב֑וֹא\rb* \rb and the LORD|וַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb has said|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb ‘You shall not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb cross|תַעֲבֹ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb Jordan.’|הַיַּרְדֵּ֥ן\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb Himself|ה֣וּא׀\rb* \rb will cross over|עֹבֵ֣ר\rb* \rb ahead of you.|לְפָנֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb He|הֽוּא־\rb* \rb will destroy|יַשְׁמִ֞יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֥ם\rb* \rb before you,|מִלְּפָנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and you will dispossess them.|וִֽירִשְׁתָּ֑ם\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֗עַ\rb*\rb |ה֚וּא\rb* \rb will cross|עֹבֵ֣ר\rb* \rb ahead of you,|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has said.|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \v 4 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb will do|וְעָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He did|עָשָׂ֗ה\rb* \rb to Sihon|לְסִיח֥וֹן\rb* \rb and Og,|וּלְע֛וֹג\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Amorites,|הָאֱמֹרִ֖י\rb* \rb when|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He destroyed|הִשְׁמִ֖יד\rb* \rb them|אֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb along with their land.|וּלְאַרְצָ֑ם\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will deliver them over|וּנְתָנָ֥ם\rb* \rb to you,|לִפְנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and you must do|וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֣ם\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb exactly as|כְּכָל־\rb*\rb |הַמִּצְוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have commanded|צִוִּ֖יתִי\rb* \rb you.|אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 6 \rb Be strong|חִזְק֣וּ\rb* \rb and courageous;|וְאִמְצ֔וּ\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּֽירְא֥וּ\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb or terrified|תַּעַרְצ֖וּ\rb* \rb of them,|מִפְּנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb it is the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb who|ה֚וּא\rb* \rb goes|הַהֹלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb with you;|עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb He will never|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb leave you|יַרְפְּךָ֖\rb* \rb nor|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb forsake you.”|יַעַזְבֶֽךָּ׃פ\rb*\f + \fr 31:6 \ft Cited in \ref Hebrews 13:5|HEB 13:5\ref*; here and in verse 8\f*
\p \v 7 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָ֨א\rb* \rb for Joshua|לִֽיהוֹשֻׁ֗עַ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֜יו\rb* \rb in the presence|לְעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of all|כָל־\rb* \rb Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֘ל\rb* \rb “Be strong|חֲזַ֣ק\rb* \rb and courageous,|וֶאֱמָץ֒\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb will go|תָּבוֹא֙\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֕רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb swore|נִשְׁבַּ֧ע\rb* \rb to their fathers|לַאֲבֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb to give|לָתֵ֣ת\rb* \rb them,|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb shall give it to them as an inheritance.|תַּנְחִילֶ֥נָּה\rb*\rb |אוֹתָֽם׃\rb* \v 8 \rb The LORD|וַֽיהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb Himself|ה֣וּא׀\rb* \rb goes|הַהֹלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb before you;|לְפָנֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb He|ה֚וּא\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb with you.|עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb He will never|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb leave you|יַרְפְּךָ֖\rb* \rb nor|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb forsake you.|יַֽעַזְבֶ֑ךָּ\rb* \rb Do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be afraid|תִירָ֖א\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb discouraged.”|תֵחָֽת׃\rb*
\s1 The Reading of the Law
\r \ref Nehemiah 8:1–8|NEH 8:1-8\ref*)
\p \v 9 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁה֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb wrote down|וַיִּכְתֹּ֣ב\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּאת֒\rb* \rb law|הַתּוֹרָ֣ה\rb* \rb and gave|וַֽיִּתְּנָ֗הּ\rb* \rb it to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priests,|הַכֹּהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Levi,|לֵוִ֔י\rb* \rb who carried|הַנֹּ֣שְׂאִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֖וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֣ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb commanded them,|וַיְצַ֥ו\rb* \rb “At the end|מִקֵּ֣ץ׀\rb* \rb of every seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb years,|שָׁנִ֗ים\rb* \rb at the appointed time|בְּמֹעֵ֛ד\rb* \rb in the year|שְׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of remission of debt,|הַשְּׁמִטָּ֖ה\rb* \rb during the Feast|בְּחַ֥ג\rb* \rb of Tabernacles,|הַסֻּכּֽוֹת׃\rb*\f + \fr 31:10 \ft That is, Sukkot, the autumn feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; also translated as \fqa the Feast of Booths \ft or \fqa the Feast of Shelters \ft and originally called \fqa the Feast of Ingathering\ft (see \ref Exodus 23:16|EXO 23:16\ref* and Exodus 34:22).\f* \v 11 \rb when all|כָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*\rb |לֵרָאוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb comes|בְּב֣וֹא\rb* \rb before|פְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb at the place|בַּמָּק֖וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He will choose,|יִבְחָ֑ר\rb* \rb you are to read|תִּקְרָ֞א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֛את\rb* \rb law|הַתּוֹרָ֥ה\rb* \rb in the hearing|בְּאָזְנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb of|נֶ֥גֶד\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb Assemble|הַקְהֵ֣ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people—|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb men,|הָֽאֲנָשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb women,|וְהַנָּשִׁים֙\rb* \rb children,|וְהַטַּ֔ף\rb* \rb and the foreigners|וְגֵרְךָ֖\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb within your gates—|בִּשְׁעָרֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb they may listen|יִשְׁמְע֜וּ\rb*\rb |וּלְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb and learn|יִלְמְד֗וּ\rb* \rb to fear|וְיָֽרְאוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and to follow|לַעֲשׂ֔וֹת\rb* \rb carefully|וְשָֽׁמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb law.|הַתּוֹרָ֥ה\rb* \v 13 \rb Then their children|וּבְנֵיהֶ֞ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb know the law|יָדְע֗וּ\rb* \rb will listen|יִשְׁמְעוּ֙\rb* \rb and learn|וְלָ֣מְד֔וּ\rb* \rb to fear|לְיִרְאָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb as|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb long as you|אַתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb live|חַיִּים֙\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|הָ֣אֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֜ם\rb* \rb are crossing|עֹבְרִ֧ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֛ן\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb to possess.”|לְרִשְׁתָּֽהּ׃פ\rb*
\s1 God Commissions Joshua
\p \v 14 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb “Behold,|הֵ֣ן\rb* \rb the time|יָמֶיךָ֮\rb* \rb of your death|לָמוּת֒\rb* \rb is near.|קָרְב֣וּ\rb* \rb Call|קְרָ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֗עַ\rb* \rb and present yourselves|וְהִֽתְיַצְּב֛וּ\rb* \rb at the Tent|בְּאֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting,|מוֹעֵ֖ד\rb* \rb so that I may commission him.”|וַאֲצַוֶּ֑נּוּ\rb*
\p \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁה֙\rb* \rb and Joshua|וִֽיהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb and presented themselves|וַיִּֽתְיַצְּב֖וּ\rb* \rb at the Tent|בְּאֹ֥הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting.|מוֹעֵֽד׃\rb* \v 15 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb appeared|וַיֵּרָ֧א\rb* \rb at the tent|בָּאֹ֖הֶל\rb* \rb in a pillar|בְּעַמּ֣וּד\rb* \rb of cloud,|עָנָ֑ן\rb* \rb and the cloud|הֶעָנָ֖ן\rb* \rb stood|וַיַּעֲמֹ֛ד\rb*\rb |עַמּ֥וּד\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֥תַח\rb* \rb to the tent.|הָאֹֽהֶל׃ס\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “You will soon|הִנְּךָ֥\rb* \rb rest|שֹׁכֵ֖ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb your fathers,|אֲבֹתֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb and these|הַזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֨ם\rb* \rb will rise up|וְקָם֩\rb* \rb and prostitute themselves|וְזָנָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb with|אַחֲרֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb the foreign|נֵֽכַר־\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb they|ה֤וּא\rb* \rb are entering.|בָא־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֙מָּה֙\rb*\rb |בְּקִרְבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb They will forsake Me|וַעֲזָבַ֕נִי\rb* \rb and break|וְהֵפֵר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the covenant|בְּרִיתִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have made|כָּרַ֖תִּי\rb* \rb with them.|אִתּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb On that|הַ֠הוּא\rb* \rb day|בַיּוֹם־\rb* \rb My anger|אַפִּ֣י\rb* \rb will burn|וְחָרָ֣ה\rb* \rb against them,|ב֣וֹ\rb* \rb and I will abandon them|וַעֲזַבְתִּ֞ים\rb* \rb and hide|וְהִסְתַּרְתִּ֨י\rb* \rb My face|פָנַ֤י\rb* \rb from them,|מֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb so that they will be|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb consumed,|לֶֽאֱכֹ֔ל\rb* \rb and many|רַבּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb troubles|רָע֥וֹת\rb* \rb and afflictions|וְצָר֑וֹת\rb* \rb will befall them.|וּמְצָאֻ֛הוּ\rb*
\p \rb On that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb they will say,|וְאָמַר֙\rb* \rb ‘Have not|הֲלֹ֗א\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb disasters|הָרָע֥וֹת\rb* \rb come upon us|מְצָא֖וּנִי\rb* \rb because|עַ֣ל\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהַי֙\rb* \rb is no|אֵ֤ין\rb* \rb longer with us?’|בְּקִרְבִּ֔י\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb And|וְאָנֹכִ֗י\rb* \rb on that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb I will surely hide|הַסְתֵּ֨ר\rb*\rb |אַסְתִּ֤יר\rb* \rb My face|פָּנַי֙\rb* \rb because of|עַ֥ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the evil|הָרָעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they have done|עָשָׂ֑ה\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb by turning|פָנָ֔ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִֽים׃\rb* \rb gods.|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Now therefore,|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb write down|כִּתְב֤וּ\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb song|הַשִּׁירָ֣ה\rb* \rb and teach|וְלַמְּדָ֥הּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it to the Israelites;|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb have them recite|שִׂימָ֣הּ\rb* \rb it,|בְּפִיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb it|הַזֹּ֛את\rb*\rb |הַשִּׁירָ֥ה\rb* \rb may be|תִּהְיֶה־\rb* \rb a witness|לְעֵ֖ד\rb* \rb for Me|לִּ֜י\rb* \rb against them.|בִּבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 20 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I have brought them|אֲבִיאֶ֜נּוּ\rb* \rb into|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאֲדָמָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I swore|נִשְׁבַּ֣עְתִּי\rb* \rb to give their fathers,|לַאֲבֹתָ֗יו\rb* \rb a land flowing|זָבַ֤ת\rb* \rb with milk|חָלָב֙\rb* \rb and honey,|וּדְבַ֔שׁ\rb* \rb they will eat|וְאָכַ֥ל\rb* \rb their fill|וְשָׂבַ֖ע\rb* \rb and prosper.|וְדָשֵׁ֑ן\rb* \rb Then they will turn|וּפָנָ֞ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִים֙\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֤ים\rb* \rb and worship them,|וַעֲבָד֔וּם\rb* \rb and they will reject Me|וְנִ֣אֲצ֔וּנִי\rb* \rb and break|וְהֵפֵ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My covenant.|בְּרִיתִֽי׃\rb* \v 21 \rb |וְ֠הָיָה\rb* \rb And when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb many|רַבּוֹת֮\rb* \rb troubles|רָע֣וֹת\rb* \rb and afflictions|וְצָרוֹת֒\rb* \rb have come upon them,|תִמְצֶ֨אןָ\rb*\rb |אֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֤את\rb* \rb song|הַשִּׁירָ֨ה\rb* \rb will testify|וְ֠עָנְתָה\rb*\rb |לְעֵ֔ד\rb* \rb against them,|לְפָנָיו֙\rb* \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb it will not be forgotten|תִשָּׁכַ֖ח\rb* \rb from the lips|מִפִּ֣י\rb* \rb of their descendants.|זַרְע֑וֹ\rb* \rb For|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb I know|יָדַ֣עְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their inclination,|יִצְר֗וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*\rb |ה֤וּא\rb*\rb |עֹשֶׂה֙\rb*\rb |הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb even before|בְּטֶ֣רֶם\rb* \rb I bring them|אֲבִיאֶ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I swore to give them.”|נִשְׁבָּֽעְתִּי׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb So that very|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb wrote down|וַיִּכְתֹּ֥ב\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb song|הַשִּׁירָ֥ה\rb* \rb and taught it|וַֽיְלַמְּדָ֖הּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the Israelites.|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb Then the LORD commissioned|וַיְצַ֞ו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֣עַ\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun|נ֗וּן\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּאמֶר֮\rb* \rb “Be strong|חֲזַ֣ק\rb* \rb and courageous,|וֶֽאֱמָץ֒\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb will bring|תָּבִיא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I swore to give|נִשְׁבַּ֣עְתִּי\rb* \rb them,|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and I|וְאָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb will be|אֶֽהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb with you.”|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*
\s1 The Law Placed in the Ark
\p \v 24 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb When Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb had finished|כְּכַלּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb writing|לִכְתֹּ֛ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in a book|סֵ֑פֶר\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb law|הַתּוֹרָֽה־\rb*\rb |עַ֖ד\rb* \rb from beginning to end,|תֻּמָּֽם׃\rb* \v 25 \rb he gave this command to|וַיְצַ֤ו\rb*\rb |מֹשֶׁה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֔ם\rb* \rb who carried|נֹ֥שְׂאֵ֛י\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD:|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 26 \rb “Take|לָקֹ֗חַ\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb Book|סֵ֤פֶר\rb* \rb of the Law|הַתּוֹרָה֙\rb* \rb and place|וְשַׂמְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb it|אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb beside|מִצַּ֛ד\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֥וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb so that it may remain|וְהָֽיָה־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֥ם\rb* \rb as a witness|לְעֵֽד׃\rb* \rb against you.|בְּךָ֖\rb* \v 27 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֤י\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֙עְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb how rebellious|מֶרְיְךָ֔\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb and stiff-necked you are.|עָרְפְּךָ֖\rb*\rb |הַקָּשֶׁ֑ה\rb*\rb |הֵ֣ן\rb* \rb If you are already|הֱיִתֶם֙\rb*\rb |עִם־\rb* \rb rebelling|מַמְרִ֤ים\rb* \rb against|עִמָּכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהֹוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |הַיּ֗וֹם\rb* \rb while I am still|בְּעוֹדֶנִּי֩\rb* \rb alive,|חַ֨י\rb* \rb how much more|וְאַ֖ף\rb*\rb |כִּי־\rb* \rb will you rebel after|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb my death!|מוֹתִֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb Assemble|הַקְהִ֧ילוּ\rb* \rb before me|אֵלַ֛י\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of your tribes|שִׁבְטֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and all your officers|וְשֹׁטְרֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb so that I may speak|וַאֲדַבְּרָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb in their hearing|בְאָזְנֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and call heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb to witness|וְאָעִ֣ידָה\rb* \rb against them.|בָּ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 29 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I know|יָדַ֗עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֤י\rb* \rb my death|מוֹתִי֙\rb* \rb you will become utterly corrupt|הַשְׁחֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |תַּשְׁחִת֔וּן\rb* \rb and turn|וְסַרְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the path|הַדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have commanded you.|צִוִּ֖יתִי\rb* \rb And in|בְּאַחֲרִ֣ית\rb* \rb the days to come,|הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb disaster|הָֽרָעָה֙\rb* \rb will befall|וְקָרָ֨את\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you will do|תַעֲשׂ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb evil|הָרַע֙\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb to provoke Him to anger|לְהַכְעִיס֖וֹ\rb* \rb by the work|בְּמַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb of your hands.”|יְדֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\s1 Moses Begins His Song
\p \v 30 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb*\rb |בְּאָזְנֵי֙\rb* \rb recited aloud|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb assembly|קְהַ֣ל\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb song|הַשִּׁירָ֖ה\rb* \rb from beginning|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb to end:|תֻּמָּֽם׃פ\rb*
\c 32
\s1 The Song of Moses
\r \ref Revelation 15:1–4|REV 15:1-4\ref*)
\q1 \v 1 \rb Give ear,|הַאֲזִ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb O heavens,|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and I will speak;|וַאֲדַבֵּ֑רָה\rb*
\q2 \rb hear,|וְתִשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb O earth,|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb the words|אִמְרֵי־\rb* \rb of my mouth.|פִֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb Let my teaching|לִקְחִ֔י\rb* \rb fall|יַעֲרֹ֤ף\rb* \rb like rain|כַּמָּטָר֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and my speech|אִמְרָתִ֑י\rb* \rb settle|תִּזַּ֥ל\rb* \rb like dew,|כַּטַּ֖ל\rb*
\q1 \rb like gentle rain|כִּשְׂעִירִ֣ם\rb* \rb on|עֲלֵי־\rb* \rb new grass,|דֶ֔שֶׁא\rb*
\q2 \rb like showers|וְכִרְבִיבִ֖ים\rb* \rb on|עֲלֵי־\rb* \rb tender plants.|עֵֽשֶׂב׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I will proclaim|אֶקְרָ֑א\rb* \rb the name|שֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*
\q2 \rb Ascribe|הָב֥וּ\rb* \rb greatness|גֹ֖דֶל\rb* \rb to our God!|לֵאלֹהֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb He is the Rock,|הַצּוּר֙\rb* \rb His work|פָּעֳל֔וֹ\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb is perfect;|תָּמִ֣ים\rb*
\q2 \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb His ways|דְּרָכָ֖יו\rb* \rb are just.|מִשְׁפָּ֑ט\rb*
\q1 \rb A God|אֵ֤ל\rb* \rb of faithfulness|אֱמוּנָה֙\rb* \rb without|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb injustice,|עָ֔וֶל\rb*
\q2 \rb righteous|צַדִּ֥יק\rb* \rb and upright|וְיָשָׁ֖ר\rb* \rb is He.|הֽוּא׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb His people have acted corruptly|שִׁחֵ֥ת\rb* \rb toward Him;|ל֛וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb the blemish on them is|מוּמָ֑ם\rb* \rb not|לֹ֖א\rb* \rb that of His children,|בָּנָ֣יו\rb*
\q2 \rb but of a perverse|עִקֵּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb and crooked|וּפְתַלְתֹּֽל׃\rb* \rb generation.|דּ֥וֹר\rb*\f + \fr 32:5 \ft Cited in \ref Philippians 2:15|PHP 2:15\ref*\f*
\q1 \v 6 \rb Is this|זֹ֔את\rb* \rb how you repay|תִּגְמְלוּ־\rb* \rb the LORD,|לַיְהוָה֙\rb*
\q2 \rb O foolish|נָבָ֖ל\rb* \rb and senseless|וְלֹ֣א\rb*\rb |חָכָ֑ם\rb* \rb people?|עַ֥ם\rb*
\q1 \rb Is He|הוּא֙\rb* \rb not|הֲלוֹא־\rb* \rb your Father|אָבִ֣יךָ\rb* \rb and Creator?|קָּנֶ֔ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb Has He not|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb made you|עָֽשְׂךָ֖\rb* \rb and established you?|וַֽיְכֹנְנֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb Remember|זְכֹר֙\rb* \rb the days|יְמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of old;|עוֹלָ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb consider|בִּ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb the years|שְׁנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb long|דּוֹר־\rb* \rb past.|וָד֑וֹר\rb*
\q1 \rb Ask|שְׁאַ֤ל\rb* \rb your father,|אָבִ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb and he will tell you,|וְיַגֵּ֔דְךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb your elders,|זְקֵנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and they will inform|וְיֹ֥אמְרוּ\rb* \rb you.|לָֽךְ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb When the Most High|עֶלְיוֹן֙\rb* \rb gave the nations|גּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb their inheritance,|בְּהַנְחֵ֤ל\rb*
\q2 \rb when He divided|בְּהַפְרִיד֖וֹ\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of man,|אָדָ֑ם\rb*
\q1 \rb He set|יַצֵּב֙\rb* \rb the boundaries|גְּבֻלֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of the peoples|עַמִּ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb according to the number|לְמִסְפַּ֖ר\rb* \rb of the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of God.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*\f + \fr 32:8 \ft DSS; LXX \fqa according to the number of the angels of God\ft ; MT \fqa according to the number of the sons of Israel\f*
\q1 \v 9 \rb But|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהֹוָ֖ה\rb* \rb portion|חֵ֥לֶק\rb* \rb is His people,|עַמּ֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֖ב\rb* \rb His allotted|חֶ֥בֶל\rb* \rb inheritance.|נַחֲלָתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb He found him|יִמְצָאֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb in a desert|מִדְבָּ֔ר\rb* \rb land,|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb in a barren,|וּבְתֹ֖הוּ\rb* \rb howling|יְלֵ֣ל\rb* \rb wilderness;|יְשִׁמֹ֑ן\rb*
\q1 \rb He surrounded him,|יְסֹֽבְבֶ֙נְהוּ֙\rb* \rb He instructed him,|יְב֣וֹנְנֵ֔הוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb He guarded him|יִצְּרֶ֖נְהוּ\rb* \rb as the apple|כְּאִישׁ֥וֹן\rb*\f + \fr 32:10 \ft Literally \fqa the pupil\f* \rb of His eye.|עֵינֽוֹ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 11 \rb As an eagle|כְּנֶ֙שֶׁר֙\rb* \rb stirs up|יָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb its nest|קִנּ֔וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb and hovers|יְרַחֵ֑ף\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb its young,|גּוֹזָלָ֖יו\rb*
\q1 \rb He spread|יִפְרֹ֤שׂ\rb* \rb His wings|כְּנָפָיו֙\rb* \rb to catch them|יִקָּחֵ֔הוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and carried them|יִשָּׂאֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb His pinions.|אֶבְרָתֽוֹ׃\rb*\f + \fr 32:11 \fqa Pinions \ft are the outer parts of a bird’s wings, including the flight feathers.\f*
\q1 \v 12 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb alone|בָּדָ֣ד\rb* \rb led him,|יַנְחֶ֑נּוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb foreign|נֵכָֽר׃\rb* \rb god|אֵ֥ל\rb* \rb was with him.|עִמּ֖וֹ\rb*
\q1 \v 13 \rb He made him ride|יַרְכִּבֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the heights|בָּמוֹתֵי\rb* \rb of the land|אָ֔רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb and fed him|וַיֹּאכַ֖ל\rb* \rb the produce|תְּנוּבֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of the field.|שָׂדָ֑י\rb*
\q1 \rb He nourished him|וַיֵּנִקֵ֤הֽוּ\rb* \rb with honey|דְבַשׁ֙\rb* \rb from the rock|מִסֶּ֔לַע\rb*
\q2 \rb and oil|וְשֶׁ֖מֶן\rb* \rb from the flinty|מֵחַלְמִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb crag,|צֽוּר׃\rb*
\q1 \v 14 \rb with curds|חֶמְאַ֨ת\rb* \rb from the herd|בָּקָ֜ר\rb* \rb and milk|וַחֲלֵ֣ב\rb* \rb from the flock,|צֹ֗אן\rb*
\q2 \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the fat|חֵ֨לֶב\rb* \rb of lambs,|כָּרִ֜ים\rb*
\q1 \rb with rams|וְאֵילִ֤ים\rb* \rb from Bashan,|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |בָשָׁן֙\rb* \rb and goats,|וְעַתּוּדִ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the choicest|חֵ֖לֶב\rb* \rb grains|כִּלְי֣וֹת\rb* \rb of wheat.|חִטָּ֑ה\rb*
\q1 \rb From the juice|וְדַם־\rb* \rb of the finest grapes|עֵנָ֖ב\rb*
\q2 \rb you drank|תִּשְׁתֶּה־\rb* \rb the wine.|חָֽמֶר׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb But Jeshurun|יְשֻׁרוּן֙\rb*\f + \fr 32:15 \fqa Jeshurun \ft means \fqa the upright one\ft , a term of endearment for Israel.\f* \rb grew fat|וַיִּשְׁמַ֤ן\rb* \rb and kicked—|וַיִּבְעָ֔ט\rb*
\q2 \rb becoming fat,|שָׁמַ֖נְתָּ\rb* \rb bloated,|עָבִ֣יתָ\rb* \rb and gorged.|כָּשִׂ֑יתָ\rb*
\q1 \rb He abandoned|וַיִּטֹּשׁ֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱל֣וֹהַ\rb* \rb who made him|עָשָׂ֔הוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and scorned|וַיְנַבֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb the Rock|צ֥וּר\rb* \rb of his salvation.|יְשֻׁעָתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb They provoked His jealousy|יַקְנִאֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb with foreign gods;|בְּזָרִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb they enraged Him|יַכְעִיסֻֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb with abominations.|בְּתוֹעֵבֹ֖ת\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb They sacrificed|יִזְבְּח֗וּ\rb* \rb to demons,|לַשֵּׁדִים֙\rb* \rb not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb to God,|אֱלֹ֔הַ\rb*
\q2 \rb to gods|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb they had not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb known,|יְדָע֑וּם\rb*
\q1 \rb to newly arrived gods,|חֲדָשִׁים֙\rb*\rb |מִקָּרֹ֣ב\rb*\rb |בָּ֔אוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb which your fathers|אֲבֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb fear.|שְׂעָר֖וּם\rb*
\q1 \v 18 \rb You ignored|תֶּ֑שִׁי\rb* \rb the Rock|צ֥וּר\rb* \rb who brought you forth;|יְלָדְךָ֖\rb*
\q2 \rb you forgot|וַתִּשְׁכַּ֖ח\rb* \rb the God|אֵ֥ל\rb* \rb who gave you birth.|מְחֹלְלֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 19 \rb When the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb saw this,|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb* \rb He rejected them,|וַיִּנְאָ֑ץ\rb*
\q2 \rb provoked to anger|מִכַּ֥עַס\rb* \rb by His sons|בָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb and daughters.|וּבְנֹתָֽיו׃\rb*
\q1 \v 20 \rb He said:|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “I will hide|אַסְתִּ֤ירָה\rb* \rb My face from them;|פָנַי֙\rb*
\q2 \rb I will see|אֶרְאֶ֖ה\rb* \rb what will be|מָ֣ה\rb* \rb their end.|אַחֲרִיתָ֑ם\rb*
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |מֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb they are a perverse|תַּהְפֻּכֹת֙\rb*\rb |הֵ֔מָּה\rb* \rb generation—|ד֤וֹר\rb*
\q2 \rb children|בָּנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb of unfaithfulness.|אֵמֻ֥ן\rb*
\q1 \v 21 \rb They|הֵ֚ם\rb* \rb have provoked My jealousy|קִנְא֣וּנִי\rb* \rb by that which is not|בְלֹא־\rb* \rb God;|אֵ֔ל\rb*
\q2 \rb they have enraged Me|כִּעֲס֖וּנִי\rb* \rb with their worthless idols.|בְּהַבְלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*
\q1 \rb So I|וַאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb will make them jealous|אַקְנִיאֵ֣ם\rb* \rb by those who are not|בְּלֹא־\rb* \rb a people;|עָ֔ם\rb*\f + \fr 32:21 \ft Or \fqa not a nation\ft ; see also LXX.\f*
\q2 \rb I will make them angry|אַכְעִיסֵֽם׃\rb* \rb by a nation|בְּג֥וֹי\rb* \rb without understanding.|נָבָ֖ל\rb*\f + \fr 32:21 \ft Cited in \ref Romans 10:19|ROM 10:19\ref*\f*
\q1 \v 22 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb a fire|אֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb has been kindled|קָדְחָ֣ה\rb* \rb by My anger,|בְאַפִּ֔י\rb*
\q2 \rb and it burns|וַתִּיקַ֖ד\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the depths|תַּחְתִּ֑ית\rb* \rb of Sheol;|שְׁא֣וֹל\rb*
\q1 \rb it consumes|וַתֹּ֤אכַל\rb* \rb the earth|אֶ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb and its produce,|וִֽיבֻלָ֔הּ\rb*
