\p \v 44 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb with Joshua|וְהוֹשֵׁ֥עַ\rb*\f + \fr 32:44 \ft LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate; Hebrew \fqa Hoshea\ft , a variant of \fqa Joshua\f* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun|נֽוּן׃\rb* \rb and recited|וַיְדַבֵּ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb song|הַשִּׁירָֽה־\rb* \rb in the hearing|בְּאָזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the people.|הָעָ֑ם\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \v 45 \rb When Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb had finished|וַיְכַ֣ל\rb* \rb reciting|לְדַבֵּ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 46 \rb he said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb “Take|שִׂ֣ימוּ\rb* \rb to heart|לְבַבְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the words|הַדְּבָרִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb have solemnly declared|מֵעִ֥יד\rb* \rb to you|בָּכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb this day,|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb so that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you may command|תְּצַוֻּם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your children|בְּנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to carefully|לִשְׁמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb follow|לַעֲשׂ֔וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb law.|הַתּוֹרָ֥ה\rb* \v 47 \rb For|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb they|הוּא֙\rb* \rb are not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb idle|רֵ֥ק\rb* \rb words|דָבָ֨ר\rb* \rb to you,|מִכֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb they|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb are your life,|חַיֵּיכֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |וּבַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb and by them|הַזֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb you will live long|תַּאֲרִ֤יכוּ\rb*\rb |יָמִים֙\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|הָ֣אֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֜ם\rb* \rb are crossing|עֹבְרִ֧ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֛ן\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb to possess.”|לְרִשְׁתָּֽהּ׃פ\rb*
\s1 Moses’ Death Foretold
\p \v 48 \rb On that|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb same|בְּעֶ֛צֶם\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \v 49 \rb “Go up|עֲלֵ֡ה\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Abarim|הָעֲבָרִ֨ים\rb* \rb Range|הַר֩\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb to Mount|הַר־\rb* \rb Nebo,|נְב֗וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb across|עַל־\rb* \rb from|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Jericho,|יְרֵח֑וֹ\rb* \rb and view|וּרְאֵה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan,|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am giving|נֹתֵ֛ן\rb* \rb to the Israelites|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb as their own possession.|לַאֲחֻזָּֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 50 \rb And there|שָׁ֔מָּה\rb* \rb on the mountain|בָּהָר֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb climb,|עֹלֶ֣ה\rb* \rb you will die|וּמֻ֗ת\rb* \rb and be gathered|וְהֵאָסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your people,|עַמֶּ֑יךָ\rb* \rb just as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb your brother|אָחִ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb Aaron|אַהֲרֹ֤ן\rb* \rb died|מֵ֞ת\rb* \rb on Mount|הָהָ֔ר\rb* \rb Hor|בְּהֹ֣ר\rb* \rb and was gathered|וַיֵּאָ֖סֶף\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his people.|עַמָּֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 51 \rb For|עַל֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb at the waters|בְּמֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Meribah-kadesh|מְרִיבַ֥ת\rb*\rb |קָדֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb in the Wilderness|מִדְבַּר־\rb* \rb of Zin,|צִ֑ן\rb* \rb both of you broke faith|מְעַלְתֶּ֜ם\rb* \rb with Me|בִּ֗י\rb* \rb among|בְּתוֹךְ֙\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb by|עַ֣ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb failing|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to treat Me as holy|קִדַּשְׁתֶּם֙\rb*\rb |אוֹתִ֔י\rb* \rb in their|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb presence.|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \v 52 \rb Although|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you shall see|תִּרְאֶ֣ה\rb* \rb from a distance|מִנֶּ֖גֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am giving|נֹתֵ֖ן\rb* \rb the Israelites,|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb* \rb you shall not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb enter|תָב֔וֹא\rb* \rb it.”|אֶל־\rb*\rb |הָאָ֕רֶץ\rb*\rb |וְשָׁ֙מָּה֙\rb*
\c 33
\s1 Moses Blesses the Twelve Tribes
\p \v 1 \rb This|וְזֹ֣את\rb* \rb is the blessing|הַבְּרָכָ֗ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb the man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb pronounced|בֵּרַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb upon the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb his death.|מוֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 2 \rb He said:|וַיֹּאמַ֗ר\rb*
\q1 \rb “The LORD|יְהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb came|בָּא֙\rb* \rb from Sinai|מִסִּינַ֥י\rb*
\q2 \rb and dawned|וְזָרַ֤ח\rb* \rb upon us|לָ֔מוֹ\rb*\f + \fr 33:2 \ft LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate; Hebrew \fqa upon them\f* \rb from Seir;|מִשֵּׂעִיר֙\rb*
\q1 \rb He shone forth|הוֹפִ֙יעַ֙\rb* \rb from Mount|מֵהַ֣ר\rb* \rb Paran|פָּארָ֔ן\rb*
\q2 \rb and came|וְאָתָ֖ה\rb* \rb with myriads|מֵרִבְבֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of holy ones,|קֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb with flaming fire|אֵשְׁדָּת\rb* \rb at His right hand.|מִֽימִינ֕וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 33:2 \ft Or \fqa with myriads of holy ones from the south, from His mountain slopes\f*
\q1 \v 3 \rb Surely|אַ֚ף\rb* \rb You love|חֹבֵ֣ב\rb* \rb the people;|עַמִּ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the holy ones are|קְדֹשָׁ֖יו\rb* \rb in Your hand,|בְּיָדֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\q1 \rb and they|וְהֵם֙\rb* \rb sit down|תֻּכּ֣וּ\rb* \rb at Your feet;|לְרַגְלֶ֔ךָ\rb*\f + \fr 33:3 \ft Or \fqa they follow in Your steps\f*
\q2 \rb each receives|יִשָּׂ֖א\rb* \rb Your words—|מִדַּבְּרֹתֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb the law|תּוֹרָ֥ה\rb* \rb that Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb gave|צִוָּה־\rb* \rb us,|לָ֖נוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb the possession|מוֹרָשָׁ֖ה\rb* \rb of the assembly|קְהִלַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of Jacob.|יַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb So the LORD became|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb King|מֶ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb in Jeshurun|בִישֻׁר֖וּן\rb*\f + \fr 33:5 \fqa Jeshurun \ft means \fqa the upright one\ft , a term of endearment for Israel; also in verse 26.\f*
\q2 \rb when the leaders|רָ֣אשֵׁי\rb* \rb of the people|עָ֔ם\rb* \rb gathered,|בְּהִתְאַסֵּף֙\rb*
\q2 \rb when the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb came together.|יַ֖חַד\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb Let Reuben|רְאוּבֵ֖ן\rb* \rb live|יְחִ֥י\rb* \rb and not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb die,|יָמֹ֑ת\rb*
\q2 \rb nor|וִיהִ֥י\rb*\f + \fr 33:6 \ft Or \fqa but let\f* \rb his men|מְתָ֖יו\rb* \rb be few.”|מִסְפָּֽר׃ס\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb And|וְזֹ֣את\rb* \rb concerning Judah|לִֽיהוּדָה֮\rb* \rb he said:|וַיֹּאמַר֒\rb*
\q1 \rb “O LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb hear|שְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb the cry|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and bring him|תְּבִיאֶ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb his people.|עַמּ֖וֹ\rb*
\q1 \rb With his own hands|יָדָיו֙\rb* \rb he defends his cause,|רָ֣ב\rb*\rb |ל֔וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb but may You be|תִּהְיֶֽה׃ס\rb* \rb a help|וְעֵ֥זֶר\rb* \rb against his foes.”|מִצָּרָ֖יו\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Concerning Levi|וּלְלֵוִ֣י\rb* \rb he said:|אָמַ֔ר\rb*
\q1 \rb “Give Your Thummim to Levi|תֻּמֶּ֥יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and Your Urim|וְאוּרֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb to Your godly|חֲסִידֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb one,|לְאִ֣ישׁ\rb*\f + \fr 33:8 \ft DSS and LXX; MT does not include \fqa to Levi\ft ; literally \fqa Let Your Perfections and Your Lights be to Your godly one\ft .\f*
\q1 \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb You tested|נִסִּיתוֹ֙\rb* \rb at Massah|בְּמַסָּ֔ה\rb*\f + \fr 33:8 \fqa Massah \ft means \fqa testing\ft ; see \ref Exodus 17:7|EXO 17:7\ref*.\f*
\q2 \rb and contested|תְּרִיבֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the waters|מֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Meribah.|מְרִיבָֽה׃\rb*\f + \fr 33:8 \fqa Meribah \ft means \fqa quarreling\ft ; see \ref Exodus 17:7|EXO 17:7\ref*.\f*
\q1 \v 9 \rb He said|הָאֹמֵ֞ר\rb* \rb of his father|לְאָבִ֤יו\rb* \rb and mother,|וּלְאִמּוֹ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb ‘I do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb consider them.’|רְאִיתִ֔יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*
\q1 \rb He disregarded|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |הִכִּ֔יר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָיו֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb know|יָדָ֑ע\rb* \rb his own sons,|בָּנוֹ\rb*
\q1 \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb he kept|שָֽׁמְרוּ֙\rb*\f + \fr 33:9 \ft Hebrew \fqa they kept\ft , most likely referring to Levi in the plural; similarly twice in verse 10\f* \rb Your word|אִמְרָתֶ֔ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and maintained|יִנְצֹֽרוּ׃\rb* \rb Your covenant.|וּבְרִֽיתְךָ֖\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb He will teach|יוֹר֤וּ\rb* \rb Your ordinances|מִשְׁפָּטֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb to Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*
\q2 \rb and Your law|וְתוֹרָתְךָ֖\rb* \rb to Israel;|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*
\q1 \rb he will set|יָשִׂ֤ימוּ\rb* \rb incense|קְטוֹרָה֙\rb* \rb before You|בְּאַפֶּ֔ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and whole burnt offerings|וְכָלִ֖יל\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb Your altar.|מִזְבְּחֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 11 \rb Bless|בָּרֵ֤ךְ\rb* \rb his substance,|חֵיל֔וֹ\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and accept|תִּרְצֶ֑ה\rb* \rb the work|וּפֹ֥עַל\rb* \rb of his hands.|יָדָ֖יו\rb*
\q1 \rb Smash|מְחַ֨ץ\rb* \rb the loins|מָתְנַ֧יִם\rb* \rb of those who rise against him,|קָמָ֛יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and of his foes|וּמְשַׂנְאָ֖יו\rb* \rb so they can|מִן־\rb* \rb rise no more.”|יְקוּמֽוּן׃ס\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb Concerning Benjamin|לְבִנְיָמִ֣ן\rb* \rb he said:|אָמַ֔ר\rb*
\q1 \rb “May the beloved|יְדִ֣יד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהֹוָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb rest|יִשְׁכֹּ֥ן\rb* \rb secure|לָבֶ֖טַח\rb* \rb in Him;|עָלָ֑יו\rb*
\q1 \rb God shields|חֹפֵ֤ף\rb*\f + \fr 33:12 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa He shields\f* \rb him|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb day long,|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb*
\q2 \rb and upon His shoulders|כְּתֵיפָ֖יו\rb* \rb he rests.”|שָׁכֵֽן׃ס\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb Concerning Joseph|וּלְיוֹסֵ֣ף\rb* \rb he said:|אָמַ֔ר\rb*
\q1 \rb “May his land|אַרְצ֑וֹ\rb* \rb be blessed|מְבֹרֶ֥כֶת\rb* \rb by the LORD|יְהֹוָ֖ה\rb*
\q2 \rb with the precious|מִמֶּ֤גֶד\rb* \rb dew|מִטָּ֔ל\rb* \rb from heaven above|שָׁמַ֙יִם֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and the deep waters|וּמִתְּה֖וֹם\rb* \rb that lie|רֹבֶ֥צֶת\rb* \rb beneath,|תָּֽחַת׃\rb*
\q1 \v 14 \rb with the bountiful|וּמִמֶּ֖גֶד\rb* \rb harvest|תְּבוּאֹ֣ת\rb* \rb from the sun|שָׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb and the abundant|וּמִמֶּ֖גֶד\rb* \rb yield|גֶּ֥רֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the seasons,|יְרָחִֽים׃\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb with the best|וּמֵרֹ֖אשׁ\rb* \rb of the ancient|קֶ֑דֶם\rb* \rb mountains|הַרְרֵי־\rb*
\q2 \rb and the bounty|וּמִמֶּ֖גֶד\rb* \rb of the everlasting|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb hills,|גִּבְע֥וֹת\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb with the choice gifts|וּמִמֶּ֗גֶד\rb* \rb of the land|אֶ֚רֶץ\rb* \rb and everything in it,|וּמְלֹאָ֔הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and with the favor|וּרְצ֥וֹן\rb* \rb of Him who dwelt|שֹׁכְנִ֖י\rb* \rb in the burning bush.|סְנֶ֑ה\rb*
\q1 \rb May these rest|תָּב֙וֹאתָה֙\rb* \rb on the head|לְרֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb*
\q2 \rb and crown the brow|וּלְקָדְקֹ֖ד\rb* \rb of the prince|נְזִ֥יר\rb* \rb of his brothers.|אֶחָֽיו׃\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb His|ל֗וֹ\rb* \rb majesty is like|הָדָ֣ר\rb* \rb a firstborn|בְּכ֨וֹר\rb* \rb bull,|שׁוֹר֜וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb and his horns|וְקַרְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb are like those|קַרְנָ֔יו\rb* \rb of a wild ox.|רְאֵם֙\rb*
\q1 \rb With them he will gore|יְנַגַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |יַחְדָּ֖ו\rb* \rb the nations,|עַמִּ֛ים\rb*
\q2 \rb even to the ends|אַפְסֵי־\rb* \rb of the earth.|אָ֑רֶץ\rb*
\q1 \rb Such|וְהֵם֙\rb* \rb are the myriads|רִבְב֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Ephraim,|אֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb and such|וְהֵ֖ם\rb* \rb are the thousands|אַלְפֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Manasseh.”|מְנַשֶּֽׁה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Concerning Zebulun|וְלִזְבוּלֻ֣ן\rb* \rb he said:|אָמַ֔ר\rb*
\q1 \rb “Rejoice,|שְׂמַ֥ח\rb* \rb Zebulun,|זְבוּלֻ֖ן\rb* \rb in your journeys,|בְּצֵאתֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and Issachar,|וְיִשָּׂשכָ֖ר\rb* \rb in your tents.|בְּאֹהָלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 19 \rb They will call|יִקְרָ֔אוּ\rb* \rb the peoples|עַמִּים֙\rb* \rb to a mountain;|הַר־\rb*
\q2 \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb they will offer|יִזְבְּח֣וּ\rb* \rb sacrifices|זִבְחֵי־\rb* \rb of righteousness.|צֶ֑דֶק\rb*
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they will feast on|יִינָ֔קוּ\rb* \rb the abundance|שֶׁ֤פַע\rb* \rb of the seas|יַמִּים֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and the hidden|וּשְׂפוּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb treasures|טְמ֥וּנֵי\rb* \rb of the sand.”|חֽוֹל׃ס\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb Concerning Gad|וּלְגָ֣ד\rb* \rb he said:|אָמַ֔ר\rb*
\q1 \rb “Blessed is|בָּר֖וּךְ\rb* \rb he who enlarges|מַרְחִ֣יב\rb*
\q2 \rb the domain of Gad!|גָּ֑ד\rb*
\q1 \rb He lies down|שָׁכֵ֔ן\rb* \rb like a lion|כְּלָבִ֣יא\rb*
\q2 \rb and tears off|וְטָרַ֥ף\rb* \rb an arm|זְר֖וֹעַ\rb* \rb or|אַף־\rb* \rb a head.|קָדְקֹֽד׃\rb*
\q1 \v 21 \rb He chose|וַיַּ֤רְא\rb* \rb the best land|רֵאשִׁית֙\rb* \rb for himself,|ל֔וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb a ruler’s|מְחֹקֵ֖ק\rb* \rb portion|חֶלְקַ֥ת\rb* \rb was reserved for him|סָפ֑וּן\rb* \rb there.|שָׁ֛ם\rb*
\q1 \rb He came|וַיֵּתֵא֙\rb* \rb with the leaders|רָ֣אשֵׁי\rb* \rb of the people;|עָ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb he administered|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb justice|צִדְקַ֤ת\rb*
\q2 \rb and His ordinances|וּמִשְׁפָּטָ֖יו\rb* \rb for|עִם־\rb* \rb Israel.”|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb Concerning Dan|וּלְדָ֣ן\rb* \rb he said:|אָמַ֔ר\rb*
\q1 \rb “Dan is|דָּ֖ן\rb* \rb a lion’s|אַרְיֵ֑ה\rb* \rb cub,|גּ֣וּר\rb*
\q2 \rb leaping|יְזַנֵּ֖ק\rb* \rb out of|מִן־\rb* \rb Bashan.”|הַבָּשָֽׁן׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb Concerning Naphtali|וּלְנַפְתָּלִ֣י\rb* \rb he said:|אָמַ֔ר\rb*
\q1 \rb “Naphtali|נַפְתָּלִי֙\rb* \rb is abounding|שְׂבַ֣ע\rb* \rb with favor,|רָצ֔וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb full|וּמָלֵ֖א\rb* \rb of the blessing|בִּרְכַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the LORD;|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q1 \rb he shall take possession|יְרָֽשָׁה׃ס\rb*
\q2 \rb of the sea|יָ֥ם\rb*\f + \fr 33:23 \ft Or \fqa the west\f* \rb and the south.”|וְדָר֖וֹם\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb And concerning Asher|וּלְאָשֵׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he said:|אָמַ֔ר\rb*
\q1 \rb “May Asher|אָשֵׁ֑ר\rb* \rb be the most blessed|בָּר֥וּךְ\rb* \rb of sons;|מִבָּנִ֖ים\rb*
\q2 \rb may he be|יְהִ֤י\rb* \rb the most favored|רְצוּי֙\rb* \rb among his brothers|אֶחָ֔יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and dip|וְטֹבֵ֥ל\rb* \rb his foot|רַגְלֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb in oil.|בַּשֶּׁ֖מֶן\rb*
\q1 \v 25 \rb May the bolts of your gate|מִנְעָלֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb be iron|בַּרְזֶ֥ל\rb* \rb and bronze,|וּנְחֹ֖שֶׁת\rb*
\q2 \rb and may your strength|דָּבְאֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb match your days.”|וּכְיָמֶ֖יךָ\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 26 \rb “There is none|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb like the God|כָּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb of Jeshurun,|יְשֻׁר֑וּן\rb*
\q2 \rb who rides|רֹכֵ֤ב\rb* \rb the heavens|שָׁמַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb to your aid,|בְעֶזְרֶ֔ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and the clouds|שְׁחָקִֽים׃\rb* \rb in His majesty.|וּבְגַאֲוָת֖וֹ\rb*
\q1 \v 27 \rb The eternal|קֶ֔דֶם\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹ֣הֵי\rb* \rb is your dwelling place,|מְעֹנָה֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and underneath|וּמִתַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb are the everlasting|עוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb arms.|זְרֹעֹ֣ת\rb*
\q1 \rb He drives out|וַיְגָ֧רֶשׁ\rb* \rb the enemy|אוֹיֵ֖ב\rb* \rb before you,|מִפָּנֶ֛יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb giving the command,|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb ‘Destroy him!’|הַשְׁמֵֽד׃\rb*
\q1 \v 28 \rb So Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֨ל\rb* \rb dwells|וַיִּשְׁכֹּן֩\rb* \rb securely;|בֶּ֤טַח\rb*
\q2 \rb the fountain|עֵ֣ין\rb* \rb of Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb lives untroubled|בָּדָד֙\rb*
\q1 \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of grain|דָּגָ֣ן\rb* \rb and new wine,|וְתִיר֑וֹשׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb where even|אַף־\rb* \rb the heavens|שָׁמָ֖יו\rb* \rb drip|יַֽעַרְפוּ\rb* \rb with dew.|טָֽל׃\rb*
\q1 \v 29 \rb Blessed are you,|אַשְׁרֶ֨יךָ\rb* \rb O Israel!|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb*
\q2 \rb Who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb is like you,|כָמ֗וֹךָ\rb* \rb a people|עַ֚ם\rb* \rb saved|נוֹשַׁ֣ע\rb* \rb by the LORD?|בַּֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*
\q1 \rb He is the shield|מָגֵ֣ן\rb* \rb that protects you,|עֶזְרֶ֔ךָ\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁר־\rb*
\q2 \rb the sword|חֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb in which you boast.|גַּאֲוָתֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\q1 \rb Your enemies|אֹיְבֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb will cower before you,|וְיִכָּֽחֲשׁ֤וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb shall trample|תִדְרֹֽךְ׃ס\rb* \rb their high places.”|בָּמוֹתֵ֥ימוֹ\rb*
\c 34
\s1 The Death of Moses
\p \v 1 \rb Then Moses|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֨עַל\rb* \rb from the plains|מֵֽעַרְבֹ֤ת\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Mount|הַ֣ר\rb* \rb Nebo,|נְב֔וֹ\rb* \rb to the top|רֹ֚אשׁ\rb* \rb of Pisgah,|הַפִּסְגָּ֔ה\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb faces|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Jericho.|יְרֵח֑וֹ\rb* \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb showed him|וַיַּרְאֵ֨הוּ\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb land—|הָאָ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from Gilead|הַגִּלְעָ֖ד\rb* \rb as far|עַד־\rb* \rb as Dan,|דָּֽן׃\rb* \v 2 \rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb of Naphtali,|נַפְתָּלִ֔י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and Manasseh,|וּמְנַשֶּׁ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb as far as|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb the Western|הָאַחֲרֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb Sea,|הַיָּ֥ם\rb*\f + \fr 34:2 \ft That is, the Mediterranean Sea, also called the Great Sea\f* \v 3 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Negev,|הַנֶּ֗גֶב\rb*\rb |וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb and the region|הַכִּכָּ֞ר\rb* \rb from the Valley|בִּקְעַ֧ת\rb* \rb of Jericho|יְרֵח֛וֹ\rb* \rb (the City|עִ֥יר\rb* \rb of Palms)|הַתְּמָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb all the way|עַד־\rb* \rb to Zoar.|צֹֽעַר׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to him,|אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb “This|זֹ֤את\rb* \rb is the land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I swore to give|נִ֠שְׁבַּעְתִּי\rb* \rb Abraham,|לְאַבְרָהָ֨ם\rb* \rb Isaac,|לְיִצְחָ֤ק\rb* \rb and Jacob|וּֽלְיַעֲקֹב֙\rb* \rb when I said,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘I will give|אֶתְּנֶ֑נָּה\rb* \rb it to your descendants.’|לְזַרְעֲךָ֖\rb* \rb I have let you see|הֶרְאִיתִ֣יךָ\rb* \rb it with your own eyes,|בְעֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |וְשָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb but you will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb cross into it.”|תַעֲבֹֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb So Moses|מֹשֶׁ֧ה\rb* \rb the servant|עֶֽבֶד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֨מָת\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֜ם\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Moab,|מוֹאָ֖ב\rb* \rb as|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb had said.|פִּ֥י\rb* \v 6 \rb And He buried|וַיִּקְבֹּ֨ר\rb* \rb him|אֹת֤וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 34:6 \ft SP and some LXX manuscripts \fqa they buried him\f* \rb in a valley|בַגַּיְ֙\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb facing|מ֖וּל\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb Beth-peor,|פְּע֑וֹר\rb* \rb and no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb one|אִישׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb knows|יָדַ֥ע\rb* \rb the location of his grave.|קְבֻ֣רָת֔וֹ\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Moses was|וּמֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb a hundred|מֵאָ֧ה\rb* \rb and twenty|וְעֶשְׂרִ֛ים\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb when he died,|בְּמֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb yet his eyes|עֵינ֖וֹ\rb* \rb were not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb weak,|כָהֲתָ֥ה\rb* \rb and his vitality|לֵחֹֽה׃\rb* \rb had not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb diminished.|נָ֥ס\rb* \v 8 \rb The Israelites|בְנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֧ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb grieved|וַיִּבְכּוּ֩\rb* \rb for Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb* \rb in the plains|בְּעַֽרְבֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֖ב\rb* \rb thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb days,|י֑וֹם\rb* \rb until the time|יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of weeping|בְכִ֖י\rb* \rb and mourning|אֵ֥בֶל\rb* \rb for Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb* \rb came to an end.|וַֽיִּתְּמ֔וּ\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Now Joshua|וִֽיהוֹשֻׁ֣עַ\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun|נ֗וּן\rb* \rb was filled|מָלֵא֙\rb* \rb with the spirit|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of wisdom|חָכְמָ֔ה\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had laid|סָמַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb his hands|יָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb on him.|עָלָ֑יו\rb* \rb So the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb obeyed|וַיִּשְׁמְע֨וּ\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֤יו\rb* \rb and did|וַֽיַּעֲשׂ֔וּ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb* \v 10 \rb Since that time,|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb prophet|נָבִ֥יא\rb* \rb has risen|קָ֨ם\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb like Moses,|כְּמֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb knew|יְדָע֣וֹ\rb* \rb face|פָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb face—|פָּנִֽים׃\rb* \v 11 \rb no prophet who did all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the signs|הָ֨אֹת֜וֹת\rb* \rb and wonders|וְהַמּוֹפְתִ֗ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb sent Moses|שְׁלָחוֹ֙\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb to Pharaoh|לְפַרְעֹ֥ה\rb* \rb and to all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb his officials|עֲבָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb and all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb his land,|אַרְצֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 12 \rb and no prophet who performed|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb all|וּלְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the mighty|הַחֲזָקָ֔ה\rb* \rb acts of power|הַיָּ֣ד\rb* \rb and|וּלְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb awesome deeds|הַמּוֹרָ֣א\rb*\f + \fr 34:12 \ft Or \fqa terrifying deeds\f* \rb |הַגָּד֑וֹל\rb*\rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb Moses did|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
